window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5201,"title":"Chapter 5201: Lesson","paragraphs":["He draped an arm over the man’s shoulder, leaning in close with a low chuckle. \"How did this even get tied to beauty? If you’re going to play the hero rescuing a damsel, shouldn’t you at least pick a pretty one? Otherwise, what if she offers herself in return? That’d be a raw deal, wouldn’t it?\"","\"This Young Master has rather high standards,\" the man chuckled wickedly, his gaze sweeping over the girl ahead before shaking his head. \"Offering oneself? That depends on both face and figure.\" He glanced at the girl, then added, \"This one has a certain lively aura about her, but her face is truly nothing to write home about. As for her figure... well, she’s like a little bean sprout, not fully developed at all. This Young Master simply can’t bring himself to take a bite.\"","Several men chatted and laughed nearby, making light of Yue’er. Little did they know, Yue’er—who appeared to be eating pastries and listening to the storyteller—had heard every word.","Just then, the audience below cheered and clapped. She smiled, eyes crinkling, and joined in the applause, never once glancing in their direction. She simply let them observe her.","Only when she heard the table over there calling for the waiter to add tea did she turn her head. \"Waiter!\" she called out, \"Refill the water!\" Her gaze naturally swept around the room, landing precisely on the table of men in brocade robes. They all wore inexplicable smiles as they looked at her. Seeing this, she lifted her own smile, beaming cheerfully at them.","\"Coming right up!\" The waiter approached, topped up her water, then walked over to the nearby table, setting a fresh pot of tea on their table before retreating.","After taking a sip of tea, Yue’er turned back to listen to the storyteller and, also, to the voices drifting over from the other table.","The group continued their conversation over tea.","\"Look at her,\" one lavishly dressed man boasted, his chin lifted in smug satisfaction. \"The moment she saw us, that girl flashed a smitten expression. Probably never seen a man as strikingly handsome and distinguished as yours truly.\"","\"Since that’s the case, why don’t you go invite the girl over to join us?\" suggested the man in brocade robes, his face tinged with mischief as he gestured in her direction.","Yet, the wicked grin on his face shifted subtly the next moment. His smile stiffened slightly, his brows furrowing ever so slightly. The figure that had been leaning back lazily in his seat suddenly sat up straight, as if struggling to suppress something.","\"What’s so hard about that? Watch me.\" The brocade-clad man stood up with a smile, but the moment he rose, a sound followed.","\"Pfft!\"","A loud fart echoed through the room. At that precise moment, the middle-aged storyteller upstairs was delivering the climax of his tale. The patrons below were holding their breath, listening intently, not making a single sound. Thus, this sudden, resounding fart was heard by nearly everyone in the teahouse.","For a moment, everyone froze, then looked up in surprise toward the source of the sound upstairs.","At the tea table where those men sat, each of them now wore an expression of struggle. A surge of gas seemed to be racing through their bellies, desperate to find an escape. They held it in with all their might, but the more they held it, the more urgent it became.","Especially the man who had let out the loud fart. He seemed utterly shocked that he’d done such a thing in front of everyone. His face flushed crimson, yet he couldn’t control the gas surging within him.","\"Pfft! Pfft pfft pfft!\""]},{"number":5202,"title":"Chapter 5202: It’s Her","paragraphs":["\"Ugh, that stinks!\"","Yue’er wrinkled her nose in disgust, waving her hand in front of her face to fan away the odor. Yet her eyes sparkled with amusement as she watched the men, their faces flushed crimson.","Hearing the sound, the crowd below stared in shock, murmuring among themselves: \"Those men in brocade robes must be Young Masters from noble families. How could they fart in public? Utterly rude.\"","Among them, the lecherous-looking man in brocade heard the murmurs below. A flash of shame and anger crossed his eyes, and in the next moment, he hastily cast a sound-blocking barrier.","After Yue’er summoned the waiter to settle the bill, she left with a look of disgust, covering her nose and mouth. Her expression made those brocade-clad Young Masters wish they could sink into the ground.","Meanwhile, inside the teahouse, the men felt a relentless surge of gas churning in their bellies. Though the sound barrier prevented others from hearing, the incessant flatulence left the Young Masters both mortified and furious. Staring helplessly at each other, they could find no solution.","\"How... how did this happen? Did we eat something bad?\" One man muttered, his face contorting as he inhaled the foul stench permeating the air.","Nothing could be more humiliating than this.","\"Someone must have tampered with our food. How else could this happen?\" The man with the wicked expression turned ashen, his gaze darkening as he recalled the girl who had just left.","\"It was that bean-sprout-like woman!\" He gritted his teeth as he spat out the words.","\"Her? How could that be? She’s been sitting there the whole time, hasn’t moved a muscle.\" Another man said, sounding skeptical.","\"Besides, we’ve got no beef with her... Wait... Could it be... she overheard us talking about her earlier? That’s impossible, right?\" The other man in brocade robes spoke, but before he could finish, another loud fart echoed through the room, making his face flush crimson.","\"Chase her! Don’t let her escape!\" they exclaimed, leaping to their feet. But as they stood, their expressions changed again.","\"Go!\" They couldn’t just stand there. They had to catch that woman first!","So, those below witnessed the Young Masters darting out like shadows, accompanied by several more resounding farts echoing through the air...","Meanwhile, Yue’er was already humming a tune as she made her way toward the Xiao residence.","\"Is this the place?\" She looked up at the Xiao family’s gate and approached to knock.","\"Who goes there?\" The gatekeeper opened the door and, seeing a young girl, immediately broke into a smile. \"May I ask if you are Miss Yun?\"","\"Yes.\" Yue’er nodded in response.","\"Miss Yun, please come in.\" The gatekeeper hurriedly opened the door for her. Just then, a middle-aged man stepped out briskly. Looking at Yun Qi, he smiled and said, \"Miss Yun, I am the steward of the household. The young master instructed that upon your arrival, you should first rest in the courtyard.\"","\"Alright.\" Yue’er responded, following the steward while taking in the surroundings.","After reaching the resting courtyard, Yue’er lay down on the bed and began to rest. Thus, she was unaware that as evening fell, a man dressed in brocade, panting heavily, sneaked in from outside and made his way toward her courtyard...","\"Little Qi?\" Xiao Junyan approached her courtyard quietly and knocked lightly on the door.","\"Coming!\" Yun Qi called out, stretching her back as she opened the door. Spotting Xiao Junyan outside, a smile touched her lips. \"Big Brother Xiao, finished your business?\""]},{"number":5203,"title":"Chapter 5203: Change","paragraphs":["\"I haven’t had a chance to properly show you around today, but I heard there’s a lantern festival in town tonight. I thought I’d take you for a stroll.\" He flashed a smile at her. \"Interested?\"","\"We’ve nothing better to do, so why not?\" Yue’er replied cheerfully, closing the door behind her before joining him.","As the two stepped out of the estate, several young boys and girls peered out from the courtyard. One girl, her eyes sparkling, remarked, \"Father told me that’s the young master of the head family—the most outstanding among the younger generation there.\"","A boy asked, \"Who’s the girl with the young master? Is she from the main family too?\"","\"No, I heard from the gatekeeper she’s surnamed Yun, a friend of the young master.\" Another boy said, glancing at them. \"There’s a lantern festival in town tonight. Shall we go check it out?\"","\"Sure! I’ll go get Big Brother.\" The girl said, about to turn away, but was pulled back by someone beside her.","\"Xiao Xiao, you don’t need to go. Seems like my cousin ate something bad outside and got an upset stomach. He’s been farting nonstop since he got back. Now he’s locked himself in the courtyard and won’t let anyone near him.\" The boy said, a suppressed smile flickering in his eyes.","\"Huh? Really? Did they call a doctor?\" The girl froze, clearly surprised.","\"Yes, the family doctor came. Don’t worry. Weren’t we going to the lantern festival? Let’s go!\" With that, the group headed out of the estate together.","As night fell, the city lights came alive. The colorful lanterns lining the streets formed a unique spectacle. Old and young alike, couples and children, had all arrived early to enjoy the festival. The bustling crowds and the vendors’ shouts along the road seemed more spirited than usual.","Xiao Junyan walked half a step behind Yun Qi, shielding her from the surrounding crowd to prevent her from being jostled. Children ran and laughed down the street, nearly colliding with them. Seeing this, Xiao Junyan reached out and pulled her close.","\"Careful.\"","He drew her closer as they watched the laughing child run past. Looking down at Yun Qi as she stepped back from his embrace, his gaze softened. \"The lantern festival is crowded. Be careful not to get knocked over.\"","Yue’er glanced up and met his gentle eyes. A flutter stirred in her heart, and she smiled, nodding. \"Alright, I know.\"","Ever since the crowd thickened, he’d stayed half a step behind her, shielding her from the jostling crowd. This considerate gesture made her heart flutter strangely.","\"Come, let’s see what’s ahead.\" As he spoke, he reached out and took her hand, leading her forward.","His large hand clasped hers, and Xiao Junyan’s lips curved into a slight smile, his mood seemingly quite good. Yet, he felt a tinge of nervousness and worry, fearing she might pull away. This tension caused a thin sheen of sweat to form on his forehead.","Yue’er looked down at the hand he held, momentarily startled. She hesitated to pull away, noticing his ears had flushed red and his expression was slightly tense, not even daring to glance back at her.","Startled, she found herself smiling inexplicably and let him hold her hand.","She was no longer the naive little girl she once was. With age came a natural understanding of matters of the heart.","Xiao Junyan had always treated her differently since childhood. Perhaps he truly hadn’t harbored such feelings back then, but as she grew older, certain things inevitably changed."]},{"number":5204,"title":"Chapter 5204: I Have Something to Say","paragraphs":["Though she’d sensed something during their time together, she hesitated to act on it. Since childhood, she’d always treated him like an older brother, but now that she vaguely understood his feelings, she didn’t know how to handle it.","\"Little Qi, what kind of lantern do you like?\" Xiao Junyan asked. Seeing she hadn’t pulled away, he silently breathed a sigh of relief.","\"Hmm...\" She glanced at the lanterns lining the street, spotting a fox-shaped one. With a smile, she pointed to it: \"That little fox one.\"","Following her gesture, Xiao Junyan’s gaze settled on the fox-shaped lantern. \"Wait here,\" he said, releasing her hand and walking toward it.","Tonight’s lanterns couldn’t be bought with money—only by solving riddles. Xiao Junyan glanced at the clue, then told the lantern vendor the answer. He took the lantern from the vendor’s hands.","Meanwhile, Yue’er bought a fox mask from a street vendor at the lantern festival. After paying and putting it on, she saw Xiao Junyan returning.","\"For you.\" Xiao Junyan handed her the fox-shaped lantern.","\"Thank you.\" Yue’er happily accepted it, tilting her fox-masked face upward and asking, \"Does it look good?\"","\"It looks good.\" Xiao Junyan smiled and nodded, then asked, \"Are you hungry? I’ll take you to get something to eat.\" He took her hand and led her forward.","Xiao Junyan brought her to a three-story viewing pavilion. \"From here, you can see the lantern festival lights across the city,\" he said. \"And the food here is quite unique. Try some later.\" With that, he called for someone to take their order.","Yue’er set her lantern aside and leaned against the railing. Below, the cityscape spread out before her eyes. The lanterns below cast a beautiful glow, and crowds of people had gathered on the streets to admire the lights.","Junyan watched the young girl, her face full of wonder as she gazed at the street lanterns. His eyes softened.","\"Big Brother Xiao, look! There are fireworks over there!\" Yue’er turned to find his gentle gaze fixed on her, making her feel a bit flustered. She blushed and asked, \"Big Brother Xiao, why are you looking at me like that?\"","Xiao Junyan smiled. \"Little Qi has grown up.\" He reached out, took her hand, and pulled her down to sit beside him. His eyes held a deep intensity as he said, \"Little Qi, there’s something I want to tell you.\"","Hearing this, Yun Qi sat up straight and met his gaze. \"Alright, speak. I’m listening.\"","\"I...\"","Perhaps it was her pure, trusting eyes that made the words catch in his throat. For a moment, he found himself unable to speak.","\"Hehe.\" Yue’er giggled softly, watching him with a mischievous smile. \" Big Brother Xiao, I feel like you’ve changed a lot since your travels.\"","The words he’d mustered the courage to say were swallowed back upon hearing her. He looked at her deeply and asked, \"Have I changed? Is it for the better? Or for the worse?\"","\"You’ve changed. You’re not as cold and distant anymore. That’s definitely for the better. \" She gazed at him, her eyes crinkling with amusement. \"When I first met you, you were completely icy, wearing that expressionless face to everyone. But after you traveled, you gradually started to change. It was like...\"","She casually withdrew the hand he was holding, cupping her chin thoughtfully. \"It was like the ice inside you had melted.\""]},{"number":5205,"title":"Chapter 5205: Secret Realm","paragraphs":["She gazed at him with a radiant smile and said, \"You’ve shed that distant, unapproachable aura and gained a warmer, more human touch. Plus, you never used to smile much before, but now your face lights up far more often.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan’s lips curved slightly. \"That’s because traveling the world has broadened my horizons. No longer confined to one place, I’ve seen so much more of life—my perspective and outlook have naturally changed.\"","\"So traveling really does make a difference. But Big Brother Xiao, don’t you need to return to the family to take charge? Can you really keep wandering like this?\" she asked curiously.","\"The family has the Old Predecessor to guard it, the Patriarch to handle affairs, and Junheng assisting. Though they’ve urged me to return, I still wish to see more of the world.\" As he spoke, he lifted his teacup and took a sip.","He rarely interfered in family affairs. Had his second uncle not sent word requesting his presence to handle a matter, he wouldn’t have come here at all.","\"By the way, there’s an opportunity for training this time. I wonder if you’re interested.\" He spoke up.","\"What kind of trial?\" she asked, turning to look at him.","\"After arriving, I learned the dispute stems from the discovery of a hidden realm. All factions in Mountain Vista City want control over it. But today, after discussing with other family heads, we decided to open the realm and let everyone explore it. Whatever they gain inside will be their own fortune.\"","His gaze shifted to her as he continued, \"The details still need final confirmation, but that’s the general plan. So, I wanted to ask—are you interested? Would you consider going in? Perhaps you’ll find unexpected rewards.\"","Hearing this, she blinked and asked, \"So if I find something in the secret realm, does it belong to me? Or do I have to hand it over?\"","Xiao Junyan smiled and replied slowly, \"Since it’s each person’s fortune, naturally it belongs to them. There’s no need to hand it over. However, this endeavor will also involve danger and deadly threats. After all...\" Treasure hunting and looting—such things were all too common.","Yue’er’s eyes lit up. \"Wonderful! I adore these secret realms. Big Brother Xiao, when can we go? And since I’m not part of your family, can I still enter?\"","\"It should be within the next few days. As for entering, that shouldn’t be an issue.\" He added, \"I’ll accompany you inside.\"","\"Great!\" she replied happily.","Soon, a knock sounded at the door. Several beautiful women entered carrying dishes, set them down, and then quietly withdrew.","With this interruption, Xiao Junyan didn’t continue his earlier unfinished words. Instead, he occasionally served her food.","When they were about seventy percent full, they set down their chopsticks. Yue’er glanced toward the lantern festival area below, her eyes lighting up. Her voice carried a hint of excitement as she exclaimed, \"Hey! Looks like there’s a fight over there!\"","Seeing her eager to join the commotion, Xiao Junyan shook his head helplessly. While others would avoid a fight like the plague, she was drawn to it.","\"Big Brother Xiao, let’s go check it out! It’ll help us digest,\" Yue’er said, turning to him as she stowed the lantern away.","With a sigh, Xiao Junyan nodded. After settling the bill, he followed her toward the gathering crowd drawn to the commotion."]},{"number":5206,"title":"Chapter 5206: Old Acquaintances from years past","paragraphs":["Inside an inn, several men were drinking and chatting.","\"Come to think of it, it’s been years since we last met, hasn’t it?\" One man looked at the other three.","\"It has been several years. Never imagined that when the clan sent me out on this mission, I’d run into all of you.\" Shen Shiqi shook his head, smiling as he turned to them. \"How have you all been these past years? Still within the clan?\"","\"Ah! It’s nothing but a bitter tale.\"","Another man said, \"After I was called back, guess what happened? The elders actually threw me into the training camp. Ugh, I spent a whole year in there—a year! They practically skinned me alive.\"","\"After I returned, they assigned me to manage the family business. Staring at stacks of ledgers all day? Utterly tedious.\" The other man glanced at Shen Shiqi. \"And you? Haven’t heard much about you these years!\"","Shen Shiqi glanced at them. \"You’ve all been busy with your own lives. Who’s been keeping tabs on me? Besides, when you came here, you didn’t expect to run into me either, did you?\"","\"Heh heh...\"","The three exchanged glances and laughed awkwardly. One of them explained, \"Back in the day, following you around on your travels, I got into plenty of trouble. So when I returned, the elders ordered me to cut ties with my rowdy friends. They threatened to lock me up if I didn’t. I had no choice—my family keeps a tight leash on me.\"","\"Same story.\"","Another chimed in, \"My family gave me the same order. They don’t know your true identities—they just think I’m hanging out with some random wandering cultivators. But I figured, if we can’t keep in touch, we can’t keep in touch. We’d probably all end up in similar situations if we got dragged back anyway. Besides, we’d meet again someday. See? Today we bumped into each other by pure accident!\" He laughed to himself.","\"But let me make one thing clear! Friendship is friendship, but when it comes to the treasures inside this secret realm, none of us will give an inch.\" The other man said, glancing at the three of them.","\"Heh heh, that’s exactly what I had in mind.\" Another one chimed in.","Shen Shiqi glanced at the trio, a lazy smile playing on his lips. \"Naturally. It’s been years since we last met, brothers. This is the perfect chance to test our skills. What do you say?\"","\"Test our skills? Who’s afraid of who?\"","\"Exactly. Back in the day, our abilities were neck and neck. Now? Heh, Old Shen, I reckon I’ve got the edge on you.\"","\"Talk is cheap. We’ll see who’s got the real skills.\" Shen Shiqi said, his gaze drifting casually before his eyebrow arched. \"Look, it’s that Xiao family heir, Xiao Junyan.\"","\"Huh? It really is him! And he’s got a young lady with him! Did he bring her out to see the lanterns?\"","The four men fixed their gaze on Xiao Junyan and Yun Qi. They’d seen Xiao Junyan today, but the girl was unfamiliar.","\"If we have rivals, Xiao Junyan is definitely one to watch. He’s the most promising young talent in the Xiao family, especially with his growing reputation these past few years. He’s riding high right now.\"","Shen Shiqi spoke, shifting his gaze from Xiao Junyan to the young girl. Spotting the fox mask on her face, he stroked his chin thoughtfully. \"A little fox, huh! Come to think of it, that little fox from back then—we never actually met her again, did we?\""]},{"number":5207,"title":"Chapter 5207: Gather","paragraphs":["Hearing this, the other three exchanged knowing smiles. \"How many years has it been? You still remember that little girl? But then again, think about it—in all our years traveling the world, have we ever been bested by anyone? Especially not some little girl.\"","Back in the day, when they were traveling together, they’d encountered that little girl named Yun Qi. Several grown men had suffered at her hands, and to make matters worse, they couldn’t find her afterward. No wonder Shen Shiqi had never forgotten that mischievous little girl. Even now, the memory of that incident remained vivid in their minds.","\"Come to think of it, I’ve heard of someone named Yun Qi these past years. I just don’t know if it’s the same person.\" Shen Shiqi mused, fiddling with the cup in his hand.","\"You mean Azure Emperor’s youngest disciple, Yun Qi? Doubt it’s the same person—probably just a coincidence of names,\" another man interjected.","\"I’ve heard of Azure Emperor’s disciple too. He dotes on her terribly, even securing the Divine Whip as her personal weapon.\" Another man chimed in, \"But her origins are said to be quite mysterious. None of the Azure Emperor’s three disciples are known to come from any particular noble house.\"","\"Hey, look! It seems like a fight broke out over there.\" One nudged his friend beside him. \"We’re just hanging around anyway. Why not go check it out?\"","With that, the group settled their bill and left the tavern, heading toward the crowd of onlookers gathering on the street.","When Xiao Junyan followed Yun Qi to the scene, he saw that the group fighting included young men from a collateral branch of the Xiao family. Aside from one girl shouting anxiously nearby, the other two or three youths were already injured—blood trickling from their mouths, eyes swollen from blows.","The four youths on the opposing side clearly held the upper hand, looking far less battered than the two Xiao family members.","Watching this scene, he neither intervened nor called for a halt, merely staying by Yun Qi’s side to observe.","If they were outmatched yet still fought, as long as no one died, let them battle it out!","Yun Qi watched their chaotic brawl with gleaming eyes. Seeing others fight made her own hands itch to join in.","After entering the Xiao family, she’d gone to the guest quarters to rest and hadn’t met the other members. Thus, she didn’t recognize that two of the brawlers were Xiao family scions.","\"Those three are slightly weaker than the other four. Plus, they have one more person, giving them the numerical advantage. If this fight continues, they’ll just end up taking a beating,\" Yue’er said, her chin resting on her hand as her gaze fixed on the brawl.","\"These are all young masters from prominent families. They know their limits. At most, they’ll just get some superficial injuries.\" Xiao Junyan spoke slowly, his gaze also fixed on the figures in front.","\"Big Brother Xiao, do you know them?\" Yue’er, sensing from his tone that he might recognize those people, couldn’t help but look at him.","Just as Xiao Junyan was about to speak, a voice called out.","\"Big Brother Xiao!\" Xiao Xiaolin’s eyes lit up upon seeing him, and she hurriedly ran towards him.","Xiao Junyan gave her a faint glance but said nothing.","Yue’er blinked, watching the delicate-looking girl with interest.","So he does know her!","\"Big Brother Xiao, what should we do? They’re fighting! I can’t stop them!\" she said anxiously, her worried gaze fixed on the group tangled in a brawl."]},{"number":5208,"title":"Chapter 5208: Strike","paragraphs":["\"They’ll stop when they’re tired,\" Xiao Junyan remarked indifferently, watching with his hands behind his back, showing no intention to intervene.","A crowd had gathered around, watching the fight unfold. Those eager for more drama even cheered them on from the sidelines. Though the seven in the center were brawling, they knew their limits—no weapons were drawn. They simply clenched their fists and beat each other mercilessly.","The sound of fists landing on flesh made Yun Qi wince in pain for the three youths. As she watched, a flash of vicious intent crossed the eyes of one of the silk-clad youths. A cold gleam seemed to flicker in his clenched fist as he swung hard at the head of a youth pinned to the ground. She couldn’t help but suck in a sharp breath.","The youth’s intent was truly vicious—a needle concealed within his fist. Was he intending to kill the boy on the ground?","Just as she moved to intervene, Xiao Junyan’s palm struck out with a swish, slapping toward the youth. Simultaneously, a blade of energy shot forth, striking the youth’s clenched fist with pinpoint accuracy.","With a thud, the youth clutching the needles in his fist cried out in pain and was sent flying several meters away.","\"Pfft!\"","A mouthful of blood spurted out, causing the brawling group to pause in shock.","\"Third Young Master!\" The other three immediately rushed over, helping him up.","The three Xiao family youths were also dumbfounded. Only upon recognizing Xiao Junyan did they snap back to their senses. Supporting each other, they stood up straight, bowed their heads in shame, and called out: \"Young... Young Master.\"","Not only had they lost a street fight, but the Young Master had witnessed it. They wanted nothing more than to find a hole to crawl into.","Yue’er silently exhaled in relief, glancing at one of the Xiao family youths. He had truly dodged a bullet. She frowned again, shifting her gaze to the blood-spitting youth. It was truly strange—such a young boy, yet his thoughts were so cunning and vicious. What would become of him when he grew up?","But... someone else seemed to have intervened just now.","She scanned the crowd in that direction and spotted four men standing out prominently. Her eyes narrowed sharply at the sight of them, and she quickly averted her gaze, shrinking back slightly.","Heavens! It was Shen Shiqi’s group! Talk about running into enemies! How could she encounter them here?","Xiao Junyan also glanced in Shen Shiqi’s direction. Noticing their gaze, he gave a slight nod in greeting before striding forward. Fixing his gaze on the blood-spitting youth, he demanded, \"Which family’s young master are you?\"","What had seemed like mere street brawling now revealed the youth harbored murderous intent.","The group instinctively took a step back at the sight of Xiao Junyan’s imposing, intimidating presence. Their lips moved, but they didn’t name their family.","\"Young Master, the one coughing up blood is the third young master of the Shen family’s second branch. The one supporting him on the left is also from the Shen family. The other two are from the Chen family,\" a youth from the Xiao family explained.","These fellows had always been at odds with them. Tonight, they’d bumped into each other at the lantern festival, exchanged provocative words, and a fight had erupted over a minor disagreement. To their shame, they’d ended up losing, forcing the Young Master to intervene.","At that moment, the youth remained unaware that he had just narrowly escaped death. Had Xiao Junyan and his companions not happened to be present, he likely would have perished tonight.","\"Young Master Xiao.\" Shen Shiqi stepped forward, flanked by three close friends.","\"Uncle... Uncle Shiqi...\" The Shen youth paled visibly upon seeing Shen Shiqi, his voice trembling as he called out."]},{"number":5209,"title":"Chapter 5209: Accountability","paragraphs":["Shen Shiqi didn’t look at him but turned to Xiao Junyan instead. \"Tonight’s incident was the Shen family’s fault. I’ll take this boy back and ensure the Xiao family receives a proper explanation.\"","Though several families had competing interests, none were outright enemies. Minor skirmishes were easily overlooked, but the Shen family’s young master had struck from the shadows with murderous intent—a clear violation of honor. If Xiao Junyan were to make this public on the street, the Shen family would find it difficult to maintain their standing in the city henceforth.","After all, striking from the shadows was the act of a petty villain, despised by all.","Xiao Junyan glanced at him and nodded. \"Agreed.\" With that, he turned away without another look at the others. As he did so, he noticed Yun Qi, who had been standing among the crowd, had vanished without a trace.","His eyes flickered briefly as he discreetly scanned the surroundings. Finding no sign of her, he began to walk away.","Several young men and women from the Xiao family hurried after him. Behind them, not only did the younger generation of the Shen family lower their heads upon seeing Shen Shiqi bow his, but even the two young members of the Chen family bowed their heads at that moment. For beside Shen Shiqi stood their own Third Young Master Chen, his face cold and stern.","Late at night, in the Shen family hall, Shen Shiqi sat in the seat of honor sipping tea. The Patriarch of the Shen family’s collateral branch occupied the seat to his right, while the clan elders sat below.","In the center of the hall knelt the youth—the third young master of the Shen family’s second branch.","\"Young Master Shen Shiqi, what is the meaning of this?\" an elder inquired, unsure why he had been summoned or why a junior was kneeling in the center.","\"Let him speak for himself,\" Shen Shiqi replied without lifting his head, lightly scraping the tea lid against the surface of his cup.","\"Speak! What exactly happened?\" the Second Master of the Shen family demanded in a deep voice, his eyes fixed intently on his son kneeling before him.","\"I... I went to the lantern festival with Chen Nan and the others. We... we ran into some people from the Xiao family. Words were exchanged, and a fight broke out. The Xiao family members were no match for us. Later, the Patriarch Xiao intervened and injured me. Uncle Seventeen came out and... and brought me back.\" The youth kept his head bowed, his words coming out haltingly.","Listening to this, Shen Shiqi’s lips curved slightly, his expression unreadable, leaving others guessing at his thoughts.","The assembled crowd also froze upon hearing this. After exchanging glances, the Second Master of the Shen family turned to Shen Shiqi seated at the head and asked, \"Young Master Shiqi, is this how it happened?\"","Others also looked at Shen Shiqi, their minds filled with doubt. If things truly unfolded as he claimed, then this should have been mere youthful mischief. How did it escalate to the point where all the clan elders had to be summoned?","Shen Shiqi set down his teacup and looked at the youth kneeling on the floor. \"I gave you a chance,\" he said.","Hearing this, the youth’s heart trembled, and his head drooped even lower.","The others felt a sinking sensation in their hearts upon hearing Shen Shiqi’s words, sensing vaguely that the matter was not as simple as Shen San had described.","Shen Shiqi rose to his feet, hands clasped behind his back as he paced the hall. \"Our Shen family stands among the foremost century-old clans. The foundation of our clan is not to subdue others through force, but to win their respect through virtue.\"","Shen Shiqi swept a glance over them. \"","\"The Shen family has countless branches. Though not part of the main lineage, you should still understand this principle. Yet I never imagined that upon coming here, I would witness a young Shen heir, not yet of age, harboring such venomous intentions.\"","His voice paused as he slowly approached the youth. \"Speak then. What reason compels you to insist on the death of that Xiao family heir?\""]},{"number":5210,"title":"Chapter 5210: Settling The Matter","paragraphs":["The youth’s face instantly drained of color. He hadn’t expected... that he actually knew...","Upon hearing this, the elders of the Shen family also grew solemn. Shen Family Second Master felt a heavy weight in his heart. He stepped forward, grabbed his son’s shoulders, and hoisted him up. His voice was deep and stern as he demanded, \"You intended to kill a junior of the Xiao family? And at the lantern festival on the street?\"","\"Father, I... I...\" His voice trembled, unable to form words.","Shen Shiqi walked slowly to the main seat and sat down. \"Those who cultivate immortality are not forbidden from killing or fighting. However, even if one must kill, it should be done with honor and integrity. And you? Hiding needles in your fists, plotting a hidden assassination—such methods are shameful. And you were foolish enough to do it. Even if that Xiao family youth hadn’t died on the spot, had he died after returning home, the Xiao family would still have held the Shen family responsible.\"","He looked at the youth in the hall and continued, \"If Xiao Junyan had exposed the matter on the street, how could the Shen family ever establish itself in Mountain Vista City again? If word spreads that the Shen family’s young heir is treacherous and vicious, striking down his victims in the dark, how will the world view my Shen family?\"","At this point, he lifted his teacup and took a sip. \"I said I would give the Xiao family an explanation. You decide among yourselves how to provide it!\" With that, he fell silent.","By now, the faces of the Shen family members had darkened to the point of being pitch black. This was especially true for the Shen family Patriarch. He had finally gotten someone sent over from the main family—the highly regarded Seventeenth Young Master—hoping to make a good impression. Yet, his subordinates had only managed to cause trouble.","\"Strip him of his cultivation. Tomorrow, in front of the entire clan, administer thirty severe lashes. Then send him to a village in the countryside!\" declared the Shen family Patriarch in a deep, measured voice.","Hearing this, the youth’s face drained of all color. He immediately began wailing and pleading, \"Patriarch, Seventeen Young Master, I’ll never dare again! I beg you, please don’t strip me of my cultivation! I beg you, I beg you! I’ll never dare again...\"","Upon hearing the Patriarch’s words, the Second Master of the Shen family also paled. He immediately knelt down and said, \"Patriarch, Seventeenth Young Master, esteemed elders, it is all my fault for failing to guide him properly, leading this wicked son to commit such an act. But he is only seventeen. If his cultivation is stripped, he will never again have any hope of treading the path of cultivation. Patriarch, Seventeenth Young Master, esteemed elders, I beg you to show leniency!\"","One elder, unable to bear the sight, looked at the Patriarch and said, \"Patriarch, stripping his cultivation is not a bit too harsh?\"","The Patriarch glanced at the two kneeling figures, his gaze flickering. He turned to Shen Shiqi and asked, \"Young Master Shiqi, do you think stripping his cultivation is acceptable?\"","Shen Shiqi set down his teacup, not answering the Patriarch. Instead, he looked at the youth below and said, \" Had Xiao Junyan and I not intervened, you would have taken the life of a young member of the Xiao family. Now, we strip you of your cultivation to spare your life. Do you consider this punishment too harsh?\"","The youth’s lips trembled, and he finally slumped to the ground. He knew his cultivation was lost forever today...","The Second Master of the Shen family had intended to plead for mercy, but upon hearing Shen Shiqi’s words, the plea died on his lips. Though his cultivation was stripped, at least his life remained. If he lived quietly and obediently, a hundred years or more was still possible.","The Patriarch watched this unfold before instructing an elder to strip the youth of his cultivation. He was then led away to be imprisoned, with thirty lashes awaiting him tomorrow.","Seeing the matter settled, Shen Shiqi rose and walked away, thinking to himself that he would pay another visit to the Xiao family tomorrow..."]},{"number":5211,"title":"Chapter 5211: Solemn","paragraphs":["In the Xiao family guest courtyard.","Yue’er sat in the courtyard, her chin resting in her hands. She couldn’t fathom how, after all these years, she’d run into Shen Shiqi and his crew again.","But then again, so much time had passed. She’d grown up now. He probably wouldn’t recognize her anyway, right?","\"Little Qi.\" Xiao Junyan entered, walking slowly to the table in the courtyard and sitting down. \"Why did you come back alone?\"","\"I ran into some people I used to tease. I was afraid they might recognize me, so I came back on my own.\" She smiled sheepishly, pouring him a cup of water as she asked, \"Big Brother Xiao, do you know Shen Shiqi and his group?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan looked at her with mild surprise. \"You mean Shen Shiqi and his group? You knew them before?\"","\"Well, not exactly. I just ran into them on the road. I played a prank on them once, and they chased me for a while, but I managed to shake them off. Never thought I’d run into them again after all these years.\"","Xiao Junyan chuckled. \"Well, you’re quite something, daring to tease them. They’re all the pride of their families—not the young masters, but influential figures nonetheless. They’re here for the secret realm matter too.\"","\"The Shen family Patriarch is Shen Shiqi. He’s meticulous and exceptionally skilled at handling matters. The Chen family Patriarch is Chen San—the third son of their current Patriarch, whose given name is Chen Tao. The other two are Zheng Yuan and Yang Hao. They’ll likely enter the secret realm on this trip too.\"","\"Oh.\" Yue’er nodded, her mind already spinning with calculations. If they were entering, how likely was it they’d cross paths?","\"Don’t worry,\" Xiao Junyan said. \"They won’t cause you trouble. After all, it was years ago. They might have forgotten by now.\"","\"Mhm, I understand,\" she replied with a nod, her smile brightening.","\"Then get some rest early.\" He stood up, spoke, and then turned to walk out.","After watching him leave, Yue’er stretched her back and also returned to her room to rest.","The next day, after eating breakfast, she wandered around the Xiao family courtyard. She heard the servants say that the Shen family had arrived, so she followed the onlookers to the front to take a look.","In the front courtyard, two Shen family guards supported a youth who could barely stand, trailing behind Shen Shiqi.","\"His cultivation was stripped, and he just endured thirty lashes. I brought him here for you to see. Soon he’ll be sent to the country estate,\" Shen Shiqi’s voice carried a hint of languor, as if the youth stripped of his cultivation and beaten were not one of his own Shen kin.","The Patriarch Xiao had heard of this incident from Xiao Junyan last night. He had been pondering how the Shen family would handle it. To have his cultivation stripped and be exiled—it was undeniably a severe punishment.","Now, observing the youth being supported, a faint trickle of blood still seeping from his buttocks, his face pale and barely clinging to life, the family head felt a slight tremor within. To lay such hands upon one’s own kin...","Such stern methods of household discipline were truly beyond the reach of ordinary people. No wonder the Shen family earned thumbs-up from everyone they met outside. Such family traditions truly commanded solemn respect.","\"I’ve long heard of the Shen family’s strict discipline,\" Xiao Junyan remarked, his gaze settling on Shen Shiqi. \"Seeing it firsthand today, it truly commands respect.\""]},{"number":5212,"title":"Chapter 5212: Take Away","paragraphs":["Shen Shiqi tugged at the corner of his mouth and said, \"Since you’ve seen the person, I won’t keep you any longer. Goodbye.\" He gave a perfunctory bow before stepping toward the exit. As his footsteps carried him outward, they faltered slightly. His gaze lingered briefly on the face of the girl peering out from nearby.","This girl—the one who had followed Xiao Junyan last night. Last night she’d worn a fox mask; today, without it, her face and those eyes held a faint, familiar quality.","Yet he rarely forgot faces. He didn’t recall ever meeting this girl. So where did this sense of familiarity come from?","As he pondered, the young girl blinked her beautiful eyes and flashed an innocent, pure smile. It was precisely that smile that suddenly brought it all back to him.","It was her!","That cunning little fox of a girl from years ago!","Yue’er caught Shen Shiqi’s gaze directed at her. Though she’d intended to look away, she blinked and offered a pure, innocent smile. Little did she know, it was precisely that smile that made Shen Shiqi, who had been about to walk away, wave his hand. \"Take him back first,\" he instructed. Then he strode toward Yue’er, who stood not far away.","Xiao Junyan watched this, his eyes flickering slightly, and followed suit, striding toward Yun Qi.","Huh? Why is he coming toward her? She’d already flashed such a friendly, innocent smile—what else could Shen Shiqi possibly want?","She wondered inwardly as Shen Shiqi stopped before her.","\"Yun Qi?\"","Shen Shiqi uttered the name. Though he’d once believed it was merely a pseudonym, it was, after all, spoken from her own lips. Even if false, she should remember it.","\"Huh?\" Yue’er froze, momentarily stunned.","Shen Shiqi, seeing this, let out a light chuckle: \"It really is you?\" With that smile, his already handsome features seemed even more striking.","\"Little girl, we’ve been searching high and low for you! Never imagined after all these years, we’d find you right here.\" He seemed in a rather good mood, staring at the young girl before him and asking, \"How did you end up in the Xiao family? Are you part of this family?\"","Yue’er understood he had recognized her. She touched her own cheek, puzzled. \"How did you recognize me? I’ve grown up now. I look different from when I was little.\"","Shen Shiqi laughed heartily, flicking her forehead playfully. \"A crafty little girl like you is hard to miss. How could I not recognize you?\"","\"Little Qi, what brings you here?\" Xiao Junyan approached, deliberately positioning himself between Shen Shiqi.","Shen Shiqi raised an eyebrow, his gaze sweeping over the pair before settling on Yun Qi. \"Little girl, since we’ve run into each other, how about we step outside? I’ve arranged to meet Chen San and the others—you know, the ones you met back then.\"","Yue’er blinked at the scene, thought for a moment, then agreed, \"Sounds good!\"","After all, she was just an idle presence in the Xiao household. Since he recognized her and wasn’t dwelling on the past, why not make a few more friends?","\"Big Brother...\" Yun Qi turned to Xiao Junyan, about to speak, but was cut off by Shen Shiqi.","\"Young Master Xiao, we have much catching up to do. I’ll take Yun Qi with me now. I’ll return her tonight, so you needn’t worry.\" Shen Shiqi smiled, his gaze fixed on Yun Qi."]},{"number":5213,"title":"Chapter 5213: Meeting","paragraphs":["\"Young lady, Young Master Xiao is a very busy man. He surely has many matters to attend to. Let’s enjoy our gathering, and I’ll escort you back later. How does that sound?\"","Yue’er had intended to invite Xiao Junyan along, but Shen Shiqi’s words caught her off guard. She glanced at Xiao Junyan, whose expression had grown noticeably colder, then looked back at Shen Shiqi. After a moment’s thought, she replied, \"Big Brother Xiao, I’ll go explore with Shen Shiqi. Don’t worry about me—I’ll be back tonight.\"","She knew he’d come here to handle matters concerning the secret realm. Now, he likely had even more discussions and arrangements to make. By going out with Shen Shiqi, she hoped to sit down and chat with them—to see if they might also be heading to the secret realm. Secondly, making a few more friends wouldn’t hurt.","\"Alright, go on then! We were just talking about you yesterday. When Chen San and the others see you, they’ll be surprised.\" Shen Shiqi chuckled, striding toward the exit.","Yue’er flashed Xiao Junyan a smile. \"Off to have some fun!\" With that, she followed Shen Shiqi out.","Not far away, Patriarch Xiao and the others watched, slightly startled. They knew the girl had come with the young master and seemed to be surnamed Yun, but why did she appear to know Shen Shiqi as well?","Outside the Xiao residence, Shen Shiqi looked at her with interest and asked, \"What’s your relationship with Xiao Junyan? How did you end up coming to the Xiao family with him? He didn’t look too pleased when he saw you leaving with me.\"","Yue’er smiled brightly. \"Big Brother Xiao Junyan is my friend! We’ve known each other for many years. This time, I came down the mountain to travel, and Big Brother Xiao brought me here.\"","\"Down the mountain? You’ve been living up there all these years? No wonder we searched for so long without finding any trace of you.\" Shen Shiqi glanced at her. \"You really know how to hide.\"","\"Hehe.\" Her eyes crinkled with laughter.","\"I’d been wondering if ’Yun Qi’ was just an alias. Looks like it really is your name.\" He paused, then looked at her intently. \"You wouldn’t happen to be that Azure Emperor’s disciple, Yun Qi, would you?\"","\"Yes!\" she affirmed. \"My master is the Azure Emperor. All these years, I’ve been cultivating in Yunxiao Mountain.\"","\"No wonder.\" He sighed softly. \"I had my suspicions back then, but it seemed unlikely. Never imagined it would be the same person.\"","Yue’er beamed. \"I always thought you were all independent cultivators! Never expected you to have such distinguished backgrounds! I’ve heard your families are all top-tier, centuries-old clans.\"","\"We’ve been wandering cultivators for many years, accustomed to freedom. Only later were we summoned back by our families—it couldn’t be helped.\" He glanced at Yun Qi and chuckled softly, \"But this time, it’s quite fortuitous. Coming to Mountain Vista City, we’ve met several long-lost companions and encountered you, little fox. It’s certainly been a worthwhile journey.\"","As they chatted, they made their way to an inn on the street. Ascending to the second floor, they entered a private room. The three men already conversing inside froze when they saw the young girl Shen Shiqi brought in.","\"No way! Old Shen, where’d you snag this little girl?\" Chen San’s eyes widened in utter bewilderment.","\"We’re a bunch of grown men drinking and chatting. Is it really appropriate for you to bring in a delicate young lady like this?\" Zheng Yuan also gave Shen Shiqi a peculiar look, then glanced at the girl.","Yang Hao, after sizing Yun Qi up with his eyes, turned to Shen Shiqi: \"This girl seems a bit too young, don’t you think? I never heard you had a thing for this sort!\""]},{"number":5214,"title":"Chapter 5214: Unsuitable","paragraphs":["Yue'er listened to this, her eyes crinkling into a smile as she stood beside Shen Shiqi, looking utterly harmless.","Shen Shiqi shook his head helplessly, smiling at them. \"Looks like you really haven't recognized her!\"","\"Recognized who?\" Chen Tao asked.","\"This girl may look ordinary, even plain, but with my eye for talent, I'd never forget someone I'd seen before. So I'm certain I've never met this girl.\"","Zheng Yuan spoke, his eyes scanning Yun Qi up and down. He paused, then added, \"Though... she does bear some resemblance to that girl who was with Xiao Junyan last night.\"","\"Little miss, what's your name? Why are you out with Old Shen? Aren't you afraid he'll kidnap you and sell you?\" Yang Hao teased, looking at Yun Qi.","Yun Qi gave them a beaming smile. \"It's been ages since I met someone daring enough to try selling me.\" She walked over, sat down at the table, and said, \"When it comes to discernment, you really can't hold a candle to Shen Shiqi.\"","The three exchanged glances. \"So we've met before? Then tell us, what's your name?\"","\"I'm Yun Qi!\" she said cheerfully. Their eyes widened as they stared at her.","\"Yun... Yun Qi? Could it be the one I'm thinking of?\"","\"You're that chubby little girl from back then!\"","\"No way! You're that mischievous little brat from back then?\"","Hearing their words, Yun Qi's mouth twitched slightly. She puffed out her cheeks in displeasure and gave a light snort before declaring in a clear voice, \"I'm not full of mischief! All these years I've been studying hard and practicing my writing. Even my master praised me for being full of knowledge.\"","The trio, however, looked utterly bewildered. They stared at her for a moment, then turned to Shen Shiqi, who had sat down with a smile, and asked, \"Old Shen, where did you find this little girl?\"","\"Met her at the Xiao residence. She's traveling with Xiao Junyan.\" Shen Shiqi added, \"This little girl really is Yun Qi, the youngest disciple of the Azure Emperor. She's been living on Yunxiao Mountain all these years—no wonder we searched for so long without finding her.\"","\"The Azure Emperor's disciple?\" The trio looked astonished, turning to Yun Qi. \"We heard the Azure Emperor has three disciples, and his favorite is the youngest female one. Never imagined it was you!\"","Hearing them mention her master, she sat up straight, lifted her chin, and declared proudly, \"That's right! I'm my master's favorite.\"","As they ate and chatted in the side room, Yue'er inquired about the secret realm.","When she mentioned the secret realm, the group exchanged glances before turning to her with puzzled expressions. \"Junyan told you about this?\"","\"So you're planning to enter the secret realm too?\" Yue'er asked them.","\"Naturally. We'll each bring carefully selected members from our clans. But you... I advise you not to go,\" Chen Tao said, looking at her.","\"Why? Are only your clans allowed in? Can no one else enter?\" Yue'er asked.","Hearing this, the others couldn't help but smile. \"This secret realm was discovered by our families. Outsiders truly won't be allowed in. Beyond that, there's another point: it's an untouched secret realm. Once inside, things like looting and killing will happen. Even if we wanted to stop it, we couldn't. For a girl like you to go to such a dangerous place... it's not really suitable.\""]},{"number":5215,"title":"Chapter 5215: Enter","paragraphs":["Yue’er’s eyes crinkled with laughter as she chirped, \"I just love dangerous places! Besides, I came down the mountain to travel and hone my skills. And since no one’s ever been inside, I bet there’s plenty of good stuff in there. Or are you worried I’ll go in and grab everything?\"","The others froze, exchanging glances before bursting into laughter. Shen Shiqi chuckled, \"You little fox! Haven’t seen you in years, and you’re still as cocky as ever!\"","\"What could a mere girl like you possibly snatch up in there? Let me tell you, the ones going in this time are all the top-tier talents from their families. You? You can’t hold a candle to them.\" Chen Tao chuckled dismissively.","\"That’s not something you need to worry about. \" Yue’er said with a smile.","\"Alright, enough about that. Let’s eat first. Later, we’ll take you around town.\" Shen Shiqi said, picking up his chopsticks and serving himself a dish.","That day, Yue’er followed them around the city until dusk fell. Only then did the four of them escort her back to the Xiao family’s main gate.","\"Go inside! Rest up these next couple of days. When the chance comes, come visit our master’s place. It’s far more interesting than here,\" Shen Shiqi said, his gaze lingering on Yun Qi.","\"Thank you all for today. I’ll head inside now! As for what happens next... we’ll see.\" She flashed a sweet smile, waved to them, then knocked on the door and stepped inside.","\"Come on! Let’s find a place to continue drinking.\" Shen Shiqi chuckled, leading the others away.","Inside the Xiao residence, Yue’er entered the courtyard and immediately spotted Xiao Junyan. She looked at the man standing there with mild surprise and asked, \"Big Brother Xiao, what are you doing here?\"","\"You’re back?\" Xiao Junyan approached her, glancing at her before asking, \"Did you have fun today?\"","\"Mm hmm! Shen Shiqi and the others took me to lots of places to play and I ate so many snacks. I really had a great time today.\" She beamed, finding Shen Shiqi and the others quite entertaining after spending time with them.","\"It’s my fault. Since returning here, I haven’t taken you out to enjoy yourself properly,\" Xiao Junyan said apologetically.","\"Not at all! Big Brother Xiao accompanied me to the lantern festival last night. Besides, you have matters to attend to here. How could you possibly keep accompanying me everywhere?\" she replied cheerfully.","\"I’ll walk you back to your quarters,\" Xiao Junyan said, accompanying her toward the guest courtyard.","Outside her guest quarters, he paused. \"I won’t come in. Get some rest early—you’ll need your strength for the secret realm in two days.\"","\"Alright,\" Yue’er replied. After watching him leave, she had servants bring hot water to prepare for her bath.","Two days later","Yue’er followed Xiao Junyan and the other Xiao family members selected for this secret realm expedition to the mountain range of Mountain Vista.","Upon arrival, many others were already waiting there.","Eight families had sent representatives on this journey, with only twenty spots allocated per family. Consequently, every participant had been meticulously chosen.","Yue’er’s presence here was entirely due to Xiao Junyan’s influence; otherwise, the Xiao family would never have relinquished a spot for her.","\"Since everyone is present, let us begin!\" Shen Shiqi said, turning to the leaders of the other families.","The eight family leaders stepped forward and jointly activated the gate to the secret realm."]},{"number":5216,"title":"Chapter 5216: Did Not Expect","paragraphs":["Yue’er watched as a fissure appeared in the mountains ahead. The crack seemed like a door within an illusion, its interior shrouded in mystery.","A member of one clan spoke up, \"We’ll take our leave then.\" As soon as the words left his mouth, twenty figures led the way toward the fissure, their forms vanishing into the illusory void.","With one clan entering, the others seemed afraid of being left behind. They too led their families into the fissure.","Shen Shiqi nodded to Yun Qi, glanced at Xiao Junyan, smiled, and followed the others inside.","\"Everyone, follow me,\" Xiao Junyan commanded, leading his group toward the fissure.","After their group entered, the fissure gently closed, returning to its original state. The Patriarchs exchanged glances, exchanged a perfunctory bow, and then each departed.","Entering through this point meant that when they wished to leave the secret realm, they need only shatter their teleportation jade tokens to return directly to their clans. Thus, they had no need to wait here and could return to their clans immediately.","What those who entered the secret realm hadn’t anticipated was that the moment they stepped inside, their original party vanished. They found themselves utterly alone.","After entering, Xiao Junyan instinctively looked for Yun Qi. But she wasn’t there. Not only had she disappeared, but everyone else who had followed behind him was gone too. The surroundings weren’t a forest or anything like that. Instead, it was a vast, white expanse, as if nothing existed at all.","His brow furrowed slightly, his expression darkening. He had been careless. He hadn’t anticipated being separated upon entering. Now, he had no idea where Yun Qi had gone.","Thinking this, he took out his communication jade to ask her where she was. Unexpectedly, the jade transmission seemed to be cut off, showing no sign of response.","He exhaled deeply, suppressing his irritation. Pressing his lips together, he stepped forward.","Meanwhile, Yue’er gazed at the peach blossom grove before her, slightly startled. \"An illusion?\" The scene before her mirrored her memories of Peach Blossom Ridge. Now, she stood amidst the blossoms, surrounded by a sea of pink.","She lightly tapped her foot, drew in a breath, and leapt up, gliding through the blossoms. After circling once, a sly smile appeared on her lips: \"I thought it was something else! Turns out it’s just a soul-confusing array of this level.\"","Standing amidst the blossoms, she drew the Divine-Slaying Whip from her spatial pouch and gripped it firmly. A surge of spirit energy coursed through the whip as she commanded with a sharp cry: \"Break!\"","The whip shot out, cutting through the air with a sharp whistle. It struck the ground with a heavy thud, powerful spirit energy surging from its tip. With a whoosh, visible air currents rippled outward. Petals scattered from the ground and trees, gradually transforming into specks of luminous light before vanishing into the air.","Before her eyes unfolded a verdant forest. A damp, musty scent mingled with the odor of decaying leaves filled the air. Dense, lush trees blocked the sunlight, casting the forest in an eerie, shadowy atmosphere.","Even a cultivator could sense the biting chill permeating the air here, making one’s pores bristle as the cold seeped into the flesh.","A palpable sense of danger hung over the forest like a vast net, causing Yue’er to wipe the smile from her face and narrow her eyes cautiously."]},{"number":5217,"title":"Chapter 5217: Danger","paragraphs":["A chilling breeze swept through the air. She sensed something approaching her, yet it remained hidden, watching her without drawing too near.","Yue’er gripped the Divine Whip in her hand and chuckled, \"This secret realm seems rather entertaining!\"","Suddenly, the whip snapped out, cracking against a nearby tree trunk. A layer of bark peeled away, leaving a fresh gash. The chilling aura that had permeated the area vanished with the crack of the whip.","She glanced around, gave a light snort, then gathered her energy and darted forward. However, after covering only a short distance, a pack of fierce beasts closed in, baring their teeth and snarling at her.","Seeing this, Yue’er tucked away her whip with a smile and drew her dagger instead. Before the fierce beasts could pounce, she lunged at them first.","Perhaps stunned that a human would dare attack them, the fierce beasts hesitated a moment before baring their claws and lunging to bite her.","Yet, after a stick of incense burned, only screams echoed as the fierce beasts scattered in flight. The air thickened with the scent of blood, and several carcasses lay sprawled on the ground. Yue’er was busy extracting beast crystals and cutting off the horns of those with medicinal value.","With her strength and the powerful contract beast by her side, these fierce beasts were no match for her. Thus, she walked on, gathering whatever she deemed useful along the way.","Surprisingly, she walked alone for an entire day without encountering a single person, as if she were the only one in this place.","As dusk fell, the air thickened with an eerie chill. The forest echoed intermittently with the roars of fierce beasts and the howls of wolves, making danger feel ever-present.","When night descended, she set up an array around herself, scattered insect-repelling powder, and lit a campfire. She rested by the fire.","As night deepened, the beastly roars vanished inexplicably, replaced by ghostly wails that echoed through the air. The chill in the atmosphere grew more bone-chilling, forcing her to abandon her plans for rest and remain vigilant.","She knew her body had always drawn such dark entities since childhood. Yet her parents had given her a protective treasure that kept these malevolent forces at bay. All these years, none had dared approach her.","Tonight, however, an inexplicable unease gripped her. Her grip tightened on the whip in her hand as she scanned her surroundings with heightened vigilance.","As midnight passed and drowsiness deepened, she inadvertently dozed off...","The very instant she fell into slumber, a chilling wind swept through. The burning branches, as if doused with cold water, hissed and died out.","A wisp of smoke began to spread, enveloping Yue’er. Faintly, an eerie sound emerged—an echoey, spine-chilling laugh. Yet Yue’er, usually so vigilant, seemed utterly oblivious. Leaning against the great tree behind her, she slept soundly until she was completely engulfed by that wisp of smoke, vanishing as if absorbed into the forest itself.","In truth, she remained seated there, leaning against the tree before the extinguished fire. Though she appeared to be in a deep slumber, her sleep seemed restless. Her brow was tightly furrowed, and beads of sweat had formed on her forehead..."]},{"number":5218,"title":"Chapter 5218: Arrives","paragraphs":["\"Get away! Get away!\"","In her sleep, Yue’er swung the whip in her hand. Yet the malevolent entity, emitting that eerie laughter, kept coiling around her again and again. Her heart raced with panic, but her entire body felt utterly powerless. Even as she wielded the Divine Whip, she sensed it held no true force.","\"Such a pure celestial spirit body is truly rare, especially one as fresh and tender as this. Heh heh heh... After waiting a thousand years, I never imagined I’d encounter such an invaluable spirit body. Truly, heaven favors me...\"","The hollow voice carried a hoarseness that sounded ancient, yet within that rasp lay a hint of sharpness. Coupled with the eerie, chilling laughter, it truly sent shivers down one’s spine.","Yue’er couldn’t see her surroundings. She only knew something kept grabbing at her feet. Even after she kicked it away, it clung back tightly. In an instant, a chill ran down her spine. A bone-chilling sensation flooded her entire body, making every hair on her skin stand on end.","\"This body is perfect—flesh and blood, warm to the touch. Such a wonderful sensation.\" \" The voice was eerie and excited, layers of cold energy rising from Yue’er’s feet, tightly binding her as if trying to strangle her.","Her entire body was immobilized. Worse, she felt her body growing colder, a bone-chilling coldness creeping upward, until it reached her neck and tightened around it.","\"No... let go... let me go...\"","Her body was utterly unresponsive, suffocated by that icy breath. Breathing grew increasingly difficult, her will gradually weakening, as if she were about to plunge into endless darkness at any moment.","And yet, precisely at this moment, the voice of that thousand-year-old specter still echoed in her ears, as if trying to lure out her soul to possess it by force.","\"M-Master...\"","She cried out in agony, her eyes closing as everything seemed to plunge into darkness. In that instant, her entire body felt possessed by the specter...","At that very moment, the Azure Emperor, seated cross-legged atop Yunxiao Mountain, abruptly opened his eyes. A flash of icy light and murderous intent flickered through his deep, enigmatic gaze. His gaze fixed forward, as if piercing through the cave abode to some distant place. The next instant, he closed his eyes and began rotating his hands before him.","Within the secret realm, beneath a great tree where light mist swirled, Yue’er leaned against the trunk. Her face was deathly pale, cold sweat soaking her clothes. Her body trembled faintly. All around her was pitch black, leaving her utterly alone.","Yet, at that very instant, the core of the ten-thousand-year-old green spirit wood nestled in her hair glowed with a luminous radiance. A streak of green light flashed, and the Azure Emperor, who had been within the Yunxiao Mountain cave abode moments before, appeared here.","Seeing Yun Qi’s ashen face, the Azure Emperor radiated a bone-chilling aura. A flash of murderous intent flickered in his eyes—a stark contrast to his usual detached, indifferent demeanor.","He extended a finger, pressing it directly against Yun Qi’s forehead. Instantly, a piercing, unwilling scream seemed to echo through the forest.","\"Who are you! How dare you disrupt my plans!\"","The Azure Emperor narrowed his eyes. His deep, icy black pupils swept over the dissipating wisps of smoke and Yin energy. His voice was cold as ice: \"Dare to touch her, and I shall obliterate your very soul! You shall never find peace for all eternity!\""]},{"number":5219,"title":"Chapter 5219: Silently Departing","paragraphs":["Accompanying the Azure Emperor’s voice was a powerful aura of destruction. He supported the unconscious Yun Qi with one hand while gathering spirit energy in the other to grasp at the void. The dissipating Yin energy around him seemed to be forcibly trapped in that instant, and his hand pierced through it to seize a fragment of shadowy nothingness.","The shadow possessed a blurred form, its eyes glowing with an eerie green fire, now wide with terror. It struggled desperately to escape, even amplifying its own Yin energy until the surrounding trees and leaves were coated in a layer of frost. Yet it could not break free from the Azure Emperor’s grasp.","\"Who... who are you?\"","Despite its millennia of cultivation, it found itself utterly unable to escape this person’s grasp. The terrifying power emanating from this being was unlike anything it had encountered in its thousand years here. In that moment, an inexplicable dread washed over it, an aura of annihilation enveloping it. It felt as though its thousand-year-old spirit would be extinguished by this person in the very next instant.","\"Spare me... spare me, sir...\" It begged instinctively, utterly unaware that targeting the little girl with the innate spirit-gathering body would draw such a terrifying presence.","\"Too late.\"","A cold, indifferent voice carried a murderous intent. He stared at the ancient specter clutched in his hand, his palm tightening slowly as a powerful current of energy gathered. A flame seemed to ignite within his grasp, consuming the millennia-old specter until it was utterly incinerated.","\"Ah... no...\"","A shrill, wretched scream, filled with resentment and unwillingness, pierced the night. The sound, starting piercingly sharp, gradually grew weaker and fainter until the ghostly soul was completely consumed in his palm, leaving only two幽 green beads.","He examined the two beads in his hand, then swept his arm to dispel the lingering Yin energy from the space. Glancing down at the unconscious Yun Qi, he frowned.","\"Master... Master...\"","Whether it was the dissipation of the Yin energy or not, her consciousness slowly returned. Though her eyes remained closed, she called out repeatedly for her master, her arms clutching his hand tightly.","\"Master...\"","Yue’er slept restlessly, feeling herself plunged into boundless darkness. The coldness within that darkness froze her limbs, leaving her utterly powerless. Worst of all, within that void, it felt as though ghostly hands were tugging at her feet, trying to pull her deeper into the darkness.","But then, she thought she saw her master’s hand reaching out, pulling her from the darkness. It dispelled the icy chill from her body, allowing her to gradually feel a hint of warmth.","Ever since childhood, whenever she faced danger, it was always her master who came to her rescue. With him by her side, she felt safe.","The Azure Emperor sat beside her, letting her rest her head on his lap as she fell asleep. One hand rested lightly on her back, patting her gently, just as he had done when she had nightmares as a child, staying by her side.","The fire that had died out was rekindled by him. Warmed by its heat, her once-chilled body gradually grew warmer, and the slight frown between her brows slowly relaxed.","As dawn broke, the Azure Emperor glanced toward a certain spot in the forest, his gaze flickering. In the next moment, he supported Yun Qi against a tree trunk. His figure gradually faded, transforming into a streak of light that settled upon the core of the ten-thousand-year-old spirit wood nestled in Yun Qi’s hair.","Xiao Junyan had followed the sounds through the night, wandering the woods for a long while before sensing a human presence nearby. He had intended to investigate, only to find Yun Qi asleep against the tree."]},{"number":5220,"title":"Chapter 5220: Accompany","paragraphs":["Yet when he drew near and saw she still hadn’t awakened, his brow furrowed slightly. He called out, \"Little Qi?\" Given her usual vigilance, she shouldn’t have failed to notice his approach.","He came to her side and saw she seemed to have fallen into a deep sleep, unresponsive to his calls. But after checking her pulse, he found nothing amiss. So he sat down beside her, letting her rest her head on his shoulder, and then took out his cloak to cover her.","As dawn broke and rays of sunlight filtered through the forest canopy, Yue’er’s eyelashes fluttered lightly. Slowly opening her eyes, she found herself covered by a man’s cloak.","Startled, she sat up straight and saw Xiao Junyan opening his eyes in response to her movement.","\"Big Brother Xiao? Is it you?\" She looked at him, slightly startled and somewhat surprised.","\"Are you alright?\" Xiao Junyan asked.","His question made her recall last night’s events. She rubbed her temples, handing the cloak back to him as she said, \"I think I had a nightmare.\"","She couldn’t quite tell if last night had been merely a dream of hers, or if those events had truly occurred. Waking this morning, she felt only a dull ache in her head and a lingering dizziness.","\"How did you get here?\" she asked, glancing at him before scanning the surroundings. \"Did you notice anything unusual about this place?\"","\"I found my way here just before dawn. When I arrived, you were the only one here.\"","His voice trailed off as he continued, \"Strangely enough, when I entered this place, I seemed to be enveloped in a thick, white mist. I walked for a long time before breaking through it. Around midnight last night, it felt like a chilling wind stirred in this area, but by the time I came to investigate, it had vanished without a trace.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er’s eyes flickered slightly, her gaze drifting off as if lost in thought.","Noticing her dazed expression, Xiao Junyan said, \"Don’t worry. I’ll protect you. I won’t let you face any danger.\"","Yue’er lifted her head to meet his gaze, a faint smile touching her lips. \"Mhm, I’m fine.\" She gathered her thoughts before continuing, \"Big Brother Xiao, this place feels unusual. It seems more dangerous than any other place I’ve been before.\"","Xiao Junyan nodded. \"This place was discovered not long ago, and no one has ventured in yet. The dangers here are unknown. Although several families have sent quite a few people in, I doubt they’ll last even half a month inside.\"","\"Let’s go! We’ll check ahead.\" Xiao Junyan gestured, leading her forward together.","Meanwhile, outside the secret realm, the Patriarchs of several families stared in astonishment at those who had appeared in their clan teleportation arrays after just a single day.","\"What happened? How did you get out?\" The Patriarch of the Chen family asked the disgraced-looking group.","In less than a day, they were a disheveled mess—filthy, disheveled, and reeking. Had they not personally escorted them to the secret realm’s entrance yesterday, it would have been impossible to believe they’d become this wretched in such a short time.","\"Patriarch, the hidden dangers within that secret realm were beyond our defenses. Even with our strength, we could barely move an inch inside. Had we not shattered our teleportation jade to escape, we would likely have perished there,\" a man stated solemnly."]},{"number":5221,"title":"Chapter 5221: Discussion","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Patriarch Chen’s expression grew grave. After all, the twenty sent inside had been carefully selected by the clan. Though not as skilled as the main family’s members, they were certainly no weaklings. Yet now they claimed that had they not shattered their teleportation jade, they likely would have perished within.","This weighed heavily on his heart. If the secret realm was truly that perilous, he feared it would become difficult for his clan to send anyone in again. After a moment’s thought, he asked, \"What did you encounter inside? Tell me.\"","\"We were actually separated when we entered. A chilling aura permeated the air, and white mist obscured our vision. I was walking along when suddenly I sank into the ground. My feet felt as if they were being pulled deep into the earth—not like a swamp, but far more terrifying. Something beneath seemed to be tugging at my legs. The more I struggled, the deeper I sank. In the end, I had no choice but to crush the teleportation jade to escape.\" A man recounted as he shuddered.","\"I was swallowed by a bizarre banana plant. It wrapped itself around me, trapping me inside, and it seemed intent on devouring me. So I had no choice but to...\"","As the Chen family member spoke, others from the other clans asked questions.","\"Where I was, the trees had all become spirits. They formed an array, trapping me within a forest of branches that lashed at me like whips. Every wound on my body was inflicted by those tree spirits. I tried burning them with fire, but one of the tree spirits opened its mouth and bit down on my arm, tearing it clean off.\"","A pale, barely breathing man spoke, supported by two guards. Even back in his clan’s territory, terror and horror still filled his eyes.","\"That’s right. Those possessed trees—I couldn’t even cut through them with my sword.\"","Another man swallowed hard, took a deep breath, and added, \"I entered a forest just like that. When I tried to cut through them with my sword, there was a faint metallic ringing sound. This place is too unnerving. I truly fear that if those of us who went in couldn’t crush the teleportation jade token and leave immediately, we’d all die inside.\"","Listening to their words, the Patriarch of the Xiao family wore a grave expression. Just as he was about to ask more, a guard hurriedly reported: \"Patriarch, more people have emerged from the teleportation array.\"","Seeing this, he immediately quickened his pace to investigate. Arriving at the teleportation array, he saw several people covered in wounds. His voice was solemn as he asked, \"How are you? Are you all all right?\"","\"Patriarch, they’re dead... Xiao Feng and Xiao Wen are dead...\" a middle-aged man said, his expression filled with grief.","\"Gah! How could this happen!\" The Patriarch Xiao staggered back a step, his face etched with disbelief.","\"Patriarch, this secret realm is too treacherous. Even with our strength, survival inside was nearly impossible,\" another man said gravely, looking at Patriarch Xiao. \"My greatest concern now is the Young Master. We didn’t encounter him inside and have no idea his situation. If anything happened to him, I fear the main family...\"","Hearing this, the Patriarch Xiao’s heart lurched. He immediately commanded, \"Someone! Go immediately and summon the other family Patriarchs to discuss this!\"","Because other families had also received injured members returning throughout the day, and some even brought back news of family members lost within the realm, upon hearing the Xiao family had sent for them to gather at the residence for consultation, they promptly went."]},{"number":5222,"title":"Chapter 5222: Tricky","paragraphs":["Within the secret realm, Shen Shiqi also walked alone. Yet ever since entering this place, he had sensed the lurking dangers here. Therefore, even he dared not let his guard down.","\"Not a single soul encountered? Where could everyone be?\" He felt a slight surprise at this strange situation—not meeting a single person in the two days since entering.","Glancing around, he took out the communication jade and tried again. The previously silent jade finally responded.","Seeing this, he first attempted to contact the others. He discovered that while he could reach some, others were already unreachable.","As he bent over, holding the communication jade to inquire about others’ situations, he failed to notice the branches of the large tree behind him silently shifting. In that instant, they transformed like a vine, suddenly whipping toward him with a sharp whoosh.","Almost simultaneously, Shen Shiqi dodged aside in a flash, spinning around to look back. Seeing the tree branches whipping through the air, he raised an eyebrow. \" A tree possessed by a spirit?\" His hand moved, gripping a long sword. Seeing the vine attack, he leaped upward, swinging his blade at the vine.","\"Clang!\"","Instead of the expected snapping of the vine, a crisp metallic clang echoed, sparks flying between the vine and the sword’s edge.","\"Huh?\"","Shen Shiqi stared in astonishment at the vine. As surrounding trees suddenly softened like vines and coiled toward him, he spun and leapt aside, swiftly retreating.","He drew a fire starter, channeling sword qi into a burst of flame that he swung downward. The flames shot out with a whoosh, propelled by the sword qi’s air current, striking the dancing branches. Yet, despite the blazing fire, the great tree remained utterly undamaged.","\"Damn it!\"","His heart sank, his expression darkening. This extraordinary scene made him realize the situation was dire!","Without hesitation, he turned and fled. As he retreated, the surrounding trees shifted, forming a barrier to block his escape. What made him gasp in horror was the corpse dangling from the tip of one of the moving trees.","\"Hiss!\"","He stared in shock at the corpse, which seemed drained of all life force. That man was one of his Shen family’s men, one of the twenty who had entered. Just two days ago, he had seen him strutting around, chest puffed out, boasting that he was worth two men. Now, he was nothing but a desiccated corpse...","\"Whoosh!\"","\"Gah!\"","In that split second of distraction, a branch lashed out, striking his arm with lightning speed. In that instant, he felt the splintered wood piercing his flesh, greedily draining his vitality.","Without a second thought, he seized the branch with his free hand. A powerful force surged through his grasp, snapping the branch clean in two.","Snap!","The branch snapped and retracted sharply. His face hardened, radiating an intimidating aura of lethal intent. He reached up, pulled the embedded splinter from his arm, and watched the dancing vines and the formation of trees blocking his path. A low, cold laugh escaped him—a laugh that didn’t reach his eyes, tinged with a bone-chilling chill.","\"So, you’re no ordinary tree spirits!\" His eyes glinted with cold light as he stared at the trees, as his grip on the sword hilt tightened."]},{"number":5223,"title":"Chapter 5223: Vital Point","paragraphs":["\"Even humans have fatal weaknesses. Do you mere demon trees think I can’t handle you?\" He snorted coldly, his gaze sweeping over the trees. Suddenly, a faint gleam flashed in his eyes as he fixed his stare on the roots buried deep beneath the ground.","\"I’ll see if you truly are impervious to blades and arrows!\"","The moment the words left his mouth, his body flickered and darted toward the nearest demon tree. As he neared its trunk, the sword gripped in his reverse hand whirled swiftly. Channeling a powerful surge of sword qi, he thrust it violently into the earth.","A burst of sword energy erupted, sending earth flying. A branch snapped clean off, spilling milky sap. In that instant, it seemed as if the tree let out a wretched howl. The branches that had been lashing out at Shen Shiqi instantly retracted, and the entire tree withered rapidly.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","The other trees swiftly launched their attacks, lunging toward Shen Shiqi. Realizing the roots were indeed the weak point of these demon trees, Shen Shiqi instantly sidestepped and spun, dodging the incoming branches while simultaneously severing the roots buried deep underground.","Xiao Junyan and Yun Qi, who were nearby, exchanged glances upon hearing the commotion and immediately rushed toward the scene. They had just emerged from a patch of carnivorous plants.","As they approached, they halted. The tree formation blocked their view of those inside, though they could see streaks of sword qi surging out from within.","\"That sword aura looks incredibly powerful. Who could it be?\" she wondered, blinking her eyes in curiosity.","Xiao Junyan observed the surging currents in the air and the dancing branches. \"Probably another team leader,\" he remarked. The sword energy was sharp and carried a powerful momentum, combined with the oppressive aura pulsing through the air. Only someone from the major families possessed such formidable strength.","The two didn’t approach but watched from a distance until the commotion gradually subsided and the swaying branches all wilted. Then, Shen Shiqi emerged from within.","\"Huh? Who could it be?\" Spotting him, Yun Qi’s eyes crinkled with a smile. She stepped forward, examined the trees again, and asked, \"How did you make these demon trees wilt?\"","Shen Shiqi, recognizing the two, gave Xiao Junyan a slight nod before explaining to Yun Qi, \"This place is deeply unnatural. These aren’t ordinary tree spirits—they’re impervious to blades and fire. I had to sever their root systems to destroy them.\"","Yun Qi listened, then circled one tree to examine it. Seeing milky sap oozing from its roots, she dabbed some with her finger and sniffed it. A sudden thought struck her, and she retrieved tools from her spatial pouch to begin digging.","\"What are you doing?\" Shen Shiqi watched her with mild surprise, teasing, \"Could there be treasure buried beneath the tree?\"","\"I’ll find out by digging,\" Yue’er declared, straining to dig.","Seeing this, Xiao Junyan stepped forward. \"Let me handle it.\" He motioned her back, then braced both hands against the trunk. Planting his feet firmly in a horse stance, he channeled his spirit energy. With a surge of force, he yanked the massive tree from the ground.","Yue’er’s eyes widened. \"Big Brother Xiao, I never knew you were so strong!\"","\"The roots were already severed, so pulling it out wasn’t difficult,\" Xiao Junyan said. After pushing the tree trunk over, he looked at the emerald-green object beneath the roots and asked, \"Is this what you were searching for?\""]},{"number":5224,"title":"Chapter 5224: Signal","paragraphs":["\"Right, right!\" Yue’er’s eyes lit up. She came to his side, took the object he handed her, and smiled so broadly her eyes crinkled into slits.","\"I never thought it would actually exist.\" She glanced at the other trees, wondering, if this one had it beneath it, what about the others?","Seeing her expression, Xiao Junyan knew she wanted to know. He immediately helped push down all the trees. However, some had this emerald-green substance at their roots, while others beneath them did not.","\"Could this be tree crystals?\" Shen Shiqi stared at the objects in astonishment.","\"You destroyed those tree spirits, but I found these. I won’t take advantage of you—how about we split them?\" Yue’er smiled brightly at him.","Shen Shiqi chuckled, waving his hand. \"Alright, you keep them! These things are rare, but they’re useless to me. Besides, refining them isn’t easy.\"","\"Thank you then.\" Yue’er didn’t refuse. She couldn’t refine them either, but her Mother could. Once she collected enough, she’d have her Mother help refine them.","After gathering together, the three decided to explore the area. Walking in the middle, Yue’er said to Shen Shiqi, \"Why is it so eerie in here? I feel the danger level isn’t low! You have no idea—we even encountered man-eating plants on our way in. You really can’t let your guard down for a second.\"","\"That’s absolutely true. I never imagined the danger level here would be this high. I thought that even if no one had ever set foot here before, it would just be a secret realm. But now it seems every step is fraught with peril.\"","Shen Shiqi glanced at her and added, \"We must remain vigilant. If we encounter a crisis we can’t overcome, don’t hesitate—leaving this secret realm immediately is the best course of action.\"","\"Yes, I know,\" Yue’er nodded.","\"Some others have perished, while others likely left already. But I suspect Chen Tao and the others are still inside. I want to find them first.\" Shen Shiqi spoke, his gaze sweeping the surroundings as his divine sense spread out, constantly monitoring the area.","\"But this place is so vast. How will we find them?\" Yue’er asked, looking at him. \"Send a signal?\"","Xiao Junyan glanced at Shen Shiqi, replying, \"That’s a good idea.\"","Seeing this, Shen Shiqi smiled. \"That’s exactly what I was thinking. Perfect timing—we can find a place to rest our legs.\"","So the three sought out a relatively safe spot to rest. Meanwhile, Shen Shiqi sent three signals skyward in quick succession.","Deep within the forest, some distance away, Chen Tao and his group spotted the signals from different directions. Their eyes lit up, and they immediately set off toward the beacons.","Other members still within the secret realm also saw the signals and aimed to join them. However, on their way to the beacon locations, some perished in the realm’s forests, while many others crushed their teleportation jade tablets to escape the secret realm...","As night fell, by the campfire, Yue’er played with two pearls gleaming with a faint green light, fastened to her waist. These pearls had appeared on her body after last night, and she had no idea where they came from. With some free time tonight, she kept holding and examining the two pearls. They seemed like spirit pearls, yet the light they emitted felt oddly peculiar. Somehow, it reminded her of last night’s dream."]},{"number":5225,"title":"Chapter 5225: Illusion","paragraphs":["She wondered if it wasn’t a dream after all, but something that had truly happened. But who could that person be? Not Xiao Junyan—could it be...","For a moment, she froze. The person she thought of was her master. Because whenever she faced danger, it was always her master who appeared to protect her. Besides her, who else would come to her side at such a time?","\"Little Qi, freshly grilled.\" Xiao Junyan cut a piece of roasted meat for her.","\"Oh, thank you.\" She responded, pulling her thoughts back, accepting the leaf-wrapped meat and eating it.","\"Something’s moving!\" Shen Shiqi, mid-bite, sprang to his feet, sword in hand, staring into the pitch-black night.","Almost the instant he stood, Xiao Junyan and Yue’er also rose swiftly. They scanned the darkness, listening to the rustling sounds at their ears, alertness sharpening.","\"It’s the Yin Wind.\"","Xiao Junyan said, observing the leaves swaying in the sudden night breeze, listening to their rustling sounds, and catching glimpses of the shadowy spirits.","Shen Shiqi saw a ring of shadowy spirits gathered in the darkness. They dared not approach, hovering about ten meters away, staring intently at the three of them.","\"I have a way to deal with them,\" Yue’er said, drawing her whip. With a swift flick of her wrist, the whip whistled through the air, lashing out at the surrounding spirits.","\"Crack!\"","\"Crack! Crack! Crack!\"","After several swift lashes, the whip’s aura radiated out, leaving marks on the surrounding trees. The ghostly spirits that had been encircling them suddenly scattered with a whoosh, vanishing swiftly.","Shen Shiqi stared at the whip in her hand and whistled in admiration. \"Who knew the Divine Whip was this powerful!\"","Yue’er chuckled. \"Well, that’s why it’s called the Divine Whip!\"","As the entities drifted away, the oppressive aura in the area eased somewhat. The three sat down to eat, continuing until midnight. Yue’er rested while Xiao Junyan and Shen Shiqi took turns keeping watch.","As dawn approached, faint cries for help echoed from the forest.","\"Help... Help me...\"","\"Sounds like someone’s there,\" Shen Shiqi remarked. \"I’ll go check.\"","Xiao Junyan and Yue’er snapped awake. Exchanging a glance, they followed Shen Shiqi toward the source of the cries.","After walking about a hundred meters, they saw a massive green plant by a black muddy pool, seemingly clutching a person. The victim’s upper body was already in its jaws, only the legs still struggling. The cries for help were coming from inside that green plant.","\"It’s someone from my Shen family!\" Shen Shiqi’s expression darkened as he rushed forward, slashing at the plant with his sword.","\"No! Come back!\" Xiao Junyan shouted suddenly, lunging forward to grab him.","Shen Shiqi paused at his words, glancing back. At that very moment, Yue’er bellowed, \"It’s a trap! Retreat!\"","In that instant, the man-biting greenery shot out two tendrils like whips, lashing toward Shen Shiqi. The person who had been trapped inside vanished without a trace, leaving not even a shadow behind.","Shen Shiqi froze for a second. He twisted his sword in his hand, severing the two tendrils. But just then, a giant leaf swept toward him, carrying a wind blade. He dodged swiftly, but his foot caught on something, sending him tumbling backward."]},{"number":5226,"title":"Chapter 5226: Changes","paragraphs":["\"Watch out!\"","Seeing him about to tumble into the black mud pit behind, Yue’er lashed out with her whip, snatching his foot and pulling him back.","With her assistance, Shen Shiqi, who had lost his balance, quickly regained his footing, spinning around to land on solid ground.","At that moment, Xiao Junyan frowned at the surrounding green plants, their mouths agape, dripping liquid. \"These plants mimic human voices,\" he said. \"And the scent they emit induces hallucinations.\"","\"Help... help...\"","The sound echoed again, emanating from the greenery. It mimicked the desperate cries of someone seeking help—or perhaps, someone had indeed fallen victim earlier, swallowed whole. In that moment of utter despair, they had cried out for rescue, yet no one could come to their aid.","After destroying the surrounding man-eating plants, the trio exchanged glances. Shen Shiqi remarked, \"I suspect the deeper we go, the stranger things will get.\"","\"Oh? It’s you guys?\" Two figures leapt through the air, bounding over the trees and landing beside Shen Shiqi.","\"Yun Qi, I didn’t expect you’d still be here. I thought you’d left long ago! But honestly, this place really isn’t suitable for a young girl like you. It’s far too dangerous.\" Zheng Yuan shook his head.","Yue’er smiled, her eyes crinkling. \"I’m fine. Don’t worry about me. I can protect myself.\"","\"This place is some kind of haunted spot. We’ve only come a short distance, yet it’s taken us forever. Let me tell you, you have to be careful around this black mud. It eats people. Once you step in, getting out is tough,\" Chen Tao chimed in.","Shen Shiqi glanced at the two of them and asked, \"How did you two end up together?\"","\"We met along the way,\" Chen Shou replied. \"Though I only encountered him—no sign of the others. I wonder if they’ve perished?\" He scanned the surroundings and sighed softly. \"I thought this secret realm wouldn’t be too dangerous, but it’s already claimed quite a few lives.\"","After gathering and chatting for a while, the group moved on. After walking for some time, they heard the sounds of combat echoing through the forest. Exchanging glances, they swiftly headed toward the source of the commotion.","\"Yang Hao?\" Shen Shiqi and the others called out in surprise. They saw him surrounded by a pack of fierce beasts. The beasts were numerous and quite powerful. Under their coordinated attack, Yang Hao had already sustained many injuries. Immediately, the group gathered their energy and leapt forward, joining the fray.","Seeing them, Yang Hao gasped for air. \"Phew! Looks like I won’t die here after all.\"","With Shen Shiqi and the others joining the fray, the beasts sensed defeat and quickly fled. Since Yang Hao had sustained multiple injuries, Yue’er took out some medicine and bandaged his wounds.","\"Thank you,\" Yang Hao said, nodding to her in gratitude.","Yue’er smiled and said, \"Fortunately, the injuries aren’t severe. Stopping the bleeding and bandaging them should do the trick. No big deal.\"","The group gathered around, sharing stories of their recent encounters and observations within this realm. They even discussed the peculiar occurrences they’d witnessed, hoping to gain insights from the others.","However, just as their conversation grew lively, the ground began to tremble faintly. Thunder and lightning erupted in the sky, and soon, rain as large as beans began to fall."]},{"number":5227,"title":"Chapter 5227: Arcadia Immortal Abode","paragraphs":["\"It’s raining?\" The group murmured in surprise, not expecting rain to suddenly fall inside.","\"Something’s off. Look—the sky feels strange, doesn’t it?\" Yue’er asked, gazing upward. The heavens seemed transformed, stretching like a vast mirror with powerful spirit energy rippling across its surface.","\"Something’s off. I think we should leave immediately. If we delay, who knows what might happen,\" Zheng Yuan said, his expression turning grave.","\"But we’ve already come this far. Leaving now feels like giving up,\" Chen Tao countered, his gaze fixed on the sky’s transformation.","\"The path of cultivation—fortune and misfortune are intertwined. How can we know what awaits us, whether blessing or curse, without daring to venture forth?\" Shen Shiqi narrowed his eyes, showing no intention of leaving.","\"Hahaha, indeed!\" Yang Hao laughed aloud. Glancing at his bandaged wound, then up at the sky, he chuckled, \"I’m also curious—what exactly is waiting for us?\"","Xiao Junyan shielded Yun Qi behind him, silent but inwardly debating whether to send her away first.","Yun Qi, however, kept her eyes fixed upward. Suddenly, as the mirror-like object in the sky began surging downward, sucking toward them, her expression changed. \"Quick, get out of the way!\"","The moment the words left her mouth, she grabbed Xiao Junyan and sprinted away. Shen Shiqi and the others, seeing them dash in one direction, immediately sprinted off in the opposite direction. But just then, a powerful suction force pulled down from above, violently drawing them all in.","\"Ah!\"","\"Whoosh!\"","They felt the undulating waves in the sky ripple briefly, like ripples spreading across a mirror-like lake surface. In that instant, it sucked them all in, then vanished as quickly as it had appeared, returning to stillness.","\"Ah!\"","Amidst the cries of alarm, two figures crashed to the ground. Xiao Junyan, shielding Yun Qi, used his own body as a cushion for her impact. The force of her fall struck him hard, causing him to grunt in pain.","\"Big Brother Xiao? Are you alright? Are you hurt?\"","Yue’er regained her senses, realizing she’d landed on top of him, her entire body cradled in his arms. His body had cushioned her fall, preventing any serious injury, so she quickly scrambled to her feet.","\"I’m fine. What about you?\" Xiao Junyan asked, sitting up and glancing around. But that single glance made his eyes narrow slightly.","\"I’m fine too.\"","Yue’er replied, glancing around curiously. \"Big Brother Xiao, where is this place? How could such a location exist within the secret realm? I recall we were sucked in earlier. Shen Shiqi and the others seem to have vanished—no idea where they went.\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, this should be the Arcadia Immortal Abode within the secret realm,\" he said, taking her hand. \"Follow me. Be careful.\" Thus, holding her hand, he led her deeper inside.","But just then, several streaks of sword energy whistled toward them. Xiao Junyan, who was in front, felt a chill in his heart. He swiftly pushed Yun Qi aside. The very instant he shoved her away, a fierce sword energy streaked past where Yun Qi had just stood.","Whoosh! Whoosh!","Several more blades shot out from within, splitting into two streams to attack Xiao Junyan and Yun Qi. As Yun Qi dodged and retreated to the side, she saw the blades already heading toward Xiao Junyan. At that very moment, a thick cloud of smoke billowed up from the cave abode, instantly obscuring their vision."]},{"number":5228,"title":"Chapter 5228: Illusion","paragraphs":["Unable to see Xiao Junyan, Yue’er had no choice but to confront the imminent danger alone. Though her strength fell short of Xiao Junyan’s, she still possessed the means to defuse certain threats.","Mist swirled thickly around them, yet slashes of icy-cold blades pierced through the haze, striking with deadly intent as if determined to end their lives.","Whoosh! Whoosh!","Yue’er calmed her mind to focus on the crisis. Yet the blades were swift and dense as arrows. Even evading vital points left her with superficial wounds. Forced back into a corner to dodge the blades,","Just then, as she was forced back into a corner, her foot seemed to step on something. Her entire body fell backward, as if tumbling into another space.","\"Ah!\"","She instinctively let out a low cry before vanishing.","\"Little Qi!\"","Xiao Junyan immediately scanned the area beyond the cry, only to see several sword blades streaking toward Yun Qi. The fierce sword qi and the murderous intent radiating from the blades sent a chill through him. He shouted, \"Watch out!\"","The words barely left his lips when he lunged forward, pulling her into his embrace. His hand swept out to deflect the incoming blades. Yet, overwhelmed by the sheer number, one sword still pierced his body with a sharp whistling sound. In that very instant, the figure he held vanished into a cloud of smoke within his arms.","Xiao Junyan froze, his brow furrowing tightly. One hand pressed against his stabbed abdomen while he scanned the surroundings. The swords had vanished, and the smoke had dispersed. Within this space, Yun Qi’s figure was nowhere to be seen.","\"Little Qi!\" he cried out. The movement caused the wound to bleed more profusely.","\"Big Brother Xiao!\"","Yue’er had no idea what was happening. She had fallen into this place, trapped as if within an invisible space. She could see Xiao Junyan, but he seemed unable to see her.","Watching the blood seep through the gaps between his fingers as he clutched his abdomen, she felt both worry and guilt. If that mist hadn’t taken her form, if he hadn’t tried to shield her, someone of his cultivation wouldn’t have been wounded.","Yet what Yue’er never anticipated was that for the long stretch that followed, the recurring visions felt as real as if she were there herself. Isolated like an outsider, she watched as Xiao Junyan’s wounds multiplied and his complexion grew paler by the moment.","She stared blankly, her eyes reddening as mist clouded her vision. Ever since leaving the mountain gates and spending time together, she knew he might truly care for her. But she never imagined that upon seeing her in danger—even if it was likely just an illusion—he wouldn’t dare take risks, leading him to suffer injury time and again...","She didn’t know what love was, but in this moment, her heart softened.","\"Hmph... Who would’ve thought he’s such a hopeless romantic.\"","A cold, female voice suddenly echoed, tinged with resentment and mockery.","\"Who’s there? Who are you? Why are you doing this to him!\" Yue’er shouted angrily, scanning her surroundings, but found nothing.","\"Heh heh heh... Not a single man in this world is worth a damn. Don’t be fooled by his willingness to suffer for you—he’ll change his heart in the blink of an eye. Besides, as an innate spirit-gathering body, he probably only covets your body.\"","The icy laughter echoed crisply in Yue’er’s ears."]},{"number":5229,"title":"Chapter 5229: Purpose","paragraphs":["\"What do you want! What’s your purpose in doing all of this?!\"","Yue’er shouted angrily. Ever since entering this place, they’d been set up. The smoke had isolated them, and she was trapped in this space, watching Big Brother Xiao get injured time and again just to protect her. What did this person want?","\"Hmph... Purpose? Naturally, it’s you.\" The woman’s voice rose slightly at the end before continuing, \"An innate spirit-gathering body, possessing an ancient Sacred Beast, and bearing a seal within. You must have quite the extraordinary background, right?\"","She chuckled softly, her voice icy yet tinged with an eerie delight. \"No one has entered for so many years. Who would’ve thought the one who came this time would have such a splendid vessel? Truly, it makes one eager!\"","Yue’er’s heart sank. Her spirit body was undetectable to ordinary people—only demons, ghosts, or powerful beings like her Father and Mother, or her master, could perceive it.","After all, they had concealed it for her. Yet now, this shadowy figure, whose true nature remained unknown, had uncovered it. Worse, they knew of the Sacred Beast within her—proof of terrifying strength.","But if this being coveted her body, it was highly unlikely to be human!","\"If I’m your target, why attack Big Brother Xiao? And why use my appearance to create an illusion?\" Yue’er pressed, her mind racing with thoughts of how to escape this space.","\"Hehehe... You’ll find out soon enough.\" As the voice faded, Yue’er suddenly felt a force propel her outward, hurling her toward the exit.","\"Big Brother Xiao!\" She rushed over to support him. \"How are you? Sit down quickly! I’ll stop the bleeding first!\"","\"Little Qi?\"","Xiao Junyan stared at her, momentarily unable to discern whether the person before him was an illusion or real. Each illusion carried Yun Qi’s aura, extremely alike the real her, leaving him unable to tell them apart.","\"It’s me, Big Brother Xiao.\" Seeing his wounds, her eyes welled with tears. \"I’m sorry. It’s all my fault.\"","\"As long as you’re unharmed, that’s all that matters. We can’t linger here. We must leave immediately.\" Xiao Junyan spoke, clasping her hand firmly. \"Let’s go!\"","\"Go? Hah... Do you really think you can leave?\"","The voice echoed again, this time audible even to Xiao Junyan.","\"Who’s there!\" Xiao Junyan barked, his face darkening as he scanned the surroundings. Despite his severe injuries, he forced himself to stand firm.","\"I was trapped by her earlier. This person is formidable, but it’s highly likely they’re not human,\" Yue’er said, examining the wounds still oozing blood on his body. She held a medicine bottle in one hand and sprinkled the liquid onto his injuries.","\"Once you enter this place, you cannot leave. You won’t escape my grasp.\"","The voice seemed to sense the two retrieving their teleportation jade. The cold tone echoed again: \"I advise you not to waste your efforts. Even with teleportation jade, it won’t help. However, if you truly wish to leave, it’s not impossible. But only one of you can leave here alive.\"","While the voice spoke, Yue’er’s gaze darted around the room. She realized they hadn’t moved since entering—there was nowhere to hide here. Even if there were, it would likely be a trap or an array.","But where exactly was that voice coming from?","Suddenly, her eyes landed on a painting on the wall not far ahead."]},{"number":5230,"title":"Chapter 5230: Divine Soul","paragraphs":["It was a portrait of a beauty, the woman in the painting holding a mirror to her face. Yet upon closer inspection, it seemed as though the lips of the beauty in the portrait were moving.","Her heart skipped a beat, a gleam flashing in her eyes. Seizing the moment while the voice still spoke, she lunged forward in a single swift stride. The dagger clenched in her hand plunged viciously into the beauty depicted in the portrait.","\"Hisssssssssss! You... How dare you!\"","A bloodcurdling scream rang out, followed immediately by an angry, frenzied voice.","At the moment the dagger pierced, Yue’er sensed a current of air seeming to sweep across the painting. She had cut through that current, driving the dagger deep into the beauty’s chest. Dimly, she thought she saw a trickle of blood emerge. Just as she tried to look closer, a powerful force from the portrait hurled her backward.","\"Damn little brat!\" The voice surged toward her, stirring a fierce wind within the space, carrying a bone-chilling cold.","\"Little Qi!\" Xiao Junyan rushed forward to catch her as she was sent flying.","\"Big Brother Xiao, it’s that painting! There’s something strange about it! If we destroy it, we might be able to leave this place.\" Yue’er seemed to have discovered something, her voice tinged with surprise and delight.","Xiao Junyan looked over. The painting now seemed to be leaking spirit energy, wisps of aura seeping from the tear made by Yun Qi’s dagger.","Immediately, he surged spirit energy from his palm. As it surged forth, a ball of flame shot toward the painting. Simultaneously, Yue’er also gathered a ball of flame in her hand and hurled it at the painting.","Both flames shot forth, igniting the wall-mounted painting in the blink of an eye. At that very moment, a shrill wail erupted from within the painting. Along with the surging energy, a translucent soul drifted out.","In that instant, she radiated a world-shattering, bone-chilling aura filled with murderous intent. That presence enveloped the entire space, sending a piercing coldness surging up from the soles of their feet, freezing them solid.","\"How dare you destroy the vessel of my divine soul! You both deserve to die!\"","As the vicious voice faded, the soul entity swept toward them, unleashing a powerful gust that violently knocked them apart.","\"Little Qi!\"","Xiao Junyan steadied himself and gasped in horror. The soul essence had seized Yun Qi, hoisting her upward as if to wring her life out. Though an invisible spirit form, it wielded terrifying strength in that moment.","\"I intended to let you taste utter despair before devouring your soul and possessing your body. That way, I could sever your seven emotions and six desires, continuing my cultivation of the Path of Indifference. But you ruined my plans!\"","She spoke with sinister relish, watching Yun Qi, her face flushed crimson and speechless. A cold smile spread across her lips. \" It’s alright. Since I couldn’t sever your seven emotions and six desires before possessing your body and devouring your soul, I’ll just have to endure the suffering myself after taking over your body—to extract those emotions and desires from within.\"","As she spoke, madness and excitement surged in her eyes. Her lips moved slightly, as if chanting some ancient incantation.","\"Get out of my way!\"","Xiao Junyan swung his sword with brutal force, striking directly at the soul fragment. A powerful surge of energy and force erupted, though it failed to extinguish the soul entirely. Instead, it faded slightly, retreating several steps backward. The momentum caused Yue’er, who had been suspended mid-air, to plummet toward the ground."]},{"number":5231,"title":"Chapter 5231: Know","paragraphs":["\"You’re asking for death!\"","The divine soul flew into a rage, slamming a palm toward Xiao Junyan. Xiao Junyan, who had been about to step forward to catch Yun Qi, couldn’t dodge in time. He took the full force of the strike as he was sent flying several metres away, spitting out a mouthful of blood.","\"Pfft!\"","At this moment, the soul fragment seemed less concerned with possessing a body. Instead, it gathered immense power once more, striking at Xiao Junyan with a vengeance, as if venting fury.","\"You’re all worthless trash!\"","Watching that lethal strike descend upon the gravely wounded Xiao Junyan, Yue’er’s heart clenched. Her eyes narrowed as she cried out in alarm.","\"Big Brother Xiao!\"","Without a second thought, she lunged forward. In that instant, only one thought occupied her mind: he must not die because of her!","As for her own fate? She had no time to consider it.","\"Thud!\"","\"Pfft!\"","The palm strike, packed with immense force, slammed into Yun Qi’s body. In that instant, even Xiao Junyan, pinned beneath her, could distinctly hear the sound of bones snapping and tendons tearing.","\"Nooooooooooooo!\"","Blood spilled from his mouth as his cry of alarm gradually faded. Even with Yun Qi shielding him from the fatal blow, its sheer force left him, pinned beneath her, unable to escape its impact.","Already gravely wounded, this strike compounded his injuries. Though not fatal, it left him barely clinging to life.","Yue’er gazed at him, her lips twitching into a pale, faint smile. \" Big... Big Brother Xiao, let me... protect you this once...\" Her voice trailed off, broken and faint, and she lost consciousness.","\"Hahahahahaha...\"","The soul laughed wildly, its laughter tinged with hatred. \"Wretched bones! All of you are wretched bones!\" As it spoke, glancing at Yue’er’s body, a strange, almost tender pain flickered across its face.","\"Such a fine body, and it’s been damaged... It’s alright. Once I’ve taken possession and left this place, I’ll simply find another body.\" She murmured, sensing her soul gradually dissipating. Paying no heed to Xiao Junyan, who was still barely alive, she swiftly transformed into a halo of light and shot into Yue’er’s brow.","\"Little Qi... Little Qi...\" Xiao Junyan himself was barely clinging to life. Forcing himself upright, he retrieved a medicinal pill from his spatial ring and tremblingly stuffed it into Yue’er’s mouth.","\"Stay alive! You must stay alive!\" he murmured. The panic and terror gripping him in that moment were beyond anyone’s comprehension.","Unbeknownst to him, within the same spatial realm, Shen Shiqi and the others found themselves isolated, just as Yun Qi had been before. Trapped there, they tried every possible method to escape but failed, forced to watch helplessly as this scene unfolded.","Almost the instant Yue’er lost consciousness, within Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor, who had been meditating with eyes closed, opened his own. His expression turned as cold as frost. This time, however, he could only sense that something had happened to Yun Qi—he couldn’t discern her condition, as if his senses had been completely severed.","At the same moment, Feng Jiu and Xuanyuan Mo Ze, who were wandering in a certain place, had been laughing and joking just a moment before. Their expressions changed abruptly.","\"Yue’er is in trouble!\"","Even though they weren’t physically beside the three children, if any of them faced life-or-death crises, the two would sense it immediately.","And at this moment, that sensation was overwhelmingly intense.","Without a moment’s hesitation, the two rushed back, intending to check on Yunxiao Mountain first.","Yet, what the soul seeking to possess Yunqi hadn’t anticipated was that the moment it entered Yun Qi’s sea of consciousness, escape became impossible..."]},{"number":5232,"title":"Chapter 5232: Meridians utterly destroyed","paragraphs":["\"Gah! This... This is the Karma Flame Red Lotus!\"","The fragment of divine soul entered Yue’er’s sea of consciousness. Upon seeing the sealed Primordial Red Lotus, it sucked in a sharp breath.","\"What on earth is this little brat’s background? How could a sealed Primordial Red Lotus exist within her sea of consciousness?\" At this moment, even a mere fragment of divine soul felt profoundly unsettled.","A sensation called fear even began to spread within its heart. From the moment it entered, it had sensed the immense power of the soul within this sea of consciousness. Now, upon seeing the Karma Flame Red Lotus, it knew it had picked the wrong target. One misstep, and even this fragment of soul might vanish into the void, unable to even enter the cycle of reincarnation.","Transformed into a halo of light, the soul drifted within the sea of consciousness. Daring not to approach the sealed Primordial Red Lotus, it instead flew toward Yun Qi’s core spirit.","Once she devoured this core spirit, this body would be hers!","At this moment, she had no retreat. She could only grit her teeth and fight. If she succeeded, this body bearing the Primordial Red Lotus would be hers!","Yet, to her shock, before she could draw near, Yun Qi’s divine essence shot toward her, seemingly intent on devouring this intruder that had invaded her consciousness.","\"Damn it! How could this happen!\"","A startled cry echoed as the soul fragment tried to retreat in terror. Yet it was suddenly seized by Yun Qi’s divine soul, which bit down fiercely. The fist-sized soul shrank instantly, and within mere moments, the invading soul was completely devoured.","\"No—\"","A voice of unwillingness echoed, growing fainter and fainter until Yun Qi’s divine soul completely devoured it. Not only did it double in size, but it even let out a satisfied burp.","Apart from that divine soul fragment, no one else knew why such a powerful divine soul had been devoured by Yun Qi’s...","\"Little Qi! Little Qi...\" Xiao Junyan called out repeatedly.","At that very moment, as Yun Qi devoured the soul fragment, the spatial barrier trapping Shen Shiqi and the others vanished.","The group paused, glancing at the vanished space. With its disappearance, the cave abode finally revealed its true form.","\"Yun Qi!\"","Shen Shiqi and the others hurried forward, taking her from Xiao Junyan’s arms. Zheng Yuan reached out to feel her pulse, wanting to assess the extent of her injuries. But the moment his fingers touched her pulse, his expression changed abruptly.","\"Yun Qi, Yun Qi, wake up!\" Shen Shiqi cried out, turning to Zheng Yuan. \"How is she? What’s wrong?\"","\"Don’t shake her,\" Zheng Yuan hurriedly said as he looked back at him and started uttering with difficulty, \"Her... her meridians are all severed, her internal organs are damaged... I’m afraid...\"","\"No! It can’t be!\" Hearing this, Xiao Junyan was overcome with rage and fury. Darkness engulfed his vision, and he collapsed unconscious.","Seeing him collapse, Shen Shiqi immediately ordered, \"Let’s go! Get them out for treatment now!\"","Without another thought for the cave abode, the group swiftly crushed their teleportation jade tablets and departed.","The very moment they exited the cave abode, the Azure Emperor’s eyes flashed within Yunxiao Mountain. His azure figure vanished instantly into the mountain’s depths.","Xiao Junyan was carried back to the Xiao family. Seeing the gravely injured and unconscious Xiao Junyan, the Patriarch Xiao dared not act on his own initiative and swiftly sent word to the main family.","At the Shen family, after Shen Shiqi had settled Yun Qi, he immediately summoned all the doctors and alchemists to treat her.","\"Quick! Examine her! We must cure her at all costs!\""]},{"number":5233,"title":"Chapter 5233: He’s the Azure Emperor","paragraphs":["Not only had Shen Shiqi issued orders to gather every doctor, healer and alchemist in the city, but Chen Tao, Zheng Yuan, and Yang Hao had also brought theirs from their own clans.","Yet, as each of them emerged, shaking their heads, their hearts sank one by one.","Could it truly be beyond saving?","\"Master Shiqi, this young lady’s meridians are completely severed, and her internal organs are all damaged. If not for the protective items on her body, she likely wouldn’t have survived,\" an elderly man shook his head and said.","\"That she’s still alive is a miracle. Anyone else would have perished instantly. As for her injuries and those utterly destroyed tendons and meridians... I’m afraid even I am powerless to help,\" another elder shook his head.","\"Is there truly no hope?\" Shen Shiqi murmured, grief clouding his eyes. \"She’s barely a teenager... Is she really ruined like this?\"","Thinking of Yun Qi—from that tiny child all those years ago to now—he couldn’t fathom how much suffering she’d endured. Now, with her tendons destroyed and organs shattered, even if healed, she’d be crippled for life. How could she bear such a blow?","Chen Tao patted his shoulder. \"We should find a way to contact her master! Perhaps he might have a solution.\"","\"Right! Let’s take her back to Yunxiao Mountain! Maybe her master can save her!\" Shen Shiqi declared, swiftly approaching the bedside. He carefully lifted the pale, barely conscious Yun Qi from the mattress.","\"We’ll go with you,\" Chen Tao and the others declared.","Yet, as they stepped out of the room, ready to leave, a gust of wind swept in, revealing a figure before them.","\"Who are you?!\" they demanded warily, staring at the suddenly appearing, strikingly handsome man clad in blue.","The Azure Emperor stood with one hand behind his back and the other before him. He didn’t answer their question, merely gazing at the pale, barely breathing young apprentice being held. Step by step, he advanced.","\"Stop! Don’t come any closer!\"","Chen Tao and the others shouted, sensing an overwhelming aura emanating from the handsome man in azure. As he drew nearer, they felt an oppressive weight descend upon them, causing cold sweat to break out and leaving them frozen in place.","The Azure Emperor raised his hand, gently brushing aside those blocking his path. He walked slowly to Shen Shiqi’s side, his gaze falling on Yun Qi, unconscious in his embrace. His brow furrowed slightly, a fleeting look of heartache flashing through his eyes.","He reached out, carefully lifting her from Shen Shiqi’s arms. Only then did he ask, \"How was she injured?\" With her cultivation level, she shouldn’t have sustained such severe wounds.","Shen Shiqi had been observing him since his arrival. Seeing how he cradled Yun Qi as if she were a precious treasure, coupled with his striking beauty and overwhelming aura, he immediately guessed that this man before him must be Yun Qi’s master—the Azure Emperor!","\"We were in the secret realm when sucked into a cave abode. There, all connections were severed. An immensely powerful divine soul attempted to possess Yun Qi. Then...\" Shen Shiqi recounted everything that had transpired inside, leaving nothing out.","Finally, gazing at the Azure Emperor’s inscrutable expression, he pleaded, \"I’ve consulted every doctor, healer and alchemist in the city, but none can heal her. I beg you, Senior, please save her.\"","The Azure Emperor shot him a glance, then turned and walked away, carrying Yun Qi in his arms. With each step forward, he vanished from their sight within just a few strides."]},{"number":5234,"title":"Chapter 5234: Words","paragraphs":["Half a month later, Yunxiao Mountain.","Feng Jiu gazed at her still-unconscious daughter and sighed softly, \"Why must this child endure so much suffering?\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze wrapped his arm around her shoulder and said, \"Don’t worry. She’ll wake up.\"","\"I thought with her ancient contract beast, the Sacred Beast protecting her, and the Azure Emperor watching over her, nothing could harm her. Yet barely out of the mountains, she’s already reduced herself to this state.\" Feng Jiu sighed softly, her eyes filled with worry.","\"The Azure Emperor said she took that blow for Xiao Junyan. Had it not been for him, with her abilities, she wouldn’t have been injured.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze’s deep voice flowed calmly, yet a flash of coldness flickered in his eyes when Xiao Junyan’s name was mentioned.","Regardless of the reason, his precious daughter had suffered such injuries for the sake of Xiao Junyan. That debt must be settled with Xiao Junyan.","\"Enough, don’t go stirring up trouble.\" Feng Jiu understood his meaning the moment she heard it. She shot him a glance and said, \"The fact that Yue’er was injured so badly trying to save him shows that Xiao Junyan still holds a certain place in her heart.\"","Her gaze drifted to Yue’er lying on the bed as she continued, \"Our Yue’er is a young lady now. Xiao Junyan and she share childhood bonds. Back then, their hearts were untouched by romance, but now, in the bloom of youth, it’s only natural for feelings to blossom through their time together.\"","She gently stroked her daughter’s gaunt little face. \"Back then, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian even mentioned the possibility of a marriage alliance. If Yue’er truly has feelings for him, agreeing to it wouldn’t be a problem.\"","\"But that boy looks more and more like a thorn in my side,\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze said, frowning.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu chuckled softly, shooting him a sidelong glance. \"You know, I don’t think you dislike Xiao Junyan—I think you dislike anyone who wants to marry your daughter.\"","\"Yue’er is still young. Don’t arrange her marriage too soon. I was thinking of bringing her home to live for a while.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze continued, gazing at his daughter on the bed. \"The three children haven’t been with us much since they were young. Hao’er and Chen’er are fine—they’re boys. But Yue’er is a girl. I’ve always worried about her being away from home. Since we’re returning now, I thought we might as well bring her back with us. It would also be a good chance to help her properly regulate her health.\"","His voice paused before continuing, \"Also, what exactly is Xiao Junyan’s attitude toward Yue’er? Could he be approaching her only because the Azure Emperor is her master? Xiao Junyan comes from a prominent family. Right now, Yue’er is merely an apprentice of the Azure Emperor with no known family background. Might the Xiao family look down on her?\"","His gaze shifted to Feng Jiu. \"Or do you intend to reveal Yue’er’s identity outright?\" Seeing Feng Jiu raise an eyebrow at him, he added, \"If that’s truly your plan, I must object. I won’t accept a suitor who values my daughter solely for her status and family background.\"","Feng Jiu chuckled softly, her eyes twinkling with amusement. \" How did I never realize that you were so calculative before? Are you saying anyone who falls for our daughter must be after her status as the Azure Emperor’s disciple? Does that mean our daughter isn’t remarkable enough?\"","She chuckled, then glanced at Yue’er on the bed. Her smile faded as she said, \"But you do have a point. We really should test them.\""]},{"number":5235,"title":"Chapter 5235: Waking Up","paragraphs":["Xuanyuan Mo Ze looked at her and asked, \"What do you plan to do?\"","Feng Jiu smiled faintly and replied, \"No rush. You’ll find out when the time comes.\"","Seeing she already had a plan, Xuanyuan Mo Ze felt reassured. Just then, he caught sight of the Azure Emperor entering the room out of the corner of his eye and rose to look at him.","\"Still not awake?\" the Azure Emperor inquired, his gaze fixed on Yun Qi, who lay unconscious on the bed.","\"I expect she’ll awaken within the next couple of days,\" Feng Jiu replied, meeting the Azure Emperor’s eyes. \"Mo Ze and I plan to take Yue’er back to recuperate. With her injuries, it’ll likely take a year or two before she fully recovers.\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor gazed at Yun Qi on the bed. After a moment of silence, he said, \"We’ll see when she wakes.\"","Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow at this, meeting his gaze before adding, \"One more thing—once Yue’er wakes, I intend to ask her wishes and arrange her marriage to Xiao Junyan of the Xiao family. As her master, what are your thoughts on this match?\"","A barely perceptible frown crossed the Azure Emperor’s brow. \"Xiao Junyan? That boy is unworthy of Yun Qi.\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze, standing nearby, nodded in agreement, a faint smile playing on his lips. \"Indeed, I also feel this youth is unworthy of my Yue’er.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but chuckle. She shot Xuanyuan Mo Ze a glance, then looked at the Azure Emperor before concluding, \" Truthfully, across the entire realm, I haven’t seen many young men of Yue’er’s age who are truly outstanding. At least for now, Xiao Junyan stands out as an exceptional young man—besides my own two sons, that is. And considering how badly Yue’er was injured this time for his sake, I think if she feels inclined, we could arrange their betrothal now. They can wait a few more years before marrying.\"","With that, she smiled again. \"Of course, if Yue’er doesn’t fancy him or has no interest in him, that’s a different matter entirely. Everything should be based on her wishes.\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor pressed his lips together, saying nothing. He simply gazed at Yun Qi, who lay unconscious on the bed, lost in thought.","At that moment, Feng Jiu spoke again, \"Oh, Azure Emperor, there’s one more thing I need to discuss with you.\"","As she spoke, Feng Jiu rose, walked to the table, poured herself a cup of water, and took a sip before turning to the Azure Emperor. \"You know the extent of Yue’er’s injuries—damage to all five vital organs, severed tendons and meridians, and a crack in her dantian. For an ordinary person, such severe wounds would leave them crippled, if not dead. But since she is my daughter, Feng Jiu’s daughter, I will ensure she recovers fully. However...\"","She pressed her lips together in a faint smile, gazing at her daughter on the bed. \"This time, with her injuries being so severe, I intend to use this as a test for Xiao Junyan and the family behind him. Therefore, if they inquire, Azure Emperor, do not tell them her injuries are treatable or that she can recover.\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor’s eyes flickered slightly. He glanced at her and nodded. \"The Azure Emperor understands.\"","Two days later","At noon, the Azure Emperor entered Yun Qi’s room. Seeing she still hadn’t awakened, he sat down beside the bed.","Feng Jiu had said she should awaken today.","After keeping vigil for about half an hour, he noticed Yun Qi’s hand twitch slightly on the bed. Seeing this, he looked at her and called out, \"Little Qi?\"","In her deep slumber, Yue’er faintly seemed to hear her master’s voice calling her. With great effort, she lifted her heavy eyelids and saw her master sitting by the bedside."]},{"number":5236,"title":"Chapter 5236: Contemplation","paragraphs":["\"Master...\"","She called out, her voice weak and hoarse.","The Azure Emperor patted her hand, speaking gently, \"It’s all right now. I’m here.\"","\"Master, I’m thirsty. I want water.\" Her voice was raspy and dry, as if a fire burned within her.","\"Alright, just a moment.\" With a wave of his hand, the teapot and cup resting on the table flew over, landing steadily beside the bedside. After pouring a cup of water, he said, \"Here, Master will help you sit up.\"","He lifted her up, propping her against the pillows behind her to sit, then pulled the quilt up higher before offering her the water.","Yue’er tried to reach for it, only to find her arms too weak to even lift.","\"Your body is still weak. After lying in bed for over ten days, your strength won’t return immediately.\" With that, he brought the cup to her lips and helped her drink.","When Feng Jiu and Xuanyuan Mo Ze entered, they saw the Azure Emperor feeding Yue’er water. Xuanyuan Mo Ze didn’t think much of it, but Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. A fleeting, inexplicable light flashed in her eyes as she studied the Azure Emperor.","\"Father? Mother?\" Yue’er looked at them in surprise. \"How did you get here?\"","The two exchanged a smile, then approached the bedside. Xuanyuan Mo Ze explained, \"Your mother and I were traveling abroad when we sensed something had happened to you. We rushed back immediately.\"","Feng Jiu chuckled, \"If Mother hadn’t rushed back, do you think this little girl would have woken up at all?\"","Yue’er’s face lit up with a delighted smile. \"It’s so good to see Father and Mother~\"","\"Yue’er, you’re so grown up now. Why would you do something that worries your parents and your master like this? Do you realize how seriously injured you were this time?\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze, seeing the little girl still smiling, spoke sternly.","\"It’s Yue’er fault, sorry, I made you worry.\" Seeing her Father’s expression, she lowered her head in guilt.","\"Enough. She’s just woken up. Don’t scold her immediately,\" Feng Jiu interjected, retrieving a small vial from her cosmos sack. \"This is the Hundred Flowers Spiritual Honey that Mother concocted for you. Drink it—it will benefit you.\"","The Azure Emperor took the vial from Feng Jiu, then produced a spoon from his own cosmos sack. He scooped some of the honey onto the spoon before feeding it to Yue’er.","Feng Jiu watched from the side, casting an extra glance at the Azure Emperor but saying nothing.","Xuanyuan Mo Ze, however, noticed and stepped forward. \"Is Yue’er still too weak? Let me feed her!\"","\"No need. I can manage,\" the Azure Emperor replied, pouring another spoonful of the nectar.","\"Mother, this is so delicious!\"","Yue’er beamed, savoring the floral fragrance of the nectar. Its sweet, cool taste slid down her throat, soothing the fiery heat that had been burning there. A surge of spirit energy coursed through her body, leaving her enveloped in pure comfort.","Feng Jiu smiled and explained, \"This is a nectar distilled from a hundred blossoms. Knowing you dislike bitter medicines, I prepared this for you. You can consume it regularly—it benefits your health. I’ll share the recipe later so you may learn to craft it yourself when the time comes.\"","\"Thank you, Mother,\" Yue’er said with a beaming smile.","Seeing her spirits lift, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly, his expression softening.","Feng Jiu, watching from the side, took note of his expression and pondered silently..."]},{"number":5237,"title":"Chapter 5237: Intentions","paragraphs":["On the other side, the Immortal Island where the Patriarch Xiao resided.","\"Old Predecessor, I must go out. Yun Qi suffered severe injuries saving me. I cannot just ignore this.\" Xiao Junyan’s wounds had healed about seventy to eighty percent. Compared to Yun Qi’s shattered meridians and internal organ damage, his injuries were relatively minor.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian, hands clasped behind his back, observed him with a slight frown. After a moment of contemplation, he spoke: \"In that case, accompany me to Yunxiao Mountain.\"","At this, Xiao Junyan’s face lit up. \"Thank you, Old Predecessor! I’ll go gather some things and be right back.\" With that, he bowed and hurried away.","After he left, the Patriarch Xiao approached from nearby. Bowing to the Old Predecessor, he asked, \"Old Predecessor, are you truly taking Junyan to Yunxiao Mountain to see that Yun Qi?\"","\"After all, she took the blow for Junyan. We must pay her a visit, no matter what.\" He sighed, hands clasped behind his back. \"Bring the medicinal pills the Phoenix Empress gave us back then. We’ll send them to Yun Qi later.\"","\"Understood.\" The Patriarch Xiao responded, then paused before adding, \"Old Predecessor, Junyan seems to hold Yun Qi in rather high regard. I fear that if this continues...\"","He trailed off, then continued, \"Recently, I heard that the descendants of several other Great Emperors have formed alliances through marriage. Our Xiao family’s influence abroad has been gradually waning these past years. I worry that if this continues, it will be detrimental to our clan’s development.\"","Hearing this, Great Emperor Xiao Tian frowned thoughtfully. \"I still believe that a marriage alliance with the Phoenix Empress’s daughter would be the best choice for our Xiao family. If it succeeds, even the other Great Emperors would have to show us some respect.\"","\"But the Phoenix Empress and Hell’s Lord might not agree!\" The Patriarch Xiao said, feeling this match was unlikely.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian smiled. \"Consider this: if all the other great emperors’ non-heir heirs were married off, how many outstanding young talents would remain? And how many of those would be the focus of their families’ cultivation? Moreover, Junyan has shown exceptional promise since childhood. I believe the Xiao family will rise to new heights under his leadership. But securing a marriage with their daughter would be a tremendous boost.\"","He paused briefly before adding, \"As for Yun Qi, though she is the Azure Emperor’s disciple, I’ve heard that her injuries are so severe she’s essentially ruined. Even if healed, she’d remain crippled—her meridians severed, her dantian shattered, her internal organs damaged. Such catastrophic wounds are beyond medical repair. How could someone incapable of cultivation possibly be worthy of our Xiao family’s most exceptional son?\"","Hearing this, the Patriarch Xiao nodded, but added, \"But will Junyan agree?\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian stroked his beard, watching Xiao Junyan approach from a short distance away, saying nothing more.","Seeing this, the Patriarch Xiao said, \"Then I shall return immediately to fetch the medicinal pill and bring it over shortly.\" With that, he bowed and withdrew.","Xiao Junyan returned the bow to the Patriarch Xiao before stepping forward. \"Old Predecessor, we may depart now.\"","\"Wait a moment longer,\" the Emperor replied slowly. \"I’ve instructed him to retrieve the medicinal pills gifted by the Phoenix Empress years ago. We’ll deliver them together to that little Yun Qi girl.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan’s face lit up. \"Thank you, Old Predecessor.\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian watched him without speaking, merely stroking his beard, lost in thought.","Meanwhile, at the foot of Yunxiao Mountain.","Shen Shiqi and Chen Tao had been wandering around for a while but still hadn’t found the path up the mountain."]},{"number":5238,"title":"Chapter 5238: Visiting","paragraphs":["\"Yunxiao Mountain is really hard to find. We’ve been circling around for so long and still haven’t found the path.\" Zheng Yuan said, glancing around. From afar, it was just a sea of mist and overlapping mountain silhouettes. It seemed to be here, yet they couldn’t find the entrance.","\"Looks like we’ll have to ask the Azure Emperor to guide us. Otherwise, we could search for three days and nights and still not find it,\" Yang Hao remarked, gazing toward the mist ahead. He felt certain Yunxiao Mountain lay beyond, yet they remained unable to draw near.","Seeing this, Shen Shiqi stepped forward. \"I’ll handle it!\" he declared, raising his voice toward the mist-shrouded area. \"Azure Emperor! We are friends of Yun Qi. Concerned for her injuries, we have come to visit. Please grant us passage up the mountain!\"","His voice, infused with spirit energy, echoed through the clouds, reaching the ears of the Azure Emperor and the others atop the mountain.","\"It’s Shen Shiqi and the others,\" Yue’er smiled, clasping Mother’s hand. \"Mother, they’re my friends.\"","Feng Jiu smiled. \"It’s rare they’ve taken the trouble to see you. Since that’s the case, let them come up! My Father and I will step aside.\"","Though her words were directed at Yue’er, her gaze remained fixed on the Azure Emperor.","The Azure Emperor nodded in response, then waved his hand. To the group at the mountain’s base, he commanded, \"Come up!\"","The moment Shen Shiqi and the others at the foot of the mountain heard the voice, a mountain path materialized before them. Exchanging glances, they responded with a single word before swiftly ascending the slope.","Upon reaching the mountaintop, they found the Azure Emperor seated beneath a large tree, sipping tea and reading a book. Yun Qi lay on a soft couch, basking in the sunlight. After so many days apart, she appeared noticeably thinner. What pierced their hearts most was the complete absence of spirit energy within her...","\"Shen Shiqi.\"","\"Chen Tao.\"","\"Zheng Yuan.\"","\"Yang Hao.\"","\"Greets Azure Emperor.\"","As they stepped forward to state their names, they bowed respectfully to the Azure Emperor.","\"Mm.\" The Azure Emperor glanced at them indifferently, responding with a faint acknowledgment.","Yue’er, upon seeing them, smiled warmly, her eyes crinkling. Rising from the soft couch, she approached them. \"What brings you here?\"","\"We came to see you. We brought some medicinal pills and tonics to help you recuperate,\" Shen Shiqi said, retrieving the items from his spatial pouch.","\"We brought medicinal pills and tonics too,\" the other three chimed in, presenting their gifts to her.","Yue’er accepted them with a beaming smile. \"Thank you all.\"","\"How is your health? Are you feeling better? Can you manage getting out of bed and walking around like this?\" Zheng Yuan inquired.","\"My master gave me some medicinal pills, and I feel much better now. It’s alright to walk around. After I returned, my master said I had been in a deep sleep for over half a month and only woke up two days ago. I’ve been lying down most of the day lately. Today the sun is just right, so I came out to bask in it.\" She spoke cheerfully, gesturing to them, \"Come, sit down.\"","Seeing the Azure Emperor still present, the group felt somewhat constrained. However, noticing he was engrossed in his book and hadn’t glanced their way, they moved the stone stools beside the soft couch to keep Yun Qi company.","\"After your master took you away, Xiao Junyan was also brought back by his master’s family. By the way, has he come to see you?\" Shen Shiqi asked.","\"Not yet. I think Big Brother Xiao’s injuries might not have healed yet,\" Yue’er replied. After all, she had Mother’s medicinal pills, but Big Brother Xiao might not have had access to them."]},{"number":5239,"title":"Chapter 5239: Bearing Gifts","paragraphs":["Fearing they might touch upon her pain, they dared not ask whether she would never be able to cultivate again, doomed to remain an ordinary person. This time, among the medicines they brought, besides those for physical restoration, there were actually more substances designed to prolong life and extend longevity.","Perhaps these substances held little value for cultivators, but for those who could no longer practice cultivation, they were the very essentials for life.","\"By the way, a few days ago, more people from our families arrived. We all entered that secret realm again. This portion is what we saved for you.\" Shen Shiqi took out the items and handed them to her.","Yue’er looked slightly surprised. \"I have more?\" She recognized the herbs. Among the items given to her were three thousand-year-old spiritual herbs, several defensive treasures, and some precious trinkets.","\"Naturally, your share won’t be less than ours. We prepared these based on your current needs. Compared to ours, they might be...\" Zheng Yuan trailed off, watching her silently.","These items represent our heartfelt intentions, tailored to her current physical condition. Compared to their haul, hers is considerably smaller.","Yue’er’s eyes crinkled with delight. \"Thank you both, but please take these back! I have no use for them. Besides, I didn’t contribute much effort—it feels awkward to accept such gifts.\"","Though their time together had been brief, their thoughtfulness deeply moved her. Besides, these items truly served no purpose for her. No matter how precious the spiritual herbs or medicinal pills, Mother would always provide them.","\"We’ve already brought these things—how could we possibly take them back?\" Chen Tao said, looking at Yun Qi. \"Take these. These three thousand-year-old spiritual herbs are excellent. In the future, see if your master can find someone to refine them into medicinal pills for you. They’ll be beneficial for your health.\"","Although Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu had stepped aside, they hadn’t gone far. They’d been watching from a short distance since Shen Shiqi and the others arrived. Seeing this scene now, Feng Jiu smiled and nodded.","\"Yue’er has made some friends with admirable character.\" True friends reveal themselves in adversity. These young people were likely Young Masters of top-tier clans, yet their thoughtful gifts and visit at this time spoke volumes of their sincerity.","\"Indeed.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze agreed, his gaze sweeping over them as he quietly assessed each.","Overwhelmed by their warmth, Yue’er finally accepted their gifts, smiling brightly as she said, \"Thank you all so much.\"","Shen Shiqi and the others laughed heartily. \"We’re friends—no need for formalities. If you ever need anything, just let us know.\"","With that, he produced a token and handed it to her. \"This is my Shen family’s token. Keep it. If anyone causes trouble for you in the future, just show this.\"","Chen Tao chuckled at the scene, nudging Shen Shiqi with his elbow. \"What are you messing around with? Your Shen family’s token isn’t nearly as useful as Yun Qi’s reputation!\"","Shen Shiqi paused at this, then laughed. \"My mistake. But you should still keep it! If it’s inconvenient to use your master’s name in the future, you can always use my token instead.\""]},{"number":5240,"title":"Chapter 5240: Avoid","paragraphs":["\"Alright.\" Yue’er accepted it with a smile and tucked the token away.","Shen Shiqi glanced around in confusion, feeling as though someone was watching them from the shadows. But when he looked around, besides their group and the Azure Emperor, he saw no one else and detected no other presence.","Was it just his imagination?","After chatting with her for a while, they rose to take their leave. \"We still need to return to the main house. Seeing you in such good spirits now puts our minds at ease. Next time we have the chance, we’ll come visit you again. Or perhaps you could come visit us at the main house instead. When you do, we’ll definitely show you around properly.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er beamed and nodded. \"Alright! Once I’m feeling better, I’ll come find you all to play.\"","Hearing her words, the group exchanged smiles. This little girl was still just a child—not worried about her health, but already thinking about fun.","So they laughed in response, \"Great! We’ll be waiting for you.\"","After bidding farewell to Yun Qi, they went to the Azure Emperor, bowed to him in farewell, and then began their descent down the mountain.","\"Let me walk you down,\" Yue’er called out, wanting to accompany them all the way down the mountain.","\"No need to see us off. We’re just a few steps down. You’re still recovering; get some rest.\" \" Signaling she needn’t accompany them further, the group gathered their energy and sped down the mountain.","At the foot of the mountain, Shen Shiqi turned to look at Yunxiao Mountain, shrouded in mist and clouds. He said to his friends, \"I can’t shake the feeling that someone was watching us from the shadows back there.\"","\"You felt it too?\" Chen Tao looked at Shen Shiqi in surprise, then mused, \"Seems it wasn’t just my imagination! But who could it be?\"","\"Could it be one of the Azure Emperor’s friends?\" Zheng Yuan suggested.","\"Perhaps it was the Azure Emperor’s friend. Otherwise, we wouldn’t have sensed their presence,\" Yang Hao added.","\"Let’s go! Regardless, we saw that little girl today. She seemed to be in good spirits,\" Shen Shiqi said, chatting with them as they walked.","\"It’s just a pity,\" Zheng Yuan sighed softly, his voice heavy with regret. \"Even if she recovers her health, she’ll never be able to cultivate again.\"","As the group walked further away, their voices gradually faded...","Up on the mountain, Feng Jiu was examining the gifts Shen Shiqi and the others had brought for Yue’er. \"These friends of yours are quite decent,\" she remarked. \"Worth keeping. These presents show they put real thought into them.\"","Yue’er smiled brightly. \"They really are wonderful. The only thing that happened on this trip down the mountain was meeting them. Actually, I knew them when I was very young, though I used to tease them back then.\"","As the group chatted on the mountain, about half an hour passed before the voice of Great Emperor Xiao Tian echoed through the air.","\"Azure Emperor, I have brought Junyan to visit Yun Qi. Might we be granted an audience?\"","Hearing the voice, the Azure Emperor glanced at Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu.","\"You two go ahead. We’ll head back to rest,\" Feng Jiu said, making no attempt to stay. After all, with the power of the Great Emperor Xiao Tian, he might sense their presence, so it was best to avoid him altogether.","Only after watching them depart did the Azure Emperor open the mountain gates, allowing them to ascend.","Truth be told, since his most cherished disciple had suffered severe injuries because of Xiao Junyan, he harbored little fondness for the Xiao family. Yet he understood that Yun Qi likely wished to see Xiao Junyan at this moment."]},{"number":5241,"title":"Chapter 5241: Medicinal Pill","paragraphs":["As the mountain gates swung open, the two of them ascended from below. Upon reaching the summit and seeing Yun Qi standing beside the Azure Emperor, Xiao Junyan strode forward, his concern evident as he asked, \"Little Qi, how are you? Has your health improved?\"","Unlike Xiao Junyan, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian first greeted the Azure Emperor before discreetly appraising the young girl. As his divine sense swept over her body, revealing her shattered meridians and fractured dantian, his gaze flickered.","It seemed this girl was truly ruined. What a pity.","\"Yun Qi,\" the Great Emperor Xiao Tian called out.","\"Yun Qi greets the Emperor,\" she replied, stepping forward to bow, her voice clear and crisp.","At that moment, Xiao Junyan also bowed to the Azure Emperor, his voice tinged with guilt. \"I failed to protect her properly, allowing her to suffer such severe injuries.\"","The Azure Emperor shot him a cold glance. \"That girl Yun Qi has always been willful. It’s only fitting she taste the bitter consequences. Only then will she learn not everything can be shielded for others.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Junyan pressed his lips together, saying nothing.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian, seeing this, spoke up, \"Azure Emperor, I know this time Yun took the punishment for Junyan. That’s why, as soon as Junyan’s injuries stabilized, I brought him here to see to Yun.\"","He then produced a medicinal pill and handed it to Yun Qi, saying, \"Little Yun, this is a healing pill gifted by the Phoenix Empress years ago—a supreme treasure. Though it cannot mend your severed tendons or ruptured dantian, it will at least treat your internal injuries. Take it. I shall seek out better medicinal pills for you in the future.\"","Seeing the medicinal pills offered, Yue’er froze, blinking in confusion.","He was giving her medicinal pills sent by her Mother? Should she accept them? Or refuse?","Unconsciously, she looked to her master.","\"Since they’re from Great Emperor Xiao Tian to heal you, you should accept them,\" Azure Emperor said indifferently.","\"Oh.\" She responded, took the pills, and bowed to him. \"Thank you, Great Emperor.\"","\"Little Qi, I need to speak with you,\" Xiao Junyan said, his gaze fixed on her.","Seeing this, Yue’er thought for a moment before saying to her master, \"Master, I’ll take Big Brother Xiao for a walk.\"","The Azure Emperor shot Xiao Junyan a glance before instructing Yun Qi, \"Go ahead! But don’t linger too long. Your body isn’t fully recovered yet; you must return to rest.\"","\"Understood.\" Yue’er acknowledged, bowing to both of them before departing with Xiao Junyan to explore elsewhere.","Yue’er led him to her cave abode and explained, \"Big Brother Xiao, this is my cave abode. Those two over there belong to my two Senior Brothers, but they’re not on the mountain right now.\"","Instead of entering the caves, they sat down at a table outside.","\"Little Qi, how are your injuries? Did the Azure Emperor find a healer to treat you?\" Xiao Junyan inquired, his heart twinging at the sight of her noticeably thinner frame.","\"Master says with gradual recuperation, my body will heal,\" she replied with a bright smile. In truth, these were Mother’s words. Mother had explained that because her injuries were severe, treatment must proceed step by step: first healing the critically damaged internal organs, then repairing the shattered meridians, and finally addressing the cracked dantian.","But Mother had forbidden her from telling anyone else—not even Big Brother Xiao.","Seeing the smile on her face, Xiao Junyan sensed it was forced. When they had met earlier, he had detected not a trace of spirit energy about her. She seemed as ordinary as any mortal, even weaker than most."]},{"number":5242,"title":"Chapter 5242: Confession","paragraphs":["\"I’m sorry. It’s all my fault. I failed to protect you and instead caused you such severe injury.\" Xiao Junyan spoke with deep remorse. He reached out and took her hand, saying, \"Little Qi, let me take care of you from now on!\"","Yue’er froze upon hearing this, blinking at him in surprise. \"Huh? What?\" She felt a bit dazed. Had she heard correctly?","\"I said, I want to take care of you for the rest of your life.\" Holding her hand, he spoke with solemn earnestness. \"Rest assured, I will seek an audience with the Phoenix Empress. I’ve heard her medical skills and alchemy are unmatched in this world. I believe she must have a way to heal your injuries. You will definitely be able to cultivate again.\"","As he spoke, he produced some medicinal pills. \"Take these. They’re all healing elixirs.\"","Yue’er listened to his words, paused for a moment, then looked at him deeply. \"Big Brother Xiao, if you’re blaming yourself, there’s no need. Even if I can’t cultivate anymore, my master will protect me.\"","\"No, Little Qi. I’ve wanted to tell you for a long time—I like you. I want to take care of you for the rest of my life.\" His expression was earnest as he spoke.","Yue’er froze, thinking to herself: So... he just confessed to me?","For a moment, looking at Xiao Junyan before her, she felt at a loss. Ever since they’d set out on this journey, she’d sensed something different in his attitude toward her compared to when they were children. Sometimes his gaze felt peculiar. Last time, he’d only spoken halfway through his thoughts, but she’d managed to piece together some of what he meant.","Now, with her current state—anyone could see she’d lost her ability to cultivate—yet he still declared his affection and desire to care for her. It was undeniable that his words made her heart skip a beat.","All she knew was that being confessed to felt strangely wonderful.","So, for the next while, he spoke while she drifted off in thought, so much so that she didn’t really catch what he was saying.","\"Little Qi?\"","Seeing her remain silent, seemingly lost in thought, Xiao Junyan paused and called out.","\"Huh? What is it?\" She snapped back to reality and looked at him questioningly.","Xiao Junyan paused, pursed his lips, shook his head helplessly, and finally asked again, \"I said, where is your family? If I want to propose marriage, I’ll need to speak with your parents, won’t I?\"","\"Huh?\" Yue’er froze for a moment. \"Well... Big Brother Xiao, please let me think it over.\"","She paused again, glancing at him before whispering, \"Besides, you said you like me, but I can’t cultivate now. I’m just like an ordinary person. You’re the heir to your family—how could your family ever agree to let you marry me?\"","\"Don’t worry about that. I’ll convince them.\" He held her hand. \"Focus on healing your wounds first. I’ll seek out the Phoenix Empress and ask her to treat your injuries.\"","Yue’er opened her mouth several times but ultimately said nothing. She only murmured, \"Truthfully, I don’t want to marry so soon. I’m still so young!\" More importantly, she hadn’t figured out her own feelings toward him.","She only knew she didn’t dislike him. In fact, seeing him get hurt time and again for her sake stirred an inexpressible emotion within her. As for anything else... she simply couldn’t understand it.","Xiao Junyan was about to speak further when the voice of his family’s Old Predecessor reached them.","\"Junyan, it’s time for us to go.\"","Seeing this, Xiao Junyan could only say, \"I’ll come see you again in a while.\""]},{"number":5243,"title":"Chapter 5243: Naive","paragraphs":["Yue’er nodded and accompanied him to where her master and the Great Emperor Xiao Tian were. After watching them depart, she fell into deep thought, lost in her own musings.","\"What are you thinking about?\"","Perhaps noticing her furrowed brow and pensive expression, the Azure Emperor inquired.","\"Master, Big Brother Xiao told me he likes me,\" Yue’er said, lifting her gaze to meet his.","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor paused briefly before asking, \"And you? Do you care for him?\"","Yue’er frowned, pondering for a moment before replying, \"I don’t know. But I don’t dislike him.\"","The Azure Emperor folded his arms behind his back, gazing elsewhere. \"In my view, Xiao Junyan is not worthy of you. But if you like him, I won’t stand in your way. All you need to do is follow your heart.\"","With that, he turned and walked away, his faint voice carried on the wind: \"Go back and rest.\"","Hearing his words, Yue’er stood still, pondering her master’s advice to follow her heart. In the end, she returned to her cave abode first and sent a message to her Mother, wanting to ask her what she should do.","In Yue’er’s cave abode, Feng Jiu smiled after hearing her words. Looking at her confused daughter, she asked, \"Then tell Mother—why did you shield him from that attack back then?\"","Yue’er shook her head. \"I don’t know. At that moment, I only thought I couldn’t let him die because of me.\"","\"Then how do you plan to respond now that he’s confessed his feelings?\" Feng Jiu propped her chin in her hand, amused by her daughter’s furrowed brow.","That once-tiny little girl had grown into such a young woman now, and someone had even confessed to her. Watching this unfold as her Mother, Feng Jiu felt a flood of emotions.","\"I don’t know how to describe it. When I saw him getting hurt over and over for me in that secret realm, my heart was moved. Especially knowing he liked me all along, just hadn’t said it yet, silently protecting me all this time.\" She spoke with a hint of conflict.","Feng Jiu smiled. \"Girls sometimes easily confuse being touched with being moved.\"","She paused, then offered a mysterious smile. \"Since Xiao Junyan says he likes you, well... Mother will test just how much he truly cares. And see how far he’s willing to go for you.\"","Yue’er blinked, her eyes brimming with curiosity. \"What does Mother plan to do?\"","\"No rush. You’ll find out soon enough.\" She chuckled softly, gently tickling her nose. \"Here’s the plan: focus on healing first. Your master’s place seems rather lonely, so stay here and keep him company. Your Father and I will head back first. Once we’ve handled this matter, we’ll come back for you.\"","\"Alright.\" Yue’er nodded. She had wanted to go back with them, but the thought of leaving her master alone on the mountain made her heart ache.","\"Take these medicinal pills. Take one each day. You can’t practice cultivation now, so use your free time to practice calligraphy and read books.\" Feng Jiu instructed, leaving her some restorative pills.","\"Mm hmm, Mother, don’t worry. I know!\" She nodded with a bright smile, then asked, \"Mother, when will you and Father return? And when will you come back for me? When that time comes, can I bring Master to live on the island with us?\"","Feng Jiu smiled, pinching her cheek gently. \"We’ll let you know when the time comes. As for your Master, if he’s willing, he’s more than welcome to join us anytime.\"","\"Mother, you’re the best!\" Yue’er slipped her arms around her waist, burrowing into her embrace with a beaming smile."]},{"number":5244,"title":"Chapter 5244: Arrive","paragraphs":["The next day, Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu bid farewell to the Azure Emperor and returned to the island ahead of him. The daughter they had intended to take back for recuperation remained behind.","After her parents departed, Yue’er stayed by her master’s side. While her master read, she practiced calligraphy nearby. Unable to cultivate due to her unhealed injuries, she spent her idle days in the kitchen, concocting dishes to bring her master for tasting.","Days slipped by unnoticed.","One month later.","Meanwhile, at the Immortal Island where Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu resided, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian had arrived.","\"Hahahaha! Upon hearing of your return from wandering the clouds, I sent my calling card to pay my respects. Truly, years have flown by in the blink of an eye! Hell’s Lord and Phoenix Empress, you both remain as radiant as ever!\" Great Emperor Xiao Tian bowed respectfully as he stepped inside.","Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu rose to greet him, smiling. \"Master Xiao, it’s been years! How have you been? Please, take the seat of honor.\" They gestured invitingly.","\"Let’s sit together.\"","Seeing how much warmer their welcome was this time, Great Emperor Xiao Tian couldn’t help but smile, his eyes crinkling. After taking a seat beside them, he remarked, \"Among all the great emperors, only the two of you truly live in carefree bliss. Look at me—stuck on this island year-round, bogged down with trivial matters. Ah, I’m truly no match for you both!\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu exchanged a glance. They chatted with him about trivial matters for a while before he cut straight to the point.","\"Hell’s Lord, your daughter should be around fourteen or fifteen this year, right?\" Great Emperor Xiao Tian looked at Xuanyuan Mo Ze and asked.","\"Yes, she is.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze nodded briefly, his response terse.","\"Heh. Well, as I mentioned to you both years ago, there’s a young talent in our clan named Junyan. These past years, he hasn’t disappointed us. In every respect, he’s exceptionally outstanding. Even among the offspring of other Great Emperor families, few can compare to him.\" He stroked his beard as he spoke, his eyes and brows radiating pride.","\"We’ve all met Xiao Junyan before. He truly is an exceptional young talent. That Old Xiao could nurture him to such excellence shows he’s put considerable effort into his upbringing,\" Feng Jiu nodded with a smile.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian chuckled. \"Given that this child lost his parents early and is the next heir of the family, it was only right to invest extra effort in his cultivation. Fortunately, he hasn’t wasted all the dedication I’ve poured into him over the years.\"","His voice paused as he glanced at the two of them. \"Truthfully, the reason for my visit today is to revisit the matter of the marriage alliance from years past. I wonder what your thoughts are on the matter?\"","Hearing this, Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu exchanged glances. Feng Jiu then looked at him and said slowly, \"Elder Xiao, I actually think highly of Junyan too. However, my husband and I agreed long ago that everything should be based on our daughter’s own wishes.\"","She paused before continuing, \"If you truly wish to pursue this match, let’s set aside other considerations for now. Allow them time to get to know each other first. Should both parties feel it is right, then we can proceed to formalize the engagement. What do you think?\"","Hearing this, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian’s face lit up with delight. He exclaimed repeatedly, \"That’s an excellent idea! Excellent indeed!\" Their willingness to budge meant the match was already half secured, and naturally, he was overjoyed.","\"However,\" Feng Jiu said, turning to face him, \"there is one more matter I must clarify beforehand.\""]},{"number":5245,"title":"Chapter 5245: Digging a Pit","paragraphs":["\"What is it? Speak.\" The Great Emperor Xiao Tian looked at her, thinking that whatever it was, he must agree before the marriage was finalized.","Feng Jiu gazed at him, her expression earnest and solemn. \"I will not tolerate my daughter’s husband having any involvement or entanglement with other women. Elder Xiao, do you understand my meaning?\"","Hearing this, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian paused, then replied, \"Rest assured. Junyan, that child, due to the early passing of his parents, has been cold-hearted since childhood. He has never had any women around him. You can be certain of that.\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze sipped his tea, saying nothing. Feng Jiu, however, spoke up: \" But I recall, at a banquet several years ago, his treatment of Azure Emperor’s disciple, Yun Qi, seemed somewhat different.\"","\"Hehe, truthfully, he only regarded her as a younger sister. Back then, Azure Emperor’s disciple, Yun Qi, arrived on our island by accident and stayed with us for a time. Junyan consistently looked after her. But Phoenix Empress, you can rest assured, there was nothing between them.\" Great Emperor Xiao Tian hastily assured her.","Feng Jiu glanced at him, her expression softening into a meaningful smile. \"Very well then.\"","Great Emperor Xiao Tian watched her, sensing an unspoken meaning behind her words. He resolved that upon returning, he must immediately sever the connection between Junyan and Yun Qi. He couldn’t risk them developing anything that might ruin this perfectly arranged marriage.","After exchanging a few more casual words and finalizing the arrangements, Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu personally saw him off. They set a date for Xiao Junyan to come stay on the Immortal Island for a while.","Watching him depart, Xuanyuan Mo Ze turned to Feng Jiu and asked, \"What if Xiao Junyan refuses this match?\"","Feng Jiu smiled. Instead of returning to the palace with him, they strolled along the Rainbow Bridge. \"Knowing Xiao Junyan’s character,\" she said, \"I suspect he’ll refuse the moment his father mentions it. But refusal is one thing—what I want to see is whether he’ll choose his heart’s desire over his family elders and the clan’s future prospects. Will he stand firm for love, or yield to reality?\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze shook his head, smiling helplessly. \"You’ve dug such a deep pit for him. Looks like I won’t need to intervene after all.\"","Feng Jiu chuckled softly. \"Marrying our daughter isn’t so simple. If he can’t pass the test, how could we entrust our precious daughter to him? Besides, if he can’t even pass this test, what if he faces similar dilemmas later? Wouldn’t he abandon our daughter anytime, using some so-called ’greater good’ as an excuse?\"","\"This Xiao Junyan may be outstanding,\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze said, \"but I still feel he’s not worthy of our Yue’er.\" He believed his daughter deserved better.","\"Hmm, if we’re talking about excellence, he actually can’t compare to our two sons.\"","Feng Jiu chuckled lightly and said, \"Look at Hao’er. He’s been out on his own for several years. Not only has he spread the fame of being the Azure Emperor’s top disciple, but behind the scenes, he’s also built a powerful underground force of his own. On the other hand, according to our investigations, everything Xiao Junyan has now is provided by his family. He has no forces of his own to command. Should any real crisis arise, he can only rely on his own abilities and the backing of the Xiao family.\"","\"If you’re not entirely satisfied with him, why set him up for such a massive fall?\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze asked, slightly surprised."]},{"number":5246,"title":"Chapter 5246: Refusal","paragraphs":["\"Our precious daughter can’t tell whether she’s moved or captivated by Xiao Junyan. So I’m just giving her a little push,\" Feng Jiu said with a light chuckle. \"Whatever the outcome, it can’t do any harm.\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze listened, then looked ahead and said, \"But speaking of which, in this world today, men of Yue’er’s age who are truly outstanding are indeed few and far between. I truly wonder what sort of man she will end up with in the future?\"","Hearing these words, Feng Jiu’s eyes flickered slightly, and she couldn’t help but think of the Azure Emperor. Perhaps it was a woman’s intuition. On this trip to Yunxiao Mountain, she felt that the Azure Emperor’s affection for Yue’er was no less than that of her own parents.","His kindness, his indulgence, his pampering, his affection—all flowed from him so naturally, as if there were nothing wrong with it, as if it were the most natural thing in the world.","If he harbored any special feelings for Yue’er, she hadn’t seen it. At least, in his eyes, there was no trace of romantic love, only that tender, gentle affection.","As parents, they treated Yue’er like a precious jewel in their hands. Yet in the Azure Emperor’s gaze, she sensed he cherished her as the apple of his eye.","\"By the way, what do you think of how the Azure Emperor treats Yue’er?\" Feng Jiu looked at him and asked.","\"The Azure Emperor?\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze raised an eyebrow slightly, somewhat surprised she would ask this question. However, after a moment’s thought, he replied, \"The Azure Emperor treats Yue’er exceptionally well. He dotes on her immensely.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at her and asked, \"Why do you ask?\"","Feng Jiu shook her head. \"No reason. I just feel that the Azure Emperor truly treats Yue’er very well. His kindness toward her is no less than what we, her parents, show her.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Xuanyuan Mo Ze nodded thoughtfully. After a moment, he added, \"Perhaps Yue’er isn’t just his current apprentice—she might also be his original disciple. Since Yun Qi from back then is no longer here, he’s poured all that affection and doting into Yue’er instead.\"","Over the years, they had pieced together bits of information about the Azure Emperor’s disciple, Yun Qi, from long ago. Mo Ze’s explanation made sense.","Hand in hand, they descended the Rainbow Bridge and strolled toward the palace, waiting for the next teleportation message...","Meanwhile, on the Xiao family’s island.","\"I refuse!\" Xiao Junyan rejected outright upon hearing the words of the Old Predecessor and the Patriarch Xiao.","\"The one I wish to marry is Yun Qi, not Xuanyuan Muyue—the daughter of the Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress!\" He stared at the two seated at the head of the table. The shock of the news caused his chest to rise and fall slightly, his fists clenched tightly beneath his sleeves.","\"My marriage is my decision! I will only marry the woman I choose!\" he declared, enunciating each word with unwavering resolve as his gaze locked onto the two figures.","\"Insolence!\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian roared, his overwhelming aura crashing down, forcing Xiao Junyan to his knees.","The Patriarch Xiao, watching from the side, couldn’t help but feel concern. Yet, seeing the Old Predecessor’s furious rage, he dared not speak to dissuade him. He only said to Xiao Junyan, \"Junyan, we all have your best interests at heart. A match like this is something many would long for but never achieve.\"","Xiao Junyan pressed his lips tightly together, not uttering a single word, remaining kneeling on the ground.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian fixed his gaze upon him and declared, \"This is no longer a matter of your consent. Do you understand? This marriage no longer concerns merely your personal happiness. It concerns the very prosperity or ruin of our entire Xiao family!\""]},{"number":5247,"title":"Chapter 5247: Responsibility","paragraphs":["Junyan’s eyes narrowed as he stared at him in disbelief.","\"You haven’t taken charge of the Xiao family affairs yet, so you don’t know how the family has been declining year after year. Especially after the descendants of the other great emperors intermarried, the blow to us has been even greater. The most fatal blow is that recently, a mysterious force has emerged, suppressing our Xiao family’s external businesses. If this continues, you should be able to imagine what the future holds for the Xiao family.\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian spoke with deep gravity, his gaze fixed on him. \"You are not alone. As the young master of the Xiao family, you bear responsibilities that cannot be shirked.\"","That day, in the grand hall of the Xiao family, Xiao Junyan knelt for a long time, receiving a stern reprimand. Beyond the Patriarch Xiao and the Great Emperor Xiao Tian, no one knew what transpired between the three inside. Only when Xiao Junyan emerged did they see him looking utterly lost and disoriented...","Meanwhile, Yue’er, residing in Yunxiao Mountain, remained unaware of these events.","She was currently perched on the edge of the table, watching the expressionless Azure Emperor eat. With a smile, she asked, \"Master, how is it? Is it tasty?\"","Azure Emperor set down his spoon, glancing at her. \"Didn’t you taste it first?\"","\"No, I brought it over right after I finished making it. But I figured it couldn’t be too bad, right?\" She stared at the bowl before her master—more than half of it gone. Could it really be bad? Unlikely.","Azure Emperor wiped the corner of his mouth. \"Next time, taste it yourself first. Make sure it’s good before bringing it to me.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er beamed. \"Master, we’re bored here. Why don’t we go visit my parents? At least Sister Mi’er is there. Her cooking is delicious. I haven’t had it in years.\"","\"If you wish to go, have them come fetch you,\" the Azure Emperor said indifferently, taking out a book to leaf through.","\"If I leave, Master will be all alone here,\" Yue’er sighed softly, resting her hand on her cheek as she gazed at him.","The Azure Emperor lifted his gaze to meet hers, his eyes settling on hers as if trying to peer through them into her very soul. Lost in thought, he remained silent for a long moment.","\"Master?\"","\"I’m accustomed to being alone,\" he said, his eyes drifting back to the book he’d casually opened.","Yue’er fidgeted with her hair, twisting strands between her fingers, lightly brushing her nose with the ends, or occasionally nibbling on a lock. Suddenly, as if struck by a thought, she pulled out two emerald-green beads.","\"Master, did you give me these?\" she asked, looking up at him.","The Azure Emperor glanced at Yue’er and replied indifferently, \"Mhm.\"","Yue’er’s eyes lit up. \"So it really was you who saved me back then? I thought I’d just dreamed about you!\" She laughed, her face radiant with joy and curiosity. \"But Master, weren’t you on the mountain? How did you end up in the secret realm? And how did you know I was in danger?\"","Perhaps finding her questions excessive, the Azure Emperor looked at her and asked, \"Have you finished your calligraphy practice for today?\"","\"Huh?\" Yue’er froze, wondering why he’d suddenly changed the subject. Still, she obediently shook her head. \"No, I haven’t written it yet!\"","\"Then go write it. Don’t disturb your master while I’m reading.\" The Azure Emperor said indifferently, his voice neither loud nor soft."]},{"number":5248,"title":"Chapter 5248: Inquiry","paragraphs":["His face bore not a trace of emotion, even carrying a hint of sternness. This made Yue’er, who had been about to ask a question, awkwardly stop herself. She obediently cleared the bowls from the table and then fetched ink, brush, and paper to practice calligraphy at the desk.","That day, after finishing her calligraphy practice, Yue’er approached her master again. Seeing he held no book, she intended to chat with him for a while. Instead, he retrieved a zither from his cosmos sack, placed it before him, and began plucking its strings lightly.","The tinkling notes rang out, crisp as pearls falling onto a jade plate. His slender fingers danced lightly across the strings, a mesmerizing sight.","She was somewhat surprised, for it was rare to see her master play the zither. And to play it so beautifully.","So she sat quietly beside him, watching him play. As she listened, she found herself closing her eyes. With her eyes shut, she could feel the beauty and depth of her master’s music even more profoundly.","Azure Emperor glanced at her, watching her there with her eyes closed, her head bobbing slightly, a look of pure rapture on her face.","He shifted his gaze to the white clouds ahead, yet his fingers never paused. As his slender fingers plucked the strings, the elegant, melodious notes echoed throughout Yunxiao Mountain...","Perched on a nearby hilltop, the Azure Emperor’s Sacred Beast narrowed its eyes, watching the two below. How familiar this scene felt...","Back in the day, it had witnessed such scenes often. Yet, everything had ceased after Yun Qi’s demise that year. Never did it expect to see it again today.","As the sun sank below the western mountains, the zither’s melody ceased. Yun Qi, who had drifted off unnoticed, seemed to have experienced a fragmented dream. In that dream, there appeared to be a girl named Yun Qi. In that dream, there seemed to be a scene just like this one...","\"If you’re tired, go rest.\" The Azure Emperor stood up, the qin already tucked away.","Yun Qi rubbed her eyes, yawned, and called out, \"Master, I had no idea you played the qin so beautifully. I fell asleep listening to you.\" A smile spread across her face as she added, \"It was so lovely I drifted off.\"","\"Master, may I ask you something?\" \" Yue’er looked at him and asked.","\"What is it?\" The Azure Emperor inquired.","\"Master, why did you name me Yun Qi? Everyone says your first disciple was named Yun Qi, but I also heard Mother say you said I was the reincarnation of your disciple Yun Qi. But I am me, and Yun Qi is Yun Qi. Did you mistake us for the same person?\" she asked curiously.","The Azure Emperor stood with his hands behind his back, his deep gaze fixed on her face. His low voice was slow and measured as he replied, \"You are indeed the same person.\" With those words, he offered no further explanation and simply turned to leave.","Yue’er stood there, stunned for a moment. She murmured softly, \"The same person? \" A scene, half-dreamlike, half-real, seemed to replay in her mind. She shook her head, watching her master’s departing figure. In the end, she said nothing and walked back to the cave abode.","That night, she lay down and fell asleep not long after. Perhaps she was truly tired, or perhaps she had simply relaxed. However, after she fell asleep, she dreamt all night long.","\"Ah! Master!\"","She cried out in alarm, rolling over and leaping to her feet. Cold sweat beaded on her forehead, her face pale, fear still lingering in her eyes.","\"What’s wrong?\"","Perhaps drawn by her cry, the Azure Emperor arrived at her cave abode. Seeing her still behind the gauze curtains on the bed, he halted in his tracks."]},{"number":5249,"title":"Chapter 5249: Habit","paragraphs":["\"Master?\" Yue’er heard the voice and thought it was her imagination. Turning her head, she saw her master standing not far away, hands clasped behind his back.","She quickly pulled on her outer robe, her hair still disheveled as she got out of bed. Approaching him, she said pitifully, \"Master, I had a nightmare. I dreamed I died.\"","The person in the dream seemed like her, yet not quite her. She had perished beneath lightning tribulation. She thought she saw her master sitting there, holding her charred corpse. In the entire Yunxiao Mountain, there was only her master and that scorched body...","Hearing her words, the Azure Emperor’s gaze flickered slightly. Watching her approach him, he reached out and patted her head, his voice carrying a touch more gentleness than usual: \"Don’t worry. It was only a dream.\"","\"Master, what if I really die?\" She bit her lip but persisted.","\"With your master here, I will protect you.\" With that, he withdrew his hand and looked at her, her face pale and clearly not well-rested. \"The sky hasn’t brightened yet. Go back to sleep for a while! Your master will stay here and watch over you.\"","As he spoke, he walked to the table in the outer room and sat down. He took out his qin and placed it on the table. His fingers gently plucked the strings, and a soothing, tranquil melody flowed softly from his hands.","Yue’er hadn’t slept deeply all night. Seeing he hadn’t left, she returned to bed. Watching her master seated there playing the zither, her worries gradually eased. Listening to the gentle, soothing melody, she slowly closed her eyes...","Azure Emperor sat plucking the strings until he sensed she had fallen asleep. Only then did he stop. He then took out a book and sat reading, quietly keeping watch.","It was nearly noon when Yue’er finally awoke. Opening her eyes to find her master still seated there, she paused in surprise: \"Master?\"","Azure Emperor closed the book, stood up, and said, \"Now that you’re awake, let’s go for a walk and soak up some sun.\" With that, he walked away, hands behind his back.","Yue’er smiled brightly in response. \"Alright.\" Watching her master depart, she quickly got out of bed to wash and dress.","\"Master, we haven’t been down the mountain in ages. Shall we go explore the city?\" Yue’er asked as she approached him.","\"Your meridians remain unrepaired, and you’ve lost all your spirit energy. It’s not advisable for you to venture out,\" the Azure Emperor replied calmly.","\"Master, don’t you ever get bored staying up here all the time?\" she asked curiously.","\"I’m used to it,\" the Azure Emperor replied, pulling out a chessboard. \"Since you’re bored, sit down and play a few games with me.\"","\"Master, I’ll lose terribly at chess.\" she protested, yet sat down anyway. \"If it were Senior Brother, he might stand a chance against you. But me? I know I’ll lose before the game even starts—and lose badly.\"","Of the three siblings, her chess skills were the weakest. Her Big Brother was the strongest player. He occasionally played against the Master and even managed draws sometimes, proving his considerable skill.","When she mentioned Yun Chen, the Azure Emperor placed a stone and remarked, \"His chess skills were taught by your father. You can see a hint of your father’s style in his play. I believe that in a few more years, when he plays against me again, he will surely surpass me.\"","\"Hehe, Senior Brother Yun has always been formidable. His reputation has grown quite renowned during his years away,\" Yue’er said with a smile, tinged with a hint of regret. \"I had hoped to make a name for myself on this journey down the mountain, but I never imagined I’d end up in such a sorry state.\""]},{"number":5250,"title":"Chapter 5250: Meeting Again","paragraphs":["Yue’er spoke while holding a chess piece against her chin, pondering for ages without deciding where to place it. Her eyes darted around, and she turned to him with a smile, asking, \"Master, where do you think I should put this piece?\"","The Azure Emperor’s mouth twitched slightly. He glanced at her and said, \"Figure it out yourself.\"","\"But I can’t figure it out! You know my chess skills aren’t great. If you don’t tell me, I’ll lose within three moves. So you really have to teach me!\" She chattered cheerfully, completely oblivious to her own thick-skinned persistence.","The Azure Emperor seemed somewhat exasperated by her words, reaching out to point at the board.","\"Thud!\"","Yue’er placed the piece with a sharp thud exactly where her master had indicated. Her eyes lit up instantly. \"Master, you’re amazing! Placing it here turns my dead-end position into a viable one!\"","Azure Emperor picked up another piece and set it down. Sure enough, after Yue’er made a few moves, she turned to him again, asking where she should go next.","By the end of the game, Yue’er had managed to draw with him. Her eyes crinkled with delight. \"Master, I actually drew with you!\"","Azure Emperor glanced at her without comment, then swept his hand across the board, scattering the pieces. \"Reconstruct this game. If you make a single wrong move, you’ll weed the medicinal fields on the back mountain.\"","\"Huh?\"","Yue’er gasped softly, rushing to examine the board only to find the pieces in disarray. She sighed lightly, \"If I’d known, I would’ve studied it more carefully earlier.\"","After sorting the black and white pieces, she began recalling the game’s sequence, thoughtfully returning each stone to its original position.","One sat sipping tea, the other held the pieces in deep thought...","Days slipped by unnoticed. On this particular day, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian brought Xiao Junyan back to Yunxiao Mountain.","But unlike their previous visit, Xiao Junyan now looked visibly haggard.","\"Big Brother Xiao? What happened to you?\"","Yue’er looked at Xiao Junyan, who appeared utterly worn out and unrecognizable. In her memory, he had never let himself go like this. How come this time he had come looking so much thinner, unshaven, with bloodshot eyes? Seeing him, she could clearly sense the deep anxiety weighing on his heart.","\"Little Qi...\"","Looking at her, Xiao Junyan struggled to find the words.","He had intended to resolve matters with his own abilities, but upon taking charge, he realized his strength was utterly insufficient.","His strength was limited to his own capabilities. The force suppressing them wasn’t a single individual but an immensely powerful faction. He’d tried to uncover the mastermind behind it, but they were deeply concealed, beyond his reach.","The family crisis and the pressure from the elders nearly crushed him. The warning from the Old Predecessor was especially agonizing.","He came to Yunxiao Mountain to see her because the Old Predecessor had ordered him to settle things with her once and for all.","He arrived, yet the words refused to leave his lips.","Not long ago, he had sworn to her that if he ever married, she would be the one. But now, just months later, he had already...","Seeing him before her, Yue’er felt a flutter in her heart. She thought she understood why he looked so haggard and anxious now.","When Mother left not long ago, she had mentioned testing him. It seemed Mother had already begun."]},{"number":5251,"title":"Chapter 5251: I am","paragraphs":["Given Mother’s methods, she’d likely pull this off without anyone noticing, leaving the Xiao family powerless to resolve it.","At that moment, a flicker of guilt stirred within her. If not for her, perhaps he wouldn’t be facing all this trouble and pressure now!","\"Big Brother Xiao, please sit down and have some tea!\" Yue’er poured him a cup and asked, \"Are you very busy after returning, Big Brother Xiao? Why haven’t you shaved? You look quite different from the Big Brother Xiao I know.\"","\"Little Qi, I’m sorry.\"","He lowered his eyes, his voice tinged with gloom. At that moment, he couldn’t even meet Yun Qi’s gaze.","Hearing this, Yun Qi understood his meaning. Yet, curiosity stirred within her. What exactly had her Mother done? That it could make him admit defeat so swiftly?","\"Big Brother Xiao, why are you apologizing to me? You haven’t done anything wrong to me!\" she spoke up.","Xiao Junyan looked at her and said, \"The Old Predecessor has arranged a marriage for me. I...\"","He took a deep breath and told her, \"I’m sorry. Not long ago, I confessed my feelings to you. But between my family and you, I ultimately couldn’t abandon my family to choose you.\"","His voice was low and hoarse as he continued, \"I am Xiao Junyan, the Young Master of the Xiao family. I cannot turn a blind eye to my clan’s peril. I...\"","\"Big Brother Xiao.\"","Yue’er’s lips curved into a gentle smile. She gazed at him and said, \"Big Brother Xiao, you needn’t blame yourself or feel guilty. In truth, the one who should be apologizing is me.\"","She sighed softly. \"I met Big Brother Xiao when I was very young. All these years, I’ve always regarded you as a Big Brother. But when we went down the mountain last time, spending time together, I realized you felt differently about me. I think you liked me, but I wasn’t ready to accept those feelings.\"","\"In that secret realm, trapped by that fragment of divine soul, I saw Big Brother Xiao confront my illusion. Even knowing it might not be my true form, he refused to let my phantom suffer the slightest harm. He chose to cover himself in wounds instead. My heart was utterly shaken.\"","\"Over the years, only my closest family had treated me this way. I never imagined Big Brother Xiao would go to such lengths. Later, when my meridians were destroyed and cracks appeared in my dantian, everyone said I was ruined—unable to cultivate anymore, doomed to live out my days as an ordinary mortal. Yet it was then that Big Brother Xiao confessed his feelings to me.\"","She smiled as she spoke, looking at him: \" My feelings were complex then—shocked and touched. I liked Brother Xiao, but I wasn’t sure if it was love. So I asked my Mother. She said, regardless of whether I loved him, since he’d confessed, she’d test him first. She wanted to see how far he’d go for me. If he truly risked everything for me, if I meant more to him than anything else, then we could build our relationship.\"","At this point, she looked at him apologetically and continued, \"Big Brother Xiao, the truth is... my father is Xuanyuan Mo Ze, Hell’s Lord and my mother is Feng Jiu. I am their youngest daughter. My name is Xuanyuan Muyue.\"","Xiao Junyan stared at her in utter shock, stumbling back in disbelief. His mind churned like a raging sea, his thoughts completely blank.","She said... her father was Hell’s Lord, her Mother was Feng Jiu, and her name was... Xuanyuan Muyue..."]},{"number":5252,"title":"Chapter 5252: Unworthy","paragraphs":["In this moment, he understood everything.","All that had transpired during this time—it was all because of this...","Yet he never imagined she would be Xuanyuan Muyue, the daughter of the Yan Emperor and Phoenix Empress...","\"I’m sorry. I never expected Mother’s actions would place such immense pressure on Big Brother Xiao. I’m the one who owes him an apology,\" she said guiltily.","She knew that if she hadn’t been so clueless about how to handle this, Mother wouldn’t have tested him. Without that test, he wouldn’t have faced this pressure and these choices. Ultimately, it was her fault. Everything he was enduring now stemmed from her.","Xiao Junyan watched her, his expression shifting from initial shock, disbelief, and shame to eventual calm. He drew a deep breath, exhaled heavily, and then smiled inexplicably.","\"I’m the one unworthy of you. You don’t need to apologize. In truth, I should be the one apologizing to you.\" He looked at her and said, \"Your Mother’s actions weren’t wrong. I’m the one unworthy of you.\"","\"Big Brother Xiao...\" She looked at him with concern.","Xiao Junyan flashed a faint smile. \"Don’t worry. I’m fine. Once I return, I must take charge of family affairs. There likely won’t be many chances to see you again.\"","Looking at her before him, his heart ached, a sharp pain twisting within him. Yet he forced a smile, reaching out to pull her tightly into his embrace.","Yue’er instinctively wanted to pull away, but after a moment’s thought, she remained still. Instead, she reached out and awkwardly patted his back.","\"You deserve better. I believe you will meet someone even better in the future.\"","He released her and stepped back, fixing her with a deep gaze. \"I’m leaving. Take care of yourself.\"","\"Mhm.\" Yue’er’s eyes glistened as she nodded. Watching him turn and stride away, she didn’t follow. She realized she liked Big Brother Xiao, but she didn’t love him. At least, she understood her feelings for him weren’t the same as those between Father and Mother.","At that moment, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian was sitting and chatting with the Azure Emperor at a table ahead.","Sipping tea, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian said, \"Recently, I visited Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress to revisit the matter of their betrothal. To my surprise, they didn’t refuse this time. Instead, they suggested letting the two youngsters spend some time together to see how things go. If neither has objections, they’ll formalize the engagement.\"","His face beamed with satisfaction as he continued, \"If it comes to pass, Azure Emperor, you must grace us with your presence at the wedding feast.\"","Azure Emperor gave him a faint, dismissive glance, sipped his tea, and replied, \"Then this Emperor shall await the good news.\"","\"Hahahaha...\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian laughed heartily, about to speak, when Xiao Junyan arrived. He immediately said, \"Then it’s settled. We have matters to attend to and won’t stay long.\"","\"Old Predecessor, Azure Emperor,\" Xiao Junyan bowed and addressed them.","\"Junyan, how did your talks with Yun Qi go?\" Great Emperor Xiao Tian inquired.","Azure Emperor sipped his tea, not even lifting his head, his expression impassive as if he hadn’t heard their exchange.","Xiao Junyan glanced at Azure Emperor before turning to Great Emperor Xiao Tian. \"Old Predecessor, let us return.\"","Hearing this, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian smiled, thinking to himself that Xiao Junyan must have already handled everything. He then bowed to the Azure Emperor in farewell: \"Azure Emperor, we shall gather again another day.\"","The Azure Emperor gave a slight nod. Watching them depart, he finally began to play with the cup in his hand, shaking his head and revealing a faint, enigmatic smile."]},{"number":5253,"title":"Chapter 5253: Upon Learning","paragraphs":["\"Master.\" Yue’er walked over. Seeing her master sitting there, twirling a teacup in his hand, she sat down across from him, cupping her cheeks with both hands as she looked at him.","\"What’s wrong?\" asked the Azure Emperor, gazing at his young disciple before him. His mood had inexplicably lifted, and as a result, the corners of his lips curled up slightly even as he spoke.","\"Master, why do you look so happy? \" Yue’er asked, letting out a soft sigh. \"I’m not feeling very happy. Something’s weighing on my mind.\"","\"Hmm? Because of Xiao Junyan?\" The Azure Emperor raised an eyebrow and glanced at her.","\"Big Brother Xiao looked so haggard when he came this time, and he’s under a lot of pressure—all because of me. I feel very uneasy.\" she murmured.","\"I believe he’ll never forget what happened this time,\" the Azure Emperor said calmly. \"Consider it a lesson for him. You needn’t feel uneasy. If he hadn’t chosen to give you up, what he would have gained would have been far greater than what he’s lost now.\"","With that, he shook his head. \"Even I must admit Mother’s methods are formidable. Most people couldn’t withstand such a trial. His choice to side with the clan is, in a way, understandable. However, someone like that is no longer worthy of you.\"","\"I just received a message from Mother. She said she’ll come to pick me up tomorrow.\" She rubbed her face and asked anxiously, \"Master, do you think Big Brother Xiao might do something reckless?\"","\"He’s not that fragile,\" the Azure Emperor said coolly, then added, \"This incident has made him realize his shortcomings. I believe that once he overcomes this hurdle, his future achievements will be no less than those of your two Senior Brothers.\"","Xiao Junyan is an exceptionally talented individual. Today’s events will serve not only as a setback but also as motivation. He believes that Xiao Junyan’s future achievements will be no less impressive—perhaps even surpassing those of the Great Emperor Xiao Tian.","\"Go pack your things. I’ll take you there. We’ll stay at your place for a while, so there’s no need for your Mother to come pick you up.\" The Azure Emperor said, gesturing for her to get ready.","\"Oh.\" Yue’er stood up and headed toward the cave abode.","Meanwhile, on the other side, the Great Emperor Xiao Tian, still unaware of the situation, was in high spirits. Halfway there, he said to Xiao Junyan, \"You handled this matter quite well. Once we return, make the necessary preparations, and then we’ll go...\"","Before he could finish, Xiao Junyan cut him off.","\"Old Predecessor, there’s no need to go anywhere. And as for the marriage between Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress’s daughter, there’s no need to mention it anymore.\" Xiao Junyan said, his voice tinged with indifference, even more so than before.","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian froze, furrowing his brow. \"What do you mean by that?\"","Xiao Junyan looked ahead and said, \"I am not worthy of her.\"","\"Nonsense! You are the most outstanding son of the Xiao clan. How could you possibly be unworthy of the Phoenix Empress’s daughter? Look at all the talented young men across the land—how many can compare to you? Moreover, the Phoenix Empress herself holds you in high regard.\" Great Emperor Xiao Tian said.","Xiao Junyan took a deep breath and said, \"Old Predecessor, do you even know who Yun Qi is?\"","\"Who could she possibly be? She’s nothing more than the Azure Emperor’s junior disciple. Now that her meridians are completely destroyed and her dantian is cracked, she can never cultivate again for the rest of her life—she’s just like an ordinary mortal.\" The Great Emperor Xiao Tian said. Upon giving it some thought, he realized there seemed to be an underlying meaning in his own words, and he couldn’t help but frown, a vague sense of foreboding rising in his heart.","\"What do you mean by that? Is there a problem with her status?\" he couldn’t help but ask."]},{"number":5254,"title":"Chapter 5254: Withdraw","paragraphs":["Xiao Junyan gazed ahead, his deep voice emerging slowly from his lips: \"She is the daughter of the Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress—Xuanyuan Muyue.\"","The Great Emperor Xiao Tian was startled and suddenly raised his voice in exclamation: \"What?!\"","However, Xiao Junyan said no more, merely gazing ahead.","\"How could Yun Qi be the daughter of Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress? You must know that back when they hadn’t yet ascended, the Azure Emperor had already taken three disciples...\" Yet, the moment the words left his mouth, he suddenly fell silent.","If Yun Qi really was Feng Jiu’s daughter, then wouldn’t the Azure Emperor’s other two disciples be...","At this thought, his heart gave a violent jolt. Under the circumstances back then, had Feng Jiu already sent the three children to the Azure Emperor to become his disciples? Had this path been laid out years ago? How—how on earth was that possible?","What terrified him even more was that if Yun Qi really was Feng Jiu’s daughter, then the marriage she had mentioned to him...","For a moment, everything went black before his eyes. His body swayed slightly as he muttered, \"This can’t be true. How could this possibly be true?\"","\"It is true. Yun Qi told me so herself,\" Xiao Junyan said, mercilessly shattering the last shred of hope in his heart.","\"Th-then what about the marriage...\" He stared blankly at Xiao Junyan, whose face was devoid of emotion. Only now did he sense that his demeanor had changed from just a few days ago.","\"Surely you don’t think, Old Predecessor, that after our visit to Yunxiao Mountain today, we’ll be allowed back onto the Immortal Islands of the Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress? That marriage was, of course, merely a pretext.\" He paused, then continued, \"I’m sure it won’t be long before the forces suppressing us are withdrawn as well.\"","Great Emperor Xiao Tian stood there in a daze, muttering, \"How could this happen? How could this happen...\"","Just as they had predicted, after they left Yunxiao Mountain, Feng Jiu sent a message to Yue’er. After ascertaining the situation, she relayed the news to Hao’er, instructing him to withdraw the pressure on the Xiao family, and also sent a message to Du Fan and the others, telling them they could stop their actions.","She had never intended to truly target the Xiao family this time; it was merely a test for Xiao Junyan and the Xiao clan. Now that the results were in, regardless of the outcome, she naturally would not continue to suppress the Xiao family.","After she sent them the message, Hao’er and Du Fan swiftly withdrew their pressure on the Xiao family.","On the Immortal Island, Feng Jiu sighed softly and said to Xuanyuan Mo Ze, \"I actually thought Xiao Junyan was quite decent, but I never expected him to give up in the end.\"","\"The facts prove he isn’t worthy of our Yue’er,\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze remarked casually. \"Besides, I wasn’t ready to let Yue’er marry so early anyway. Let her stay by our side for a few more years.\"","However, Feng Jiu was troubled. \"Then tell me,\" she asked, \"what kind of man will be worthy of our Yue’er in the future?\"","\"Why the rush? What is meant to be hers will eventually be hers. Just because he hasn’t appeared yet doesn’t mean he won’t appear later. Who knows, perhaps he’s already here—we just haven’t met him yet.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze spoke calmly and unhurriedly; he wasn’t the least bit worried about his daughter.","With a daughter as exceptional as hers, what kind of man wouldn’t she want? She could take her time choosing; she was bound to find the very best.","Seeing that he wasn’t the least bit worried, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but roll her eyes at him. She snorted lightly and said, \"If you ask me, you’d rather your daughter never married at all—just stayed by your side forever.\""]},{"number":5255,"title":"Chapter 5255: A Chance Encounter","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Xuanyuan Mo Ze smiled, reached out to take her hand, and said, \"I just want the best for our daughter. Besides, I truly want her to stay by our side for a few more years. After all, the children have been away these past years and have rarely been with us.\"","Seeing this, Feng Jiu finally said, \"Yue’er has already come here with her master. It will take at least half a year for her injuries to heal properly, so you’ll have plenty of opportunities to see her during that time.\"","She shook her head as she spoke. \"Yue’er is such a worry. Her two older brothers are out in the world and only send occasional messages to let us know they’re safe, so I feel at ease with them. But with this child, if I don’t keep a close eye on her, I’m genuinely afraid she’ll get into trouble at any moment.\"","\"So, before her injuries flared up, we’ve kept her confined to this island to prevent her from causing trouble elsewhere,\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze said with a smile.","\"Come to think of it, given the Azure Emperor’s abilities, he should have reached our Immortal Island by now. Why haven’t we seen him yet?\" Feng Jiu asked curiously.","\"I suppose Yue’er got distracted playing and got delayed!\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze said, not giving it a second thought.","Meanwhile, Yue’er had indeed left Yunxiao Mountain with her master. However, in the end, her master couldn’t resist her pleading and agreed to take her on a scenic journey to the Immortal Island.","She knew that if she went to her parents’ place this time, she wouldn’t be able to go out and play for a long while. She’d stayed on Yunxiao Mountain for so long, and had only just come down before getting seriously injured. Now she was headed to the Immortal Island to recuperate, and wouldn’t be allowed to go out and play. Being the playful type, she simply couldn’t stand being cooped up, so she had to make the most of her time and have one last good time before reaching the Immortal Island.","Along the way, the Azure Emperor indulged her. Seeing how much she enjoyed exploring towns, he let her wander around and buy little trinkets she liked whenever they arrived at a new place.","One day, after they entered the city, the Azure Emperor went to an inn to rest, while Yue’er eagerly set off to explore the market. Although she was currently unable to cultivate like a mortal, her master—fearing she might be bullied while out—had left a strand of his divine consciousness within her to protect her. Thus, even when he wasn’t by her side, there was no need to worry that she would encounter danger.","After wandering around the city and buying a few trinkets, just as she was about to head back, she noticed quite a few cultivators heading toward the outskirts. Glancing up at the sky beyond the city walls, she detected faint fluctuations of powerful energy—as if caused by the turbulence of a battle.","\"Is there a fight? It looks pretty intense,\" she murmured, her curiosity piqued. She decided to follow the crowd to take a look—after all, with her master’s fragment of divine consciousness protecting her, she figured she’d be safe.","So, full of excitement, she ran after the cultivators toward the city gates to catch the spectacle. Though she couldn’t channel her spirit energy, her agility remained, allowing her to move quite swiftly.","When she reached the city gates, a large crowd had already gathered. She pushed her way to the front, but the sight that met her eyes left her stunned; she stared in disbelief, her eyes wide.","Shen Shiqi?","How could it be him? How did he end up here? Were those dead bodies on the ground members of the Shen family? And who were those black robed men? Why were they attacking him?","In an instant, a flood of thoughts rushed through her mind, and seeing the numerous wounds on Shen Shiqi’s body only made her even more anxious."]},{"number":5256,"title":"Chapter 5256: Kill her","paragraphs":["Shen Shiqi was a formidable fighter, but so were those dozens of black robed men. Now, only three or five of his men remained by his side, and every one of them was wounded and looked utterly exhausted. In contrast, the black robed men radiated a fierce killing intent; their attacks were relentless, and the slightest misstep would mean certain death by the sword!","\"These are people from the Shen family, one of the top clans. I’ve met the Seventeenth Young Master once. But how did they end up crossing paths with the Rakshasa Hall? These are all top-tier assassins, and they’re all willing to die for the cause. I’ve heard that once the Rakshasa Hall strikes, there’s absolutely no chance of survival.\"","The cultivator murmured to himself. Though he wanted to step forward to help—hoping to forge ties with a top-tier clan like the Shen family—the Rakshasa Hall was no force to be trifled with. Each of their members possessed formidable strength that could not be underestimated. Valuing his own life, he dared not offer assistance.","\"I don’t think they can hold out much longer. The dozens of assassins the Rakshasa Hall sent are all top-tier killers. Even if that man is the Seventeenth Young Master of the Shen family, I doubt he’ll survive their attack.\"","Another cultivator remarked, quietly stepping back. It was best not to get involved in such matters, and certainly not to get too close—otherwise, one could easily invite trouble.","Yue’er watched the scene while alerting her master to come over immediately. When she saw a black robed man hurl a hidden weapon at Shen Shiqi, she immediately shouted a warning.","\"Watch out for the hidden weapons!\"","\"Whoosh, whoosh!\"","Perhaps thanks to her warning, Shen Shiqi narrowly dodged the two projectiles. As they struck the ground, even a single blade of grass withered instantly, causing those nearby to gasp in horror.","Those projectiles were laced with a deadly poison!","However, compared to the poison on the projectiles, what shocked and alarmed Shen Shiqi even more at that moment was that he actually saw Yun Qi here!","\"Let’s go!\" he barked at Yun Qi, urging her to leave quickly.","He knew her physical condition—she was currently unable to practice her cultivation, and her combat strength was practically nonexistent. If anything were to happen to her...","It was Yue’er’s timely warning that allowed Shen Shiqi to dodge the projectiles, and it was Shen Shiqi’s panic and concern that caused the two black robed men to exchange a glance in that instant. Suddenly, they shifted their attack and lunged toward Yue’er, who was about ten meters away.","Seeing the two black robed men reaching for her, Yue’er’s eyes widened. \"I can’t actually fight, can I?\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, her hand swept across her waist. shot out with a whoosh and struck the two black robed men attacking her with a crack.","\"Ouch! It’s the Ancient Divine Whip!\"","A searing pain shot through their hands, and upon seeing the whip, the two black robed men stared at her in utter shock, gazing at her—and the Ancient Divine Whip in her hand—with disbelief.","If their memory served them correctly, the Ancient Divine Whip should be in the possession of Yun Qi, the Azure Emperor’s junior disciple. As the Azure Emperor’s disciple, Yun Qi was said to possess extraordinary talent and exceptional prowess—it was absolutely impossible for her to be an ordinary mortal with no trace of spirit energy!","And as for snatching the Ancient Divine Whip—no one would dare do such a thing. After all, the Azure Emperor had long made it clear: whoever dares to seize the whip will have their entire clan slaughtered!","So, the Ancient Divine Whip held by the young girl before them must be a fake?","Although they felt pain in their hands, the whip’s impact on their limbs and bodies seemed far less devastating than they had imagined. Moreover, how could anyone hold the Divine Whip without channeling spirit energy to wield it?","Therefore, this whip is most likely a fake!","\"Kill her!\""]},{"number":5257,"title":"Chapter 5257: Instant Kill","paragraphs":["As soon as they were almost certain of this, a flash of murderous intent flickered in the two assassins’ eyes. One of them let out a cold snarl and swung his long sword at Yue’er.","Seeing the two assassins heading toward Yun Qi, and realizing she had lost all her power, she grew anxious and immediately shouted, \"She is the Azure Emperor’s disciple! If you dare harm a single hair on her head, the Azure Emperor will not spare you!\"","The two assassins paused only briefly before continuing without hesitation: \"The person before us is nothing but a mere mortal! If we kill her, so be it!\"","Yue’er watched their swords hurtle toward her. Knowing she was no match for them, she quickly dodged and retreated. However, her opponents were far too powerful, and since she was relying solely on basic footwork, she couldn’t keep up with their speed. In the blink of an eye, the icy sword qi was already bearing down on her face.","\"Yun Qi!\"","Shen Shiqi cried out in alarm, wanting to rush forward to save her, but he was entangled by the other assassins and couldn’t break free. In that split second of distraction, he was struck by a palm strike, causing him to spurt out a mouthful of blood.","\"Pfft!\"","Seeing she couldn’t evade it, Yun Qi stopped dodging and stood her ground, staring intently as the sword qi hurtled toward her. Yet, just as the sword qi was about to strike her, a green-clad figure appeared beside her. With a flick of the wrist, he dispersed the sword qi, sending the two attackers tumbling dozens of meters away as they spat out a mouthful of blood.","\"Pfft!\"","The two assassins felt their blood surging violently within them as they spat blood; with every breath, more blood trickled from the corners of their mouths. Their eyes widened in horror as they stared at the man who had suddenly appeared before them.","His power was so great that a single wave of his hand had severely injured both of them. Such strength was rare in the world today...","\"Master!\"","Seeing him, Yue’er gave a sweet smile. She knew her master would come to save her.","The Azure Emperor frowned and looked at her. \"It’s only been a moment—how did you go and get yourself into trouble again?\"","She stuck out her tongue, sounding a bit guilty. \"No, no, I didn’t cause trouble. Really, I just came to watch the commotion, and then I saw Shen Shiqi, and those people tried to kill me.\"","As she spoke, she tugged at his sleeve and said pitifully, \"If Master hadn’t come to save me, they would’ve sliced me in half.\"","Hearing this, a flash of coldness crossed the Azure Emperor’s eyes as he glanced at the black robed men. \"You mere members of the Rakshasa Hall dare lay a hand on this Emperor’s disciple?\"","No sooner had the words left his mouth than a powerful, palpable aura surged forth, bearing down on the black-clad assassins. The dozens of assassins were startled by his words; before they could even utter a sound, they felt an immense, crushing pressure descend upon them.","\"Boom! Boom! Boom!\"","A series of heavy thuds echoed out. The dozens of assassins were sent crashing into the ground as if struck by a palm, their bodies sinking deep into the earth. They lay motionless, not even managing to utter a scream.","Shen Shiqi paused in astonishment. As he watched the crisis resolve in an instant and breathed a sigh of relief, he was even more shocked by the Azure Emperor’s power. Such strength was truly beyond their reach.","However, among the dozens of black robed men, only one had not been slammed into the ground. Instead, he knelt there with shattered knees, cold sweat streaming down his face.","\"Within three days, I command the Rakshasa Hall to vanish from existence! Get out!\" As the deep voice fell, a flick of his sleeve sent the sole surviving assassin flying a hundred meters away."]},{"number":5258,"title":"Chapter 5258: A Happy Encounter","paragraphs":["The few surviving members of the Shen family exchanged glances, then, led by Shen Shiqi, stepped forward to stand before the Azure Emperor and bowed respectfully to him.","\"Thank you, Azure Emperor, for saving our lives.\"","The Azure Emperor cast a glance at them and said indifferently, \"You’re overthinking it. I only killed those who sought to take my disciple’s life. \" The implication was clear: saving them was never part of the plan; he had merely eliminated them all because they had sought to kill his disciple.","\"What are you still standing there for?\" The Azure Emperor turned and walked toward the city, but seeing Yun Qi still standing in place, he glanced back at her.","\"Mm, I’m coming over!\" Yun Qi called out, turning to Shen Shiqi. \"Let’s go! My master and I are staying at an inn in town. Once we get there, I’ll help bandage your wounds.\"","\"Thank you,\" Shen Shiqi replied with a smile. Leaving the two behind to clean up the area, the rest of the group followed Yue’er and the others into the city.","Watching them leave, some cultivators were still in a daze. It wasn’t until much later that they heard them murmuring among themselves: \"Was that the Azure Emperor just now? And that’s his disciple, Yun Qi? The one wielding the Ancient Divine Whip? How could she be someone without any cultivation?\"","\"The Azure Emperor’s power is truly formidable. Those dozens of ’Heaven-Ranked’ assassins from the Rakshasa Hall were actually killed just like that.\"","\"The Rakshasa Hall has really hit a brick wall this time. I doubt the Rakshasa Hall will exist after today.\"","Recalling what the Azure Emperor had said earlier, the cultivators’ eyes flickered. When would they ever become figures like the Azure Emperor?","At an inn in the city, after Yue’er had tended to Shen Shiqi’s wounds, she asked, \"How did you end up here? I thought you’d already returned to your master’s estate.\" \"","\"I was delayed along the way. Plus, I don’t know who hired a ’Heaven’s Mark’ assassin from the Rakshasa Hall to kill me. If I hadn’t run into you all this time, I’m afraid I really would have met my end right here.\" Shen Shiqi sighed lightly.","\"Are there a lot of people after your life?\" Yue’er looked at him in surprise and asked curiously, \"Do you have that many enemies?\"","Shen Shiqi smiled wryly and said, \"I have too many enemies to count, but there aren’t many who can actually hire the Rakshasa Hall.\" As he spoke, he smoothed out his robe and added, \"You’re just a little girl; you wouldn’t understand these things.\"","Yue’er laughed and said smugly, \"That’s true. Although there are quite a few people who want to kill me, they only dare to think about it—they don’t dare to act.\"","Hearing this, Shen Shiqi smiled, looked at her, and asked, \"Your injuries haven’t healed yet. Why aren’t you recuperating on Yunxiao Mountain? Why did you come here instead?\"","\"Hehe, I’ll let you in on a secret. My master was going to take me to the Ghost Doctor Phoenix Empress for treatment, but I’m a bit of a troublemaker. I figured if I went there, I’d have to stay for ages and wouldn’t be able to go out, so I begged my master to take a scenic route there instead.\" She said with a mischievous smile.","Shen Shiqi was slightly surprised, then laughed. \"That one is indeed renowned for her medical skills. It’s fortunate that you’re the Azure Emperor’s disciple; otherwise, it would be difficult for an ordinary person to even get a glimpse of her.\"","After chatting for a while, Yue’er said, \"Well then, you should get some rest! I’m going to check on my master. Let’s have dinner together tonight!\"","\"Alright,\" Shen Shiqi replied, rising to see her out.","After leaving Shen Shiqi’s room, Yue’er set off toward her master’s quarters. Suddenly, she paused in her tracks, furrowing her brow slightly. She felt a faint pang in her heart, as if a sense of unease had crept in."]},{"number":5259,"title":"Chapter 5259: Not Good","paragraphs":["Her heart was pounding in her chest, as if it had lost its normal rhythm. But the sensation came on suddenly and vanished just as quickly.","In just a moment, the feeling was gone.","She stood there in a daze, pressing her hand to her chest as she felt her heartbeat gradually return to normal.","\"What are you doing?\" The Azure Emperor happened to open the door and step out. Seeing her standing at the doorway, one hand pressed against her chest, staring blankly, he asked, \"Are you feeling unwell?\"","\"Master, my heart was beating very fast just now. I had a really bad feeling, but it disappeared after just a moment.\" Yue’er spoke honestly, unable to figure out what had happened herself.","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor glanced at her and said gently, \"As long as you stay by my side and don’t wander off, you don’t need to worry about anything happening.\"","\"Oh.\" She replied, and seeing him come out, added, \"Master, I was just about to ask—what would you like to eat tonight?\"","\"You decide.\" The Azure Emperor said, walking with his hands behind his back to a table by the window on the second floor and sitting down.","Yue’er followed him over and sat down beside him. As she poured him a cup of tea, she said, \"Master, are the people of the Rakshasa Hall all that formidable? Shen Shiqi is considered quite strong, yet I never expected him to be injured so badly. It’s a good thing they ran into you today; otherwise, they really would have died by those people’s swords.\"","\"The Rakshasa Hall is considered formidable in the eyes of most cultivators, but in the eyes of your master and your parents, they are nothing to speak of,\" said the Azure Emperor, lifting his teacup and taking a sip.","The two sat there, chatting casually while watching the street scene outside. As night fell, Yue’er called Shen Shiqi over to join them for dinner. After the meal, they sat for a while before retiring to their respective rooms to rest.","The next day, since Shen Shiqi and his group happened to be traveling the same route, at Yun Qi’s insistence, the Azure Emperor agreed to take them along.","Once aboard the airship, their speed increased significantly, and they made almost no stops. However, as they neared the town where the Shen family’s Patriarch’s residence was located, Yue’er—who had been in high spirits all day—suddenly fell silent.","She sat quietly, saying nothing. The others on board were resting with their eyes closed. Shen Shiqi, sensing that something was wrong with her, stared at her. Seeing that she seemed to be holding something back, he asked with concern, \"Yun Qi, what’s wrong? Are you feeling unwell?\"","The Azure Emperor, who had been resting with his eyes closed at the bow of the ship, opened his eyes upon hearing this and looked toward Yun Qi. Noticing that her complexion was alternately pale and flushed, and that her overall aura seemed off, he immediately swept his sleeve, causing the airship to descend.","The others quickly stepped aside. Watching as the Azure Emperor stepped forward to take her pulse, they couldn’t help but feel tense as well. Although the other members of the Shen family weren’t very familiar with the Azure Emperor or Yun Qi, they had grown fond of this cheerful and mischievous young girl along the way. Seeing her in such a poor state now, they couldn’t help but worry for her too.","After checking her pulse, the Azure Emperor furrowed his brow slightly. He immediately condensed a pure stream of spirit energy, forming a seal that he pressed into the center of her forehead.","\"Crack!\"","\"Boom!\"","At that moment, a dark cloud suddenly formed in the sky. Lightning flashed through it, crackling loudly, followed by a muffled rumble of thunder within the clouds, carrying a faint yet formidable force.","The Azure Emperor looked up abruptly, his expression changing. \"Oh no!\""]},{"number":5260,"title":"Chapter 5260: True Form Revealed","paragraphs":["\"Wh-what’s going on?\" Shen Shiqi, standing beside him, was startled by the sight; his voice stuttered, and he grew tense.","The Azure Emperor supported Yun Qi as he gazed up at the sky, his expression grave as he muttered, \"Why now of all times? Damn it!\" As soon as the words left his mouth, he turned to Shen Shiqi and said, \"You must leave immediately! Go!\"","Before Shen Shiqi and the others could ask any questions, a powerful force hurled them a hundred meters away. Having traveled together all this way, they now witnessed this strange phenomenon in the sky and had no idea what was about to happen. Naturally, they couldn’t leave at a time like this, so they remained a hundred metres away, watching anxiously.","However, in the brief moment that followed, the cloud mass gathering above the Azure Emperor and Yun Qi swirled ever larger, and the rumbling grew louder. It seemed as though a dark, vortex-like cloud had formed in the sky, with powerful air currents converging overhead, drawing cultivators from nearby towns to come and witness the spectacle.","Seeing the Celestial Tribulation take shape and begin to surge, the Azure Emperor realized he could no longer carry her away. He had no choice but to cast a barrier around them to try and hold it back, while simultaneously sending a telepathic message across a thousand miles to Feng Jiu, urging her to come quickly.","Meanwhile, Yun Qi was moaning in agony, cold sweat beading on her forehead, yet her body felt as scorching as flames.","\"Ughhh! Master, I—I feel so terrible...\" Yue’er cried out in pain, her hands clutching his arms tightly.","\"I’m here, don’t be afraid. Everything will be fine.\" With one hand, he supported her, letting her lean against his chest; with the other, he channeled spirit energy to press against her brow, attempting to suppress the crimson lotus that threatened to break through its seal and burst forth.","The Primordial Red Lotus sealed within her had remained dormant all these years, causing no trouble. Even when her meridians were completely destroyed and her dantian cracked not long ago, it had only shown faint signs of loosening. Yet, unexpectedly, today it had triggered a heavenly tribulation here, threatening to break free from the seal.","Had her meridians remained intact, her cultivation intact, and her dantian uncracked, she could have withstood the lightning tribulation even if the lotus had broken free. But now, in her mortal form, she could not endure even the power of the Primordial Red Lotus, let alone the lightning tribulation—it would be enough to cause her body to explode!","For a mortal body to bear the Primordial Red Lotus, once activated, it would bring about a heavenly tribulation of utter destruction. And even for powerful beings of their caliber, facing the will of Heaven, they were still powerless to stop it.","As her body temperature soared, the Azure Emperor, who was supporting her, felt as though he were holding a ball of fire in his arms. Had his robes not been made of extraordinary materials, they would surely have been reduced to ashes by the intense heat.","With one hand, he channeled an unending stream of spirit energy into the space between her eyebrows, attempting to contain the flame that threatened to burst forth. Yet the Primordial Red Lotus was no ordinary entity; even the power of the Azure Emperor struggled to suppress it at this moment.","As he watched the spirit energy he channeled into her brow being consumed until he could send no more, and as her true features gradually emerged beneath the powerful crimson lotus flame raging within her, his heart grew heavier and heavier.","A crimson lotus, no larger than a fingernail, gradually emerged from Yue’er’s brow. Her face seemed to ripple with waves of flame as her previously delicate and charming features faded inch by inch, revealing the face of a breathtakingly beautiful young maiden.","Against that exquisite face, the tiny crimson lotus that was gradually emerging added a touch of alluring, mysterious, and captivating beauty. Yet the Azure Emperor, the only one who could see her true form at that moment, had no heart to admire it; instead, his eyes were filled with nothing but concern..."]},{"number":5261,"title":"Chapter 5261: Red Lotus Appears","paragraphs":["Yue’er’s outer garments were originally just ordinary clothes, but beneath them she wore a divine robe. However, as her body temperature rose higher and higher, and layers of fiery ripples spread from her body, her outer garments were reduced to ashes, leaving only the protective divine robe she wore underneath.","Seeing this, the Azure Emperor gathered immortal energy in his fingers and used it to conjure a blue robe to cover her. Just then, a bolt of lightning suddenly struck down from the clouds, but instead of striking directly, it dissipated upon touching the top of the barrier above their heads.","A hundred metres away, Shen Shiqi and the others stared wide-eyed, their faces filled with bewilderment and shock. One of the older middle-aged men gasped and said, \"If I’m not mistaken, that flower between Yun Qi’s eyebrows is... is it the Primordial Red Lotus? THE Primordial Red Lotus?!\"","\"That’s right. Look at the waves of fire surging from her body—those aren’t ordinary flames. But how could she possess a Primordial Red Lotus? I’ve never heard of the Primordial Red Lotus being found anywhere!\"","\"It seems her original appearance wasn’t her true face; the one now revealed is her true form. But since we’re a hundred metres away, we can only see her profile.\"","While they discussed this, Shen Shiqi spoke with concern: \"She’s merely a mortal now—how can she withstand the power of the Primordial Red Lotus? And the strikes of that lightning tribulation? If this continues, she’ll die! No, I have to go help her!\" As he spoke, he tried to step forward, but was held back firmly by the people beside him.","\"Master Shiqi, are you out of your mind? This is the lightning tribulation summoned by the Primordial Red Lotus—it’s no ordinary lightning tribulation. Its power is immense; even with our strength, we couldn’t withstand even a fraction of it!\"","\"That’s right. It seems the Primordial Red Lotus was originally sealed within her body. We just don’t know why it was triggered now, summoning this second-tier heavenly tribulation. If she still had any cultivation left, it might be manageable. But now, with her spirit energy completely depleted—she’s as vulnerable as a mortal—yet still harboring the Primordial Red Lotus, I fear this heavenly tribulation intends to annihilate her and reclaim the Primordial Red Lotus.\"","\"Exactly. All we can hope for now is that the Azure Emperor can protect her. If even the Azure Emperor cannot shield her, then she will likely meet her end today.\" At this point, the group sighed, their eyes filled with regret.","Cultivators who had gradually gathered here upon hearing the commotion couldn’t help but gasp when they saw the situation at the barrier. Watching the dark clouds churning in the sky, seemingly brewing powerful air currents and lightning tribulations, one cultivator whispered, \"Who are those two? How could they trigger such a powerful heavenly tribulation?\"","An elderly man standing nearby recognized the figure as the Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain and couldn’t help but express mild surprise. \"That is the Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain. But who is the woman in his arms? And why is the Primordial Red Lotus appearing between her eyebrows?\"","\"The Primordial Red Lotus?\"","\"Whoa! It really is the Primordial Red Lotus!\"","\"This woman possesses no spirit energy at all—she’s merely a mortal!\"","\"How is that possible! How could a mere mortal body possibly withstand the immense power of the Primordial Red Lotus?\"","At that moment, a bolt of heavenly lightning tribulation crashed down from the clouds with a thunderous roar, striking the barrier the Azure Emperor had erected. In that instant, the mighty lightning and the two forces within the barrier collided, producing a deafening explosion. A powerful gust of wind surged down from above the barrier; as it struck the surface surrounding the barrier, it transformed into a terrifying wave of air that surged outward with a whoosh."]},{"number":5262,"title":"Chapter 5262: Holding Up the Sky","paragraphs":["\"Arghhhhh!\"","A hundred metres away, the cultivators who had gathered to watch the spectacle were all caught in the wake of this powerful shockwave. One by one, they were hurled dozens of meters away; those with lower cultivation levels even coughed up blood on the spot, their faces etched with terror.","\"Boom!\"","Perhaps because of the barrier’s protection, the Heavenly Tribulation Lightning failed to strike Yue’er. As if the Dao of Heaven were even more enraged, the second bolt of lightning struck with blinding speed, appearing even more powerful and forceful than the first.","Once again, as the heavenly tribulation lightning collided with the barrier, a powerful surge of air rippled out. The cultivators, having already learned their lesson, had long since retreated to a safe distance; this time, the blast did not reach them.","However, the barrier set up by the Azure Emperor had developed a fine, spiderweb-like crack due to the impact of these two bolts of heavenly lightning tribulation.","Seeing the crack in the barrier, the Azure Emperor immediately channeled a surge of spirit energy to swiftly repair it. Yet, before he could fully mend the crack, the third bolt of heavenly lightning tribulation, accompanied by a flash of lightning, struck down without delay.","\"Boom!\"","\"Crack!\"","The moment the third bolt of heavenly lightning tribulation struck, the barrier emitted a cracking sound. Immediately afterward, a powerful gust of wind erupted as the barrier shattered, and the lightning tribulation that had originally struck the barrier now tore through the breach, hurtling toward Yun Qi below.","Seeing that there was no way to block it, the Azure Emperor immediately placed Yun Qi, who was in his arms, inside the airship. With a flick of his hand, he cast a barrier over her. At the same time, he leaned down, using his chest to shield her and his back to block this heavenly tribulation lightning—a strike powerful enough to obliterate her.","\"Azure Emperor!\"","Shen Shiqi cried out in shock, never expecting him to use his own body to shield Yun Qi from the heavenly tribulation lightning. After all, if anyone else were to bear this strike, its power would be many times greater than if she had faced it herself!","Lightning and lightning tribulation struck the Azure Emperor’s back simultaneously. The lightning surged through his body, coursing through his meridians, while the lightning tribulation caused him to tremble involuntarily. Wisps of azure smoke rose from his azure robe, suggesting that even his immortal garment had suffered some scorching damage.","\"Master...\"","Yue’er’s eyes welled with tears. She clutched the hem of her own azure robe tightly, enduring the excruciating pain caused by the powerful energy surging chaotically within her body, all while watching her master use his own body to shield her from the lightning tribulation’s devastating strike.","She knew it—she knew that one could not normally take the Heavenly Tribulation lightning upon oneself for another. But if one did, the power would be many times greater than what the person would have endured. Even though her master was incredibly powerful, the damage such a strike would inflict upon him was unimaginable...","After the lightning tribulation and lightning struck, the sky began to brew another storm. In that brief lull, the Azure Emperor saw Yun Qi calling out to him with reddened eyes and comforted her: \"Don’t cry. Your master is fine.\"","However, it would have been better if he hadn’t said anything; the moment he spoke, tears began to stream uncontrollably down Yue’er’s cheeks.","\"Boom!\"","Another bolt of heavenly tribulation thunder, accompanied by lightning, struck down. The Azure Emperor remained in the same posture, using his back to block the thunder and lightning. Yue’er, lying beneath him, still hadn’t suffered even the slightest injury, yet the red lotus between her brows flickered, and its power continued to surge through her meridians, as if stretching them to their limits. The pain felt like a flame burning within her veins—excruciatingly hot, piercing her heart and searing her bones.","Shen Shiqi clenched his fists, his heart racing. Watching the four bolts of heavenly lightning tribulation that had yet to dissipate, he asked in a deep voice, \"Just how many bolts of heavenly lightning tribulation are there?\""]},{"number":5263,"title":"Chapter 5263: Enough","paragraphs":["The slightly older middle-aged man standing nearby took a deep breath and said, \"At least forty-nine bolts. Moreover, since he is taking the Heavenly Lightning Tribulation upon himself, I fear even the Azure Emperor would struggle to withstand the destructive force of these forty-nine bolts of heavenly lightning.\"","No one dared to step forward in the face of such heavenly tribulation lightning, nor could anyone approach. One by one, they could only watch as the bolts of lightning struck the Azure Emperor one after another.","Yue’er watched, tears streaming down her face. She couldn’t count how many bolts of heavenly tribulation lightning had struck her master; she only knew that whenever a bolt struck, he would groan deeply and spit out a mouthful of blood.","\"Master!\"","She wept bitterly, feeling her heart clench tightly, as if being sliced by a knife. Struggling to rise, she cried out, \"Enough, enough... Enough, Master! Don’t shield me anymore. No, no... I beg you, I beg you... Don’t shield me anymore...\"","\"Guh!\"","The Azure Emperor coughed up another mouthful of blood. A faint, acrid smell of scorched flesh wafted from his body. His spirit energy was already wavering, and the protective divine aura surrounding him had long since been shattered. Now, every bolt of the Heavenly Tribulation struck him directly.","\"Boom!\"","Another bolt of heavenly tribulation lightning struck down. The powerful and terrifying energy crashed into the Azure Emperor’s body before radiating outward. Even the cultivators who had retreated to a great distance could feel the destructive aura carried by the lightning.","As if unable to withstand the blow, the Azure Emperor collapsed onto Yue’er. Blood trickled from his mouth, and the divine energy that had once enveloped him seemed to have been shattered, now drifting into the air around them.","He tried to rise from atop Yue’er, but his body collapsed back down. After two failed attempts, he finally managed to push himself up with his hands, still shielding her beneath him with his own body.","\"Master... Master... Master...\"","Yue’er’s hands clenched tightly into fists. The intense agony caused by the chaotic surges of the Red Lotus energy within her, combined with the sight of her master so grievously wounded while shielding her, left her utterly heartbroken. She screamed in anguish.","\"Ah... Ah... Ahhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh!\"","In the sky, that powerful and terrifying current continued to surge. The dark clouds seemed to roar in response to her screams; waves of clouds churned, and the sounds of wind, lightning, and muffled thunder echoed one after another, as if they too were snarling in fury.","At that moment, the sky above was completely shrouded in dark clouds. The next bolt of heavenly tribulation lightning did not strike immediately; instead, it seemed to be gathering strength, as if it were channeling the combined power of all the previous bolts to deliver a single, decisive blow—as if determined to eliminate both figures below in one fell swoop.","The rumbling sounded like drums echoing through the clouds, one blast following another. Within the dark clouds, it seemed as though a wrathful god of death stood there, wielding a thunder hammer and striking it, producing a series of crackling, lightning-like sounds.","Watching this scene, Shen Shiqi saw that the Azure Emperor below was already struggling to hold on, and his heart sank. He gasped, \"No! If that strike lands, they’re both as good as dead!\"","Suddenly, he broke free from the grip of those holding him back and, bracing against the overwhelming pressure and gale-force winds, took steps as heavy as lead toward them: \"Yun Qi! Azure Emperor! Run! Run!\"","Yet at that moment, the Azure Emperor looked at Yun Qi, who was weeping bitterly, and offered a smile tinged with helplessness and regret: \"I never imagined that back then, I couldn’t protect you, and today, I still cannot protect you...\""]},{"number":5264,"title":"Chapter 5264: Fusion","paragraphs":["His words reached her ears and echoed in her mind. It was as if scenes were flashing before her eyes; the stirrings in her soul, the pain radiating through her body, and the excruciating agony in her head—as if it were about to explode—filled her entire being.","\"Ahhhhhhhhhhh!\"","She clenched her fists tightly and cried out in agony, blood seeping from her knuckles. Suddenly, she fell silent. The crimson lotus between her brows faintly took the shape of a flame. She closed her eyes, and the scenes in her mind grew clearer...","A soul that did not originally belong to this world or this realm had, by a twist of fate, found its way here, inhabiting the body of a small child. Yet, on a day of heavy snow, the child was abandoned and left in the snow.","Just as the child lay on the snowy ground, freezing to the point of death, a celestial-like immortal in azure robes passed by, picked her up, brushed the snow and ice from her body, and carried her back to Yunxiao Mountain. He named her Yun Qi, and from then on, she became the disciple of the Azure Emperor, showered with every conceivable form of affection...","At the mountain’s peak, he personally taught her the ways of immortality and guided her in cultivation. Month after month, year after year, master and disciple lived together, secluded in Yunxiao Mountain, untouched by the ways of the world...","Yet, while the Azure Emperor was in seclusion, Yun Qi faced the Lightning Tribulation during her advancement. Struck by lightning, her body perished and her soul scattered into nothingness, drifting through the heavens and earth until her spirit finally coalesced once more and entered the cycle of reincarnation...","Each memory, each scene, felt as though it were yesterday; yet time flies, and in the blink of an eye, who knows how many years have passed.","Yue’er opened her eyes. In that moment, the radiance in her eyes seemed different from usual, as if an innocent young girl had suddenly grown up.","\"Master... your disciple has returned.\"","She spoke softly, gazing into his narrowed eyes, and a smile blossomed on her lips: \"It was your disciple who caused you worry, Master.\"","As she spoke, a layer of crimson flame surged from her body. With a whoosh, the flames instantly incinerated the barrier the Azure Emperor had cast over her. She sat up, supported her master with both hands, and guided him toward Shen Shiqi.","\"Take good care of my Master.\"","Shen Shiqi caught the Azure Emperor who was being passed to him. Supporting her, he stumbled backward more than ten meters. The Azure Emperor seemed to freeze, staring blankly at the figure shrouded in flames, momentarily unable to recover.","Yue’er soared upward, her entire body engulfed in flames. Unseen by others, the Karma Flame Red Lotus surged through her body, reshaping her mind and repairing her dantian.","Only she could sense it: as her blood flowed and the fluctuations of her spiritual essence rippled, the powerful aura of the Primordial Red Lotus, which had previously raged chaotically within her, had now entirely transformed into crimson flames, reshaping and tempering every vein and bone in her body. As her meridians expanded, the aura of spirit energy emanating from her grew ever more potent. As if spurred by the Primordial Red Lotus, the Nine-Tailed Sacred Beast—an ancient Sacred Beast that had been in deep meditation for many years—burst forth from her body at that very moment.","\"Whoa! The ancient Sacred Beast, the Nine-Tailed Divine Fox? She actually harbors an ancient Sacred Beast within her?\"","The cultivators around her couldn’t help but gasp in shock at the sight of the Nine-Tailed Divine Fox bursting from her body, soaring through the air atop a bed of flames, with Yun Qi standing firmly upon its back.","It was a fully grown Ancient Divine Fox. Its nine immense tails danced through the air; its fur was pure white without a single stray hair, the only visible feature being the fiery mark on its forehead.","The overwhelming aura of the Ancient Divine Sacred Beast, combined with the oppressive pressure from the Dao of Heaven, permeated the surrounding area, making the suffocating atmosphere even more intense than before."]},{"number":5265,"title":"Chapter 5265: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["\"That can’t be right. She was completely devoid of spirit energy before—how could such a powerful aura of spirit energy suddenly surge from her now?\" the cultivator exclaimed in a low voice, clearly baffled by the sight.","\"Look, the Primordial Red Lotus seems to have fused completely with her. I’ve heard that the Karma Flame of the Red Lotus can purify the body and burn away all worldly impurities, but if the body bearing that fire can withstand the Primordial Red Lotus’s immense power, it will shed its mortal form and attain an immortal body—one that even the Karma Flame Red Lotus cannot destroy!\"","The crowd murmured among themselves, unaware that some distance away, Xuanyuan Mo Ze, Feng Jiu, and Mo Chen were all watching from the shadows.","Long before the Azure Emperor had sent his message to Feng Jiu, Mo Chen had been playing chess with Xuanyuan Mo Ze on the Immortal Island, while Feng Jiu lay on a nearby couch, listening to the news Mo Chen had brought them from his journey.","Yue’er faced a tribulation, and they were powerless to assist her in overcoming it; the key to breaking this tribulation lay with the Azure Emperor. If she could survive this ordeal, the long path of immortality that lay ahead—no matter how fraught with difficulties and dangers—would become smooth sailing, turning misfortune into good fortune.","Therefore, upon hearing the Azure Emperor’s telepathic message, the three of them had rushed to the scene. They did not reveal themselves to assist, but instead watched from the shadows. Seeing Yue’er endure such agony and face such a life-and-death ordeal, Feng Jiu had wanted to rush out to help her several times, but each time she was held back by Xuanyuan Mo Ze.","Now, seeing the Primordial Red Lotus sealed within her body finally broken, and its powerful, domineering energy perfectly fused with her—even reshaping her meridians in the process—and having gained an immortal body through the tempering of the Karma Flame Red Lotus, she could finally put her mind at ease.","\"She’s even stronger than I imagined,\" Feng Jiu murmured softly, gazing at her daughter—whose features had fully revealed themselves, radiating breathtaking beauty—her eyes brimming with pride.","This was her daughter, Feng Jiu’s daughter!","Xuanyuan Mo Ze held Feng Jiu’s hand as he looked at their daughter, his heart equally filled with pride.","Their daughter was as radiant as Mother, and in the future, she would surely grow to be as powerful as they were!","\"Boom!\"","The powerful heavenly tribulation lightning that had been gathering in the sky for so long finally struck down. This time, it struck Yue’er precisely in midair, and the Nine-Tailed Divine Fox beneath her feet bore the brunt of the strike as well.","However, due to the return of her spirit energy, the strike not only failed to harm her but actually further tempered her immortal body. At the same time, a powerful aura of spirit energy surged from her. In that moment, she and her soul-bound contract beast, the Ancient Divine Fox, both advanced together...","\"Whoa! She’s... she’s advanced...\"","The cultivator’s eyes widened in utter disbelief. It had clearly been a dead end—how had it been resolved in the end? And how had it even helped her advance again?","Amid the astonished and shocked gazes of the onlookers, Yue’er successfully advanced once more, her strength rising three realms in a single go. Only when the dark clouds in the sky dispersed and the powerful, oppressive air currents dissipated with the wind did she land steadily on the ground, with the Ancient Divine Fox crouching by her side.","Her jet-black hair cascaded down like silk. The crimson lotus between her brows had faded, leaving only a red flame-like pattern—identical to the one on the Ancient Divine Fox’s forehead.","With her advancement and having survived this ordeal, her aura had completely transformed. Set against the backdrop of the crimson flame pattern on her brow, she appeared more majestic and peerless than ever before."]},{"number":5266,"title":"Chapter 5266: The Phoenix Empress’ Daughter","paragraphs":["\"Master!\"","After advancing in cultivation, Yue’er hurried over to the Azure Emperor, taking his arm as he leaned on her.","\"Master, are you all right?\" She supported him, looking at his pale face and uneven breathing, her heart filled with anxiety. \"Here, I have some medicinal pills. Master, please take one first.\"","As she spoke, she hurriedly retrieved medicinal pills from her spatial ring. However, Mother had given her so many that, in her frantic state, she didn’t know which one to give him.","Just then, a voice rang out.","\"Yue’er.\"","Feng Jiu called out. Seeing that she had finally broken through the Heavenly Tribulation and survived the ordeal of life and death, she stepped out of the shadows and walked toward her and the Azure Emperor.","As she appeared, Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Mo Chen followed her out.","\"Phoenix Empress... Hell’s Lord... and the Holy Emperor? Whoa!\" A Divine Lord, upon seeing the three figures enter the group’s view, couldn’t help but gasp in shock.","How did these three Great Emperors arrive? And all at the same time? Could it be that they sensed the commotion here and came to investigate?","\"This old man greets Hell’s Lord, Phoenix Empress, and Holy Emperor.\" After regaining his composure, the elderly Immortal Lord hurriedly bowed respectfully to the three of them.","Hearing the elderly Immortal Lord’s words, the crowd around them turned to look at the trio and immediately bowed their heads in trembling reverence: \"We pay our respects to Hell’s Lord, Phoenix Empress, and Holy Emperor.\"","\"Hmm.\" Xuanyuan Mo Ze gave a faint reply. Seeing them gathered around, he couldn’t help but frown and said in a deep voice, \"Dismissed!\"","\"Yes.\" The crowd dared not say a word; after respectfully acknowledging the order, they gradually stepped back. Just as they were about to leave, they heard the anxious, tearful voice of the young girl named Yun Qi, who was supporting the Azure Emperor.","\"Father, Mother, please look at Master! Master is gravely injured.\"","Father and Mother?","For a moment, the hearts of the gathered cultivators jolted. Their eyes widened in shock as they looked up at them in disbelief. Could it be that Yun Qi, the Azure Emperor’s disciple, was actually the daughter of Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress?","Whoa!","Who would have thought? No wonder—no wonder she possessed an ancient divine fox at such a young age, no wonder the Primordial Red Lotus resided within her, no wonder she possessed such cultivation at such a tender age, no wonder her breathtakingly beautiful features bore a faint resemblance to Feng Jiu...","Though shock and disbelief churned within them, they dared not linger. With their minds reeling, they hurriedly retreated.","Shen Shiqi was also stunned. He never imagined that Yun Qi was actually the daughter of Hell’s Lord and the Phoenix Empress. Precisely because of this, he stood there frozen, unable to recover from the shock.","The few people behind him had intended to step back, but after calling out to him softly several times with no response, they found themselves in a bind. They could neither advance nor retreat, so they could only stand behind him with their heads bowed, doing their best to make themselves as inconspicuous as possible.","Feng Jiu checked the pulse of the Azure Emperor, furrowing her brow slightly. \"I didn’t expect the power of the Heavenly Tribulation Thunder to be so formidable,\" she said. Withdrawing her hand, she looked at the Azure Emperor and sighed softly, her tone complex. \"By shielding her, you’ve dissipated a thousand years of cultivation, and even your divine soul is somewhat unstable. Coupled with the scorching wounds from the Heavenly Tribulation Thunder, if it were anyone else, I fear their soul would have long since scattered, their divine essence extinguished, and their immortal body lost.\"","The Azure Emperor’s cultivation was truly unfathomable; even she could not guarantee that anyone else would remain conscious under such circumstances.","\"Thank you. If not for you, Yue’er would not have survived this tribulation.\""]},{"number":5267,"title":"Chapter 5267: Etched Deep in Her Heart","paragraphs":["To be honest, Feng Jiu’s feelings at that moment were rather complicated. The Azure Emperor had shielded Yue’er from the heavenly tribulation’s lightning and helped her overcome the tribulation of life and death; the bond between the two of them would surely only grow deeper.","Watching her daughter, who was supporting the Azure Emperor with a look of anxiety and concern on her face, and recalling the divine soul energy surging through her earlier, as well as the words she had spoken to the Azure Emperor—\"Master, I’m back\"—","She knew her daughter had regained her memories from her past life.","Feng Jiu let out a soft sigh. Well then, children have their own destinies. Whatever her future holds, it is entirely up to her to decide. As her Mother, all she could do was support her and offer her blessings.","\"Protecting her is my duty,\" said the Azure Emperor, a trickle of blood spilling from the corner of his mouth.","\"Master!\"","Yue’er’s eyes reddened slightly, her heart clenching in anxiety as she looked at her Mother: \"Mother, Mother, please save Master! Mother...\"","\"Let’s return to the Immortal Island first!\" Feng Jiu said. With a wave of her hand, a spatial teleportation array appeared before them.","\"You all go back! I’m going to visit an old friend, so I won’t be joining you,\" Mo Chen smiled at them and said gently.","\"Alright,\" Feng Jiu replied, adding, \"Come visit us sometime.\"","\"Mm hmm,\" Mo Chen nodded, then lightly touched the ground with his toes, soaring into the air and riding the wind until he vanished from their sight.","\"Shen Shiqi.\" Feng Jiu turned to Shen Shiqi, who was still standing there in a daze, and smiled.","\"Yes.\" Shen Shiqi snapped out of his daze and replied quickly.","\"You’re Yue’er’s friend. In a while, have her bring you to the island to visit.\" Feng Jiu said with a smile.","Hearing this, not only was Shen Shiqi pleasantly surprised, but the few Shen family members behind him were overjoyed as well.","\"Alright, thank you, Phoenix Empress,\" he said quickly, bowing his hands in a gesture of respect.","Yue’er, supporting the Azure Emperor, said to Shen Shiqi, \"I’ll take my master back first. We’ll get in touch with you later.\" With that, she helped the Azure Emperor into the teleportation array.","Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu also stepped inside. As the teleportation array vanished, the group disappeared from the spot, leaving only Shen Shiqi and the others standing there.","Three days later, on the Immortal Island.","\"Mother, why hasn’t my master woken up yet?\" Yue’er asked her mother, looking at the Azure Emperor on the bed.","\"He’s been asleep for three days since we returned. His injuries have been gradually healing over the past couple of days, so I expect he’ll wake up tomorrow.\" Feng Jiu said, handing her a small vial: \"This is a potion I just refined. Apply it to his back, and once he’s healed, there won’t be any scorched scars left.\"","\"Thank you, Mother.\" Yue’er took it and held it in her hand.","Looking at her, Feng Jiu paused for a moment before asking, \"Yue’er, what are your plans from here on out?\"","Yue’er turned to face her, thought for a moment, and said, \"Mother, once Master’s injuries have healed a bit, I want to accompany him back to Yunxiao Mountain.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu paused and asked, \"Yue’er, have you fallen in love with the Azure Emperor?\"","Hearing these words, Yue’er froze for a moment, then broke into a smile. \"Mother, when I underwent that tribulation, I regained my memories from my past life. I remembered every little thing Master did for me back then, as well as the years Master and I spent together on Yunxiao Mountain.\"","She reached out and took her hand, saying, \"I know that Master has always treated me only as his disciple. He cares for me and spoils me—I know all of that. I’ve known it since my past life. Since my past life, my heart has been filled with thoughts of Master. But I didn’t dare say it, nor did I dare let him know. I was afraid that if he found out, he would drive me away from Yunxiao Mountain, away from his side.\""]},{"number":5268,"title":"Chapter 5268: Good stuff","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu couldn’t help but feel a pang of sympathy. \"Silly girl,\" she said, \"if you love him, you should let him know. Besides, your master might just have feelings for you too.\"","However, Yue’er shook her head and said, \"Mother, you don’t understand Master. All these years, there has never been a woman by his side, nor has he ever had a woman he fancied. I am already content just to be by Master’s side. Besides, we are master and disciple; I don’t want Master to be criticized by the world because of me.\"","If she were to break the master-disciple bond between them, she feared the world would view her master with suspicion, and she feared he would face public censure because of her. She did not want to see him treated that way because of her.","Therefore, simply being by her master’s side was enough to make her content.","Upon hearing this, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but smile. \"How do you know the Azure Emperor cares about what others think? Besides, what do other people have to do with you two? Whether you’re happy or not, only the two of you know. Why should you pay so much attention to the gazes and words of others? And anyway, in this world of cultivation, what hasn’t happened before?\"","She smiled, reached out, and ruffled her hair, saying, \"Your fate with the Azure Emperor was decided long ago. If you’re meant to be together in this life, wouldn’t it be better to open your heart and accept it? As for whether the Azure Emperor has you in his heart...\"","She pursed her lips and gave a mysterious smile. \"Mother will help you find out.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er stared at her in bewilderment. \"How will you test it? Can—can you really do that? What if... what if...\" She couldn’t help but worry.","\"You’ll find out soon enough. Mother will go prepare first.\" With that, Feng Jiu smiled and left ahead of her.","Yue’er sat by the bed, gazing at her master who lay fast asleep, and couldn’t help but ask herself: Had her master ever been moved by her as well?","The next day, Feng Jiu toyed with a vial of medicinal pill in her hand, a mysterious smile playing on her lips.","She had enhanced the True Word Medicinal Pill by several grades, intending to give it to the Azure Emperor. Once he took it, she would know immediately whether Yue’er held a place in his heart. Considering his unfathomable power, she had deliberately increased the potency of the pill. With his cultivation weakened and his injuries still unhealed, this was the perfect opportunity to test it.","Upon entering the guest room, she saw Yue’er helping the Azure Emperor lean against the headboard. Smiling, she walked over. \"Awake? It seems I’ve arrived just in time.\"","\"Mother, Master just woke up. I was just about to go get you.\" Upon seeing her, Yue’er hurriedly said, \"Mother, please take Master’s pulse!\"","\"Alright.\" Feng Jiu stepped forward, checked the Azure Emperor’s pulse, and said, \"Do not use any spirit energy for the next three months. With gradual recuperation, he will naturally recover.\"","With that, she produced a medicinal pill and said, \"Here, take this one first.\"","The Azure Emperor looked at the medicinal pill in her hand. The scent was somewhat strange, and he furrowed his brow slightly. Just as he was about to speak, Feng Jiu flipped her palm, and the medicinal pill was already stuffed into his mouth, sliding down his throat. His face instantly darkened.","\"What did you give me?\" Though he knew it couldn’t possibly be harmful, the medicinal pill’s scent was oddly peculiar, and he had no idea what its effects might be.","Yue’er blinked in mild surprise, staring at the medicinal pill her master had swallowed. That scent—if she wasn’t mistaken—seemed to be the True Word Pill her Mother had refined?","Unconsciously, she glanced at Mother, silently seeking an answer.","Feng Jiu smiled and said, \"It’s for nourishing the body. The taste is a bit strange, but it’s definitely good stuff.\""]},{"number":5269,"title":"Chapter 5269: You’re on your own","paragraphs":["She found a chair nearby and sat down, saying to Yue’er, \"Pour your master a glass of water to moisten his throat.\"","Seeing this, Yue’er glanced at her master, then went to the table, poured a cup of water, and handed it to him, saying, \"Master, here’s some water.\"","The Azure Emperor had been unconscious for several days, and his throat was a bit dry. He took the cup, drank, then handed it back to Yue’er. He glanced at Feng Jiu and asked, \"Did you call me here for a reason?\"","Knowing Feng Jiu as he did, he doubted she would be sitting here idly if she had nothing to discuss.","\"Yes, there is something I’d like to talk to you about.\" Feng Jiu smiled, glanced at Yue’er, and said to the Azure Emperor, \"You sustained such severe injuries saving Yue’er. Both Mo Ze and I would like to ask you to stay here and recuperate. What do you think?\"","\"She is my disciple; saving her was simply my duty. You needn’t dwell on it. As for my injuries, once I’ve recovered a bit in a few days, I’d like to return to Yunxiao Mountain to recuperate,\" the Azure Emperor said softly.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu nodded. \"Very well, we respect your decision. However, I have one more question: in your heart, is Yue’er truly just a disciple? Nothing more?\"","Yue’er, listening from the side, felt her heart skip a beat. She looked at her master with a mix of nervousness and trepidation.","Upon hearing this, the Azure Emperor furrowed his brow slightly and gave Feng Jiu a deep look. \"What do you mean?\" At the same time, he felt his heart skip a beat at her question, as if an answer were trying to leap from his heart and escape his lips, only to be ruthlessly suppressed.","Feng Jiu observed the Azure Emperor’s expression and smiled faintly. She stood up and said, \"All right, you two talk. I won’t disturb you.\" With that, she turned and walked toward the door.","\"Mother...\" Yue’er hurriedly grabbed her arm.","Feng Jiu smiled, turned back, ruffled her hair, and said, \"This is your own problem; you should try to solve it yourself. I’ve helped you this far; the rest is up to you.\" As soon as she finished speaking, she stepped out of the room and closed the door behind her.","Xuanyuan Mo Ze, who was sitting outside the courtyard, raised an eyebrow when he saw her come out and close the door for them. \"You really have a lot of trust eh,\" he said. \"Aren’t you worried our daughter might get taken advantage of?\"","Feng Jiu took his hand, and the two walked out together, laughing as she said, \"The Azure Emperor is just as clueless as Jun Jueshang was back in the day—both are thick-headed, unromantic types. Sigh! It’s a real hardship for my precious daughter. I wonder when the Azure Emperor will ever come to his senses.\"","Hearing this, Xuanyuan Mo Ze laughed. He said no more, but instead wrapped his arm around her waist as they strolled toward the garden together...","Elsewhere, with Feng Jiu’s departure, the atmosphere in the room had grown somewhat awkward. The Azure Emperor leaned back on the bed, his eyes half-closed, pondering the true meaning behind Feng Jiu’s earlier words.","Yue’er, however, felt a mix of nervousness, anxiety, and inner conflict. Should she speak up? If she did, what if her Master...","After pondering for a moment without reaching a conclusion, the Azure Emperor looked up at Yue’er and asked, \"Little Qi, have you remembered?\"","Yue’er looked at him, took a deep breath, pulled up a chair, sat down in front of him, and nodded. \"Master, I—I remember. I remember everything: how you took me as your disciple in my past life, our years on Yunxiao Mountain, and how I died during a lightning tribulation during my cultivation breakthrough. I remember it all.\""]},{"number":5270,"title":"Chapter 5270: A Moment of Realization","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, the Azure Emperor paused briefly before saying, \"I never expected you to remember. I had assumed you had long since entered the cycle of reincarnation, only to be taken under my wing as a disciple in this life—and renewing our master-disciple bond would be just the same.\"","He looked at her and said, \"Whether or not you remember your past life, in my eyes, you have always been my most cherished disciple, Yun Qi.\"","Hearing his words, Yue’er felt a pang of sadness in her heart. She rushed forward and embraced him. \"Master!\"","The Azure Emperor was taken aback for a moment, then patted her head and laughed. \"You’re all grown up now; you can’t keep throwing yourself into your master’s arms like this.\"","Upon hearing this, Yue’er wiped away a tear, lifted her head from his embrace, and with a look of earnestness and resolve on her breathtakingly beautiful face, said, \"Master, I love you. I’ve loved you since my past life. Master, do you love me?\"","Even someone as calm and composed as the Azure Emperor couldn’t help but look taken aback and stunned by her bold confession.","This momentary lapse of concentration, combined with the shock of her words, caused his heart to race involuntarily. A strange and wondrous sensation rippled through his chest, eventually filling his entire being.","\"Master, have you ever had feelings for me?\" Yue’er asked again, her gaze fixed intently on him. She knew that since Mother had given him the Truth-Speaking Medicinal Pill, this was the perfect moment to draw out his true thoughts.","However, just as the Azure Emperor opened his mouth to speak, he snapped back to his senses. Looking at Yun Qi before him, he took a deep breath and said softly, \"I am tired. Please leave.\"","With that, he closed his eyes, suppressing the chaotic pounding of his heart.","Hearing this, Yue’er’s whole being dimmed for a fleeting moment. Heaven only knew how much courage she had mustered to ask those questions, yet she had not received her master’s answer.","She opened her mouth, intending to say something more, but in the end, she said nothing and turned to leave.","The Azure Emperor opened his eyes and watched her receding figure. He placed a hand over his wildly pounding chest. What was this unfamiliar feeling?","\"Love?\" he murmured to himself.","\"Love.\"","After a long silence, a voice—part resignation, part whisper—escaped his lips. He had never known the taste of love, but in that moment, he realized that all these years, he had always held her in the very center of his heart. It was precisely because of love that he had been so devastated when he witnessed her death and the scattering of her soul in her previous life—so much so that he was willing to sacrifice hundreds of years of cultivation just to find a glimmer of hope for her...","Simply because he wanted to see her again. Simply because he loved her...","Once he realized this, his heart suddenly felt clear and unburdened. So that was why—no wonder he had always found Xiao Junyan so unbearable back then. He suspected that, aside from himself, he felt no one was worthy of Yun Qi, and thus found everyone else objectionable.","With this realization, he relaxed completely, a faint smile curving his lips. Thinking back to Yun Qi’s confession moments ago, his mood had shifted from initial shock to the joy and happiness he felt now.","So this, then, was what it felt like to fall in love with someone—a sensation that truly brought joy to both body and soul.","Just as Feng Jiu had suspected, he had never been one to care about the opinions of others. He had once been ignorant of what love was, but now that he had awakened to it and understood his own feelings, he naturally would no longer hide his emotions."]},{"number":5271,"title":"Chapter 5271: Always on My Mind","paragraphs":["Thinking back to how Yun Qi had left so gloomily just a moment ago, he decided he should find an opportunity to have a proper talk with her.","That night, Feng Jiu went to Yue’er’s room. Seeing her lying there listlessly, she smiled and asked, \"What’s wrong? Didn’t Mother’s Truth Medicinal Pill work?\"","\"Mother,\" Yue’er called out, \"I confessed my feelings to Master, but he told me he’s tired and needs to rest, and asked me to leave for now.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu paused for a moment, then chuckled softly. \"He truly lives up to his reputation as the Azure Emperor. I never expected he could even suppress the potency of the Truth Medicinal Pill.\" She sat down at the table, looked at Yue’er, and smiled. \" \"Don’t be disappointed. Trust Mother’s judgment—the Azure Emperor still cares for you.\"","\"Is that true?\" Yue’er couldn’t help but look at her.","\"It’s true.\" She gently pinched her nose and laughed. \"When have I ever lied to you? Come, let me tell you the story of your Aunt Qianhua and Jun Jueshang.\"","And so, that night, the two of them chatted in the room until dawn...","The next day, when Yue’er stepped out, she felt refreshed and invigorated, her face radiating energy and determination. She had made up her mind: no matter what, she was the only one by her master’s side—and she would remain the only one. She refused to believe that, over the long years, her master could remain unmoved!","In the days that followed, the Azure Emperor watched her smile grow brighter day by day. Especially when she faced him, her radiant smile was just as it had always been, as if that day’s confession had never happened. Seeing this, he felt a strange unease. The words he had originally intended to speak to her were held back as he observed her peculiar demeanor.","It wasn’t until half a month later, when his health had gradually improved, that one evening, as he sat reading in the courtyard, she entered as usual, bustling about and keeping him company at the table.","He said, \"Little Qi, I plan to return to Yunxiao Mountain.\"","\"Then I’ll go back with you, Master,\" she replied immediately.","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor paused slightly. He held the book but had no heart to read; his mind was elsewhere. After a long while, he finally set the book down and looked at her. \"Little Qi, you confessed your feelings to me that day.\"","\"Yes, Master. It’s alright. Even if you don’t have feelings for me now, it’s alright. I’ll always be by your side. Besides, I won’t let any other woman come within a step of you. I...\" Before she could finish, her hand was taken. For a moment, she froze, staring at him in shock.","\"I’ll tell you now: as far back as my previous life, I’ve already placed you here.\" He took her hand and pressed it against his chest.","Yue’er’s eyes widened, her face frozen in astonishment.","Seeing her expression, the Azure Emperor actually laughed. \"Overjoyed to the point of being speechless?\"","\"Master, you... you’re not lying to me? Are... are you confessing your feelings to me?\" Yue’er asked, her voice trembling.","\"Yes, I’m not lying. It’s true. I’ve always kept you in my heart. Long before I even realized it, you had already become an indispensable part of my life.\"","He looked at her and asked softly, \"Little Qi, will you stay by my side forever?\"","\"Yes! I will! I will!\" She joyfully rushed forward and hugged him tightly.","Azure Emperor also reached out to embrace her, savoring the feeling of her in his arms. After a moment, he said, \"Let’s go tell your parents about us.\"","Yue’er laughed and said, \"My parents left on a journey early this morning. They said they won’t interfere in our affairs; we can just tell them when we’re ready to marry in the future.\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly. Taking her hand, he said, \"Then let’s return to Yunxiao Mountain.\"","\"Yeah.\" Yue’er gave a sweet smile, interlaced her fingers with his, and walked out with him.","The two figures walked side by side, their fingers intertwined. Laughter and conversation carried on the gentle breeze, faintly revealing their hopes for the future...","End of the Side Story"]}]);
